      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"Cold start: execution begins here at power-on and reset.\nInterrupts off, A = 0 and DE = $FFFF (the top address for the RAM fill and check), then\nRAM_FILL.\nDoes not return.","comment":"Interrupts off for the start-up"},
        "1": {"comment":"A = 0: the fill byte"},
        "2": {"comment":"DE = the top address to test"},
        "5": {"comment":"RAM_FILL"},
        "8": {"synopsis":"RST $08: stops with an error. The byte after the RST holds the error code (the report minus\none); X_PTR = CH_ADD marks where it happened. Goes on at ERROR_CODE.","comment":"X_PTR = CH_ADD: where the error was found"},
        "14": {"comment":"On at ERROR_CODE"},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: prints the character in A through the current channel (CURCHL), by PRINT_A_CHAN.","comment":"PRINT_A_CHAN"},
        "19": {"comment":"Unused ($FF)"},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: A = the character at CH_ADD, moving CH_ADD past what SKIP_TEST skips: spaces, most\ncontrol codes, and the codes $10-$17 with the bytes after them.\nExit: HL = CH_ADD.\nChanges: AF, HL; CH_ADD.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "27": {"comment":"A = the character there"},
        "28": {"synopsis":"The loop GET_CHAR and NEXT_SKIP share: returns when SKIP_TEST keeps the character in A,\notherwise moves on (NEXT_CHAR) and tests again.","comment":"Skipped?"},
        "31": {"comment":"No: kept"},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: CH_ADD + 1 (NEXT_CHAR), then past what SKIP_TEST skips, as GET_CHAR does; A = the\ncharacter.\nChanges: AF, HL; CH_ADD.","comment":"CH_ADD + 1"},
        "35": {"comment":"Tested again"},
        "37": {"comment":"Unused ($FF)"},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: enters the calculator. The bytes after the RST are its operation codes and\nliterals, up to end-calc ($38); the 48K decoding lists them. Goes on at CALC_ENTRY.","comment":"CALC_ENTRY"},
        "43": {"comment":"Unused ($FF)"},
        "48": {"synopsis":"RST $30: makes BC bytes of room at the end of the workspace, at the old STKBOT, moving the\ncalculator stack up; WORKSP is kept. Goes on at WORK_ROOM_END.\nExit: DE = the room's first byte, HL = its last byte, BC = the count.\nChanges: F, DE, HL.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "49": {"comment":"HL = STKBOT"},
        "52": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "53": {"comment":"On at WORK_ROOM_END"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"INT (interrupt mode 1), once a frame: adds one to the three-byte FRAMES counter, then reads\nthe keyboard (KEYBOARD).\nKeeps AF, BC, DE and HL; returns with interrupts enabled.","comment":"AF and HL kept"},
        "58": {"comment":"FRAMES' low word"},
        "61": {"comment":"One more"},
        "65": {"comment":"Wrapped to 0?"},
        "67": {"comment":"No"},
        "69": {"comment":"The low word wrapped: FRAMES' third byte ($5C7A)"},
        "72": {"synopsis":"The keyboard part of INT_FRAME: KEYBOARD with BC and DE kept, then the registers back and\nEI.","comment":"BC and DE kept"},
        "74": {"comment":"The keyboard read"},
        "79": {"comment":"HL and AF back"},
        "81": {"comment":"Interrupts on again"},
        "83": {"synopsis":"RST $08's tail: HL = its return address, the byte after the RST; L = that byte, the error\ncode. Goes on into ERROR_L.","comment":"HL = the byte after the RST"},
        "84": {"comment":"L = the error code"},
        "85": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code L: ERR_NR = L, the stack back to ERR_SP, and CALC_RESET empties the\ncalculator stack; its RET then takes the address in the slot ERR_SP points at.\nTEST_ROOM (NO_ROOM) enters here with L already set.","comment":"ERR_NR = it"},
        "88": {"comment":"The stack back to ERR_SP"},
        "92": {"comment":"CALC_RESET; its RET goes to the error handler"},
        "95": {"comment":"Unused ($FF)"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The NMI handler: when NMIADD ($5CB0) is zero it jumps to address 0 (HL = 0), restarting the\nmachine; otherwise it returns at once (NMI_RETURN).\nStart-up leaves NMIADD zero: RAM_CHECK clears all of RAM.","comment":"AF and HL kept"},
        "104": {"comment":"HL = NMIADD"},
        "107": {"comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "109": {"comment":"No: just return"},
        "111": {"comment":"HL = 0 here: a restart"},
        "112": {"synopsis":"HL and AF back, and RETN."},
        "116": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD + 1; A = the character there.\nExit: HL = CH_ADD.\nChanges: A, HL; CH_ADD.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "119": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD = HL + 1; A = the character there.\nChanges: A, HL; CH_ADD.","comment":"One on"},
        "120": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD = HL; A = the character there.\nChanges: A; CH_ADD.","comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "123": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "125": {"synopsis":"Decides whether the character in A is skipped while scanning: no carry keeps it, carry skips\nit. Kept: $21 and above, and $0D. Skipped: the rest below $10, and $18-$20. $10-$15 also\nskip the one byte after them, $16-$17 the two (SKIP_TEST_SET).\nChanges: F, HL; CH_ADD.","comment":"$21 and above are kept"},
        "128": {"comment":"$0D (ENTER) is kept"},
        "131": {"comment":"Below $10: skipped"},
        "134": {"comment":"$18-$20 skipped; $10-$17 go on"},
        "136": {"comment":"Carry for $18-$20: skipped"},
        "138": {"comment":"$10-$17: past their first parameter byte"},
        "139": {"comment":"$16-$17 (AT, TAB) have two"},
        "143": {"comment":"Past the second"},
        "144": {"synopsis":"Carry set (skip), and CH_ADD = HL, now on the last byte after the code, so the next\nNEXT_CHAR passes them.","comment":"Carry: skipped"},
        "145": {"comment":"CH_ADD on the last parameter byte"},
        "149": {"synopsis":"Keyword table: 92 strings, each with bit 7 set on its last character. Entry 0 is a lone \"?\";\nentries 1-91 are the keywords RND to COPY, in the order of the manual's token codes $A5-$FF.\nPRINT_TOKEN prints from it. Listed as .defc rows, one per keyword; the key tables\n(KEYS_MAIN) follow straight on."},
        "517": {"synopsis":"Key table, main: 39 bytes, the code of each key but CAPS SHIFT, by READ_KEYS's key number: B\nH Y 6 5 T G V, N J U 7 4 R F C, M K I 8 3 E D X, SYMBOL SHIFT ($0E) L O 9 2 W S Z, SPACE\nENTER ($0D) P 0 1 Q A. KEY_MAIN_CODE reads it at $0205 + key number.\nThe key tables after it run to $028D; each is indexed from its start less its first code."},
        "556": {"synopsis":"Key table, E mode letters: 26 tokens for A-Z, read from $01EB + the letter: READ BIN LPRINT\nDATA TAN SGN ABS SQR CODE VAL LEN USR PI INKEY$ PEEK TAB SIN INT RESTORE RND CHR$ LLIST COS\nEXP STR$ LN (spelt from KEYWORD_TABLE)."},
        "582": {"synopsis":"Key table, E mode letters with a shift key: 26 bytes for A-Z, read from $0205 + the letter:\n~ BRIGHT PAPER \\ ATN { } CIRCLE IN VAL$ SCREEN$ ATTR INVERSE OVER OUT, $7F for P, ASN VERIFY\n| MERGE ] FLASH ACS INK [ BEEP."},
        "608": {"synopsis":"Key table, CAPS SHIFT digits: 10 control codes for 0-9, read from $0230 + the digit: $0C $07\n$06 $04 $05 $08 $0A $0B $09 $0F, the manual's DELETE, EDIT, CAPS LOCK, TRUE VIDEO, INV.\nVIDEO, the four cursor keys (5 left, 6 down, 7 up, 8 right) and GRAPHICS. In G mode, 0 and 9\ngive these codes too."},
        "618": {"synopsis":"Key table, SYMBOL SHIFT letters: 26 bytes for A-Z, read from $0229 + the letter: STOP * ?\nSTEP >= TO THEN ^ AT - + = . , ; \" <= < NOT > OR / <> ` AND :."},
        "644": {"synopsis":"Key table, E mode SYMBOL SHIFT digits: 10 tokens for 0-9, read from $0254 + the digit:\nFORMAT, DEF FN, FN, LINE, OPEN #, CLOSE #, MOVE, ERASE, POINT, CAT. READ_KEYS follows."},
        "654": {"synopsis":"Scans the keyboard: reads the eight half-rows (port $FE with B = $FE, $FD, ... $7F) and\ncollects up to two keys down as key numbers, E the last found and D the one before ($FF for\nnone).\nA key number is $2F less the half-row number less 8 x (bit + 1): CAPS SHIFT is $27, SYMBOL\nSHIFT $18 (Klive's key matrix: row 0 bit 0, row 7 bit 1).\nReturns NZ at once on a third key. At the end Z means the keys are usable: fewer than two,\nor two with CAPS SHIFT or SYMBOL SHIFT as one of them (then in D).\nExit: DE = the key numbers.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"L = $2F: the first half-row's key number"},
        "656": {"comment":"No keys yet"},
        "659": {"comment":"B = $FE: the first half-row"},
        "662": {"synopsis":"Reads one half-row: A = its five key bits, 1 for a key down.","comment":"The half-row's bits"},
        "664": {"comment":"1 for a key down"},
        "665": {"comment":"Five keys"},
        "667": {"comment":"A key down in this half-row?"},
        "669": {"comment":"H = the keys down"},
        "670": {"comment":"A = the half-row's number"},
        "671": {"synopsis":"One more key found: NZ out at once when D already held one (three keys)."},
        "672": {"comment":"A third key: not usable"},
        "673": {"synopsis":"Finds the key's column: 8 off the number per bit shifted out of H."},
        "675": {"comment":"The next key into the carry"},
        "677": {"comment":"Until the key down"},
        "679": {"comment":"D = the key before"},
        "680": {"comment":"E = this key"},
        "681": {"comment":"More keys in the half-row"},
        "683": {"synopsis":"The next half-row, L one lower, until B's 0 bit has gone round.","comment":"The next half-row's number"},
        "684": {"comment":"The next half-row"},
        "686": {"comment":"Until all eight"},
        "688": {"comment":"A second key in D?"},
        "690": {"comment":"No: Z, done"},
        "691": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT?"},
        "693": {"comment":"Z: usable"},
        "694": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "696": {"comment":"Z: usable"},
        "697": {"comment":"D and E swapped: the shift key into D"},
        "700": {"comment":"Z when it is SYMBOL SHIFT; NZ: two keys, no shift"},
        "703": {"synopsis":"Reads the keyboard, from INT_FRAME every frame, and keeps the two key sets of KSTATE (4\nbytes each: the main code or $FF when unused, a release counter, the repeat counter, the\ndecoded code):\n1. READ_KEYS; nothing when it reports NZ (three keys, or two without a shift key).\n2. Each set in use counts its release counter down; at 0 the set is freed (KBD_SET_LOOP).\n3. KEY_MAIN_CODE turns the scan into a main code; none for no key or a shift key alone.\n4. A code a set already holds is a key still held: KBD_REPEAT. A new one goes into a free\n   set, the second one first, and is decoded (KBD_NEW_KEY); with both sets in use it is\n   ignored.\nA new or repeated key goes into LAST_K, with FLAGS bit 5 set.\nObserved: holding 1 gave a new key on the first interrupt, again after 35 (REPDEL) and then\nevery 5 (REPPER); after release the set was freed on the fifth interrupt.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; KSTATE, LAST_K, FLAGS.","comment":"The keys down"},
        "706": {"comment":"Not usable"},
        "707": {"comment":"HL = KSTATE's first set"},
        "710": {"synopsis":"One key set: in use (bit 7 of its first byte clear)? Then its release counter one down, and\nthe set freed ($FF) when it reaches 0."},
        "715": {"comment":"Its release counter down"},
        "719": {"comment":"Freed"},
        "721": {"synopsis":"After the set at $5C00, the one at $5C04.","comment":"A = L: which set?"},
        "722": {"comment":"The second set next"},
        "728": {"comment":"No usable key?"},
        "735": {"comment":"Held in the first set?"},
        "738": {"comment":"DE = the first set"},
        "742": {"comment":"Held in the second set?"},
        "745": {"comment":"The second set free?"},
        "749": {"comment":"HL = the first set"},
        "750": {"comment":"The first set free? Neither: the key is ignored"},
        "753": {"synopsis":"A new key into the free set at HL: its main code, release counter 5, repeat counter REPDEL,\nthen the code KEY_DECODE gives for MODE (C), FLAGS (D) and the shift key (B).","comment":"E = the main code"},
        "754": {"comment":"Into the set"},
        "756": {"comment":"Release counter 5"},
        "759": {"comment":"Repeat counter REPDEL"},
        "764": {"comment":"C = MODE"},
        "767": {"comment":"D = FLAGS"},
        "771": {"comment":"A = the decoded code"},
        "775": {"comment":"Into the set"},
        "776": {"synopsis":"LAST_K = A, and FLAGS bit 5 set: a key is waiting."},
        "784": {"synopsis":"A key still held: its release counter back to 5, and the repeat counter one down; at 0 it is\nset to REPPER and the set's decoded code goes into LAST_K again (KBD_STORE_KEY)."},
        "785": {"comment":"Release counter 5 again"},
        "788": {"comment":"Repeat counter down"},
        "789": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "790": {"comment":"REPPER from now on"},
        "795": {"comment":"A = the set's decoded code"},
        "798": {"synopsis":"Turns READ_KEYS's key numbers into a main code: E is the key, D the shift key ($FF for\nnone).\nExit: carry and A = the key's code from KEYS_MAIN; no carry for no key, CAPS SHIFT alone\n($27) or SYMBOL SHIFT alone; B = the shift key, D = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, D, HL.","comment":"B = the shift key"},
        "799": {"comment":"D = 0 for the index"},
        "801": {"comment":"A = the key"},
        "802": {"comment":"No key, or CAPS SHIFT alone?"},
        "805": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT as the key..."},
        "809": {"comment":"... with no other: none"},
        "812": {"synopsis":"A = KEYS_MAIN's code for key number E; carry set.","comment":"HL = KEYS_MAIN"},
        "815": {"comment":"+ the key number"},
        "817": {"comment":"Carry: a key"},
        "819": {"synopsis":"Turns a main code into the code the key gives: E = the main code, B = the shift key ($FF\nnone, $27 CAPS SHIFT, $18 SYMBOL SHIFT), C = MODE (0 K/L/C, 1 E, 2 G), D = FLAGS (bit 3 set:\nL mode). Letters ($41-$5A):\n1. MODE 0, no shift or CAPS SHIFT: a keyword token in K mode (KD_K_TOKEN); in L mode the\n   capital, or the small letter when neither CAPS SHIFT nor CAPS LOCK (FLAGS2 bit 3) is on.\n   SYMBOL SHIFT: KEYS_SYM_LETTERS.\n2. MODE 1: KEYS_E_LETTERS, or KEYS_E_SHIFTED with either shift key (KD_E_LETTER).\n3. MODE 2: the letter + $4F, A to U giving $90-$A4.\nDigits go to KD_DIGIT; the other codes come back as they are.\nExit: A = the code.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"A = the main code"},
        "820": {"comment":"Below \":\": a digit, space, ENTER or SYMBOL SHIFT"},
        "824": {"comment":"MODE - 1"},
        "825": {"comment":"MODE 0?"},
        "828": {"comment":"MODE 1?"},
        "830": {"comment":"MODE 2: A-U to $90-$A4"},
        "833": {"synopsis":"A letter in E mode: KEYS_E_LETTERS with no shift key, KEYS_E_SHIFTED with either."},
        "836": {"comment":"No shift key ($FF + 1 = 0)?"},
        "839": {"comment":"Either: KEYS_E_SHIFTED"},
        "842": {"synopsis":"A = the byte at HL + E: the key's entry in the table chosen (HL is the table's start less\nthe first code).","comment":"DE = the code"},
        "847": {"synopsis":"A letter in K, L or C mode: with SYMBOL SHIFT (B bit 0 clear) from KEYS_SYM_LETTERS;\notherwise a token in K mode, a letter in L mode.","comment":"HL for KEYS_SYM_LETTERS"},
        "850": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT ($18, bit 0 clear)?"},
        "854": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 3 clear: K mode?"},
        "858": {"comment":"CAPS LOCK: the capital"},
        "863": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT: the capital"},
        "865": {"comment":"Otherwise the small letter"},
        "868": {"synopsis":"K mode: the letter + $A5, a keyword token (A gives $E6, NEW)."},
        "871": {"synopsis":"Codes below $3A: below \"0\" (space, ENTER, SYMBOL SHIFT's $0E) as they are; digits by MODE.\nMODE 1 (E): SYMBOL SHIFT from KEYS_E_SYM_DIGIT; otherwise 0-7 give $10-$17, or $18-$1F with\nCAPS SHIFT, and 8, 9 (KD_E_8_9).","comment":"Below '0': as it is"},
        "874": {"comment":"MODE - 1"},
        "875": {"comment":"MODE 0?"},
        "878": {"comment":"MODE 2?"},
        "880": {"comment":"HL for KEYS_E_SYM_DIGIT"},
        "883": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT (bit 5 clear)?"},
        "887": {"comment":"8 or 9?"},
        "891": {"comment":"0-7: $10-$17..."},
        "895": {"comment":"... or $18-$1F with CAPS SHIFT"},
        "898": {"synopsis":"8 and 9 in E mode: 2 and 3, or 0 and 1 with CAPS SHIFT.","comment":"8 and 9 become 2 and 3"},
        "900": {"comment":"No shift: done"},
        "902": {"comment":"Less 2: 0 and 1"},
        "905": {"synopsis":"A digit in G mode: 0 and 9 from KEYS_CAPS_DIGITS; 1-8 give the block graphics $81-$87 and\n$80 (for 8), or with CAPS SHIFT the same XOR $0F ($8E-$88, $8F).","comment":"HL for KEYS_CAPS_DIGITS"},
        "908": {"comment":"9?"},
        "912": {"comment":"0?"},
        "916": {"comment":"1-8 become 1-7 and 0"},
        "918": {"comment":"$80-$87"},
        "920": {"comment":"No shift: done"},
        "922": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT: the inverse block"},
        "925": {"synopsis":"A digit in K, L or C mode: the digit with no shift key; with CAPS SHIFT from\nKEYS_CAPS_DIGITS; with SYMBOL SHIFT the character $10 below it (1 \"!\", 3 \"#\" ... 9 \")\"),\nexcept 2 (\"@\", KD_AT_SIGN) and 0 (\"_\").","comment":"No shift: the digit itself"},
        "927": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT (bit 5 of B + 1 set)?"},
        "934": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT: the character $10 below"},
        "936": {"comment":"2: \"@\""},
        "940": {"comment":"0: \"_\""},
        "943": {"comment":"\"_\""},
        "946": {"synopsis":"SYMBOL SHIFT + 2: \"@\"."},
        "949": {"synopsis":"Makes a tone on the speaker (port $FE bit 4), the border kept in BORDCR's paper colour and\nbit 3 set in every write: DE + 1 cycles, each half-cycle a delay set by HL (H counts the\nouter loop, L / 4 the inner one, and L's low two bits pick an entry into TONE_NOPS for the\nfinest step). Interrupts are off meanwhile. The editor's click calls it with DE = PIP, HL =\n$00C8.\nObserved: BEEP .5,0 called it with DE 130 and HL 1642, BEEP .5,12 with DE 261 and HL 806.","comment":"No interrupts: exact timing"},
        "950": {"comment":"A = L"},
        "951": {"comment":"L / 4: the inner count"},
        "955": {"comment":"3 - L's low bits"},
        "958": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "961": {"comment":"IX = TONE_NOPS + it"},
        "967": {"comment":"The border colour from BORDCR"},
        "972": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-2"},
        "975": {"comment":"Bit 3 set"},
        "977": {"synopsis":"The entry JP (IX) uses: 0 to 3 NOPs (IX = $03D1 + 3 - L's low bits), then the delay loop."},
        "980": {"comment":"B and C one more for the loops' first DEC"},
        "982": {"synopsis":"The delay: C counts down, then B (from H) with C reloaded."},
        "985": {"comment":"C = $3F for the outer rounds"},
        "991": {"comment":"The speaker bit flipped"},
        "993": {"comment":"The edge"},
        "995": {"comment":"B = H again"},
        "996": {"comment":"C = the byte sent"},
        "997": {"comment":"A rising edge?"},
        "999": {"comment":"Yes: the second half"},
        "1001": {"comment":"Cycles left?"},
        "1003": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "1005": {"comment":"A back, C = L"},
        "1007": {"comment":"One cycle less"},
        "1008": {"comment":"The next half-cycle"},
        "1010": {"synopsis":"After a rising edge: the second half-cycle, one inner count longer."},
        "1011": {"comment":"One count longer"},
        "1014": {"synopsis":"DE ran out: interrupts back on.","comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1016": {"synopsis":"BEEP t,p: a tone of p semitones above (or below) 261.6 Hz for t seconds. The pitch's whole\npart picks the octave (p / 12, the result's exponent raised by it) and the semitone\n(SEMITONES); the fraction scales it by 1 + 0.0578 x the fraction. Then TONE_OUT's count (f x\nt, DE - 1) and timing (437500 / f - 30.125). A pitch outside the small-integer range, or t\nof 11 or more, is report B.\nObserved: BEEP .5,0 gave TONE_OUT DE 130, HL 1642; BEEP .5,12 DE 261, HL 806; BEEP 11,0\nreport B."},
        "1031": {"comment":"Memory 0: the pitch's whole part, a small integer?"},
        "1034": {"comment":"The exponent byte"},
        "1036": {"comment":"Not 0: report B"},
        "1039": {"comment":"C = the sign byte"},
        "1041": {"comment":"B = the low byte"},
        "1042": {"comment":"A = the low byte's sign extension"},
        "1045": {"comment":"The sign byte must match it"},
        "1048": {"comment":"The high byte too: -128 to 127"},
        "1052": {"comment":"The pitch + 60"},
        "1055": {"comment":"From -60 to 67: on"},
        "1058": {"comment":"Below -60 (no overflow): report B; above 67 goes on"},
        "1061": {"synopsis":"The octave: B counts how many 12s fit (from -6), A the semitone left (0-11).","comment":"B from -6"},
        "1063": {"synopsis":"One octave more.","comment":"One octave"},
        "1064": {"comment":"Less 12"},
        "1068": {"comment":"A = the semitone"},
        "1070": {"comment":"The octave kept"},
        "1071": {"comment":"HL = SEMITONES"},
        "1074": {"comment":"HL = the semitone's entry"},
        "1077": {"comment":"Its frequency stacked"},
        "1083": {"comment":"A = the octave"},
        "1084": {"comment":"Added to the exponent: times 2 ^ octave"},
        "1094": {"comment":"11 seconds or more: report B"},
        "1115": {"comment":"BC = the timing, the top number"},
        "1119": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "1122": {"comment":"HL = the timing"},
        "1123": {"comment":"DE = the count"},
        "1125": {"comment":"No cycles?"},
        "1127": {"comment":"Then nothing"},
        "1128": {"comment":"TONE_OUT makes DE + 1 cycles"},
        "1132": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B, \"Integer out of range\")."},
        "1134": {"synopsis":"Semitones: 12 numbers of 5 bytes, the frequencies of the semitones from pitch 0 to 11 in Hz:\n261.626, 277.183, 293.665, 311.127, 329.628, 349.228, 369.994, 391.995, 415.305, 440,\n466.164, 493.883. BEEP reads the semitone's entry (at $046E + 5 x semitone) and raises its\nexponent by the octave."},
        "1194": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a string expression (SCAN_EXPR; a number is report C) and, when running, sets bit\n7 of its last character. Nothing in this ROM calls it or holds its address.","comment":"The expression"},
        "1197": {"comment":"FLAGS"},
        "1200": {"comment":"Bit 6 (a number) into bit 7, bit 7 (running) into the carry"},
        "1201": {"comment":"A number: report C"},
        "1207": {"comment":"DE = the string, BC = its length"},
        "1210": {"comment":"HL = its start"},
        "1212": {"comment":"Empty: done"},
        "1214": {"comment":"HL = past it; the length one less, so its last character"},
        "1215": {"comment":"Its bit 7 set"},
        "1218": {"synopsis":"Saves a block to tape: A = the flag byte, IX = the start, DE = the length. Klive traps it to\nsave to the tape file.\n1. The pilot: $1F80 edges for a flag below $80 (a header), $0C98 otherwise, the border\n   flipping between colours 2 and 5 with them.\n2. Two sync edges.\n3. The flag, the DE bytes and a parity byte (the XOR of all), most significant bit first,\n   each bit two edges, longer for a 1. SPACE stops it.\nReturns through TAPE_RETURN, which puts the border back and turns interrupts on.","comment":"TAPE_RETURN as the return address"},
        "1222": {"comment":"$1F80 pilot edges for a header"},
        "1225": {"comment":"Flag bit 7: data?"},
        "1229": {"comment":"$0C98 for data"},
        "1232": {"synopsis":"A' = the flag; DE + 1 and IX - 1 for the loop's first round.","comment":"A' = the flag"},
        "1236": {"comment":"No interrupts: exact timing"},
        "1237": {"comment":"A = 2: red border, output low"},
        "1239": {"comment":"B = 2"},
        "1240": {"synopsis":"The pilot: an edge on port $FE (the border colour and the output bit flipping) after each\ndelay, HL times.","comment":"The delay"},
        "1242": {"comment":"An edge"},
        "1244": {"comment":"Red and cyan, the output bit flipped"},
        "1246": {"comment":"B = the delay"},
        "1248": {"comment":"L counts the edges"},
        "1251": {"comment":"One less for H's round"},
        "1252": {"comment":"H counts down past 0"},
        "1256": {"comment":"The first sync delay"},
        "1258": {"synopsis":"The first sync edge, after a short delay."},
        "1262": {"comment":"A = $0D"},
        "1264": {"comment":"The second sync delay"},
        "1266": {"synopsis":"The second sync edge, after a short delay."},
        "1270": {"comment":"B = the first delay, C = $0E: the second edge's byte"},
        "1273": {"comment":"A = the flag"},
        "1274": {"comment":"L = the flag: the first byte"},
        "1278": {"synopsis":"The next byte: from (IX), or the parity byte when DE is 0.","comment":"DE 0?"},
        "1280": {"comment":"Then the parity"},
        "1282": {"comment":"L = the next byte"},
        "1285": {"synopsis":"The parity H takes the byte in (XOR).","comment":"A = the parity XOR the byte"},
        "1287": {"synopsis":"Starts with the flag byte (L = A').","comment":"H = the parity so far"},
        "1288": {"comment":"A = 1"},
        "1290": {"comment":"Carry: a marker bit into L, so L is 0 after the eighth bit"},
        "1294": {"synopsis":"The last byte: the parity.","comment":"L = the parity"},
        "1297": {"synopsis":"The bit's second edge.","comment":"A = $0E, the second edge's byte"},
        "1298": {"comment":"Z; the carry (the bit) kept"},
        "1300": {"synopsis":"One edge after the bit's delay, longer for a 1 (SAVE_ONE_DELAY).","comment":"The delay"},
        "1302": {"comment":"A 0 bit: no more"},
        "1304": {"comment":"A 1: $42 more"},
        "1306": {"synopsis":"A 1: the extra delay."},
        "1308": {"synopsis":"The edge.","comment":"The edge"},
        "1310": {"comment":"B = the next delay"},
        "1312": {"comment":"NZ: after the first edge, the second"},
        "1314": {"comment":"B one less"},
        "1315": {"comment":"A = 1 for the next bit's first edge"},
        "1317": {"synopsis":"The next bit of L (shifted out at the top); after 8, the next byte.","comment":"The next bit into the carry"},
        "1319": {"comment":"L not 0: more bits"},
        "1322": {"comment":"One byte less"},
        "1323": {"comment":"IX to the next"},
        "1325": {"comment":"B = the delay before the next byte"},
        "1327": {"comment":"Half-row $7F"},
        "1329": {"comment":"Read"},
        "1331": {"comment":"SPACE (bit 0) into the carry"},
        "1332": {"comment":"SPACE: stop (carry clear)"},
        "1333": {"comment":"D + 1: 0 once DE has gone past 0, the parity sent"},
        "1335": {"comment":"More bytes"},
        "1338": {"comment":"The last delay"},
        "1340": {"synopsis":"A last delay before the return."},
        "1343": {"synopsis":"Where a tape save or load returns: the border back to BORDCR's colour, interrupts on; SPACE\nheld is report D. Keeps AF (carry: the load's success).","comment":"AF kept"},
        "1344": {"comment":"The border colour from BORDCR"},
        "1352": {"comment":"The border back"},
        "1354": {"comment":"Half-row $7F"},
        "1358": {"comment":"SPACE into the carry"},
        "1359": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1360": {"comment":"Not held: fine"},
        "1362": {"comment":"SPACE: report D"},
        "1364": {"synopsis":"AF back."},
        "1366": {"synopsis":"Loads (carry set) or verifies (carry clear) a block from tape: A = the flag byte, IX = the\nstart, DE = the length. Returns with carry set on success.\n1. The input settles for about a second, then a pilot: 256 edges of the right length\n   (LOAD_PILOT), then the sync (LOAD_SYNC_WAIT).\n2. The first byte must be the flag (LOAD_FLAG_TEST, LD_BAD_HEADER); then DE bytes loaded\n   into memory or compared with it; then the parity, which must leave 0.\n3. Each bit is two edges timed by TAPE_TWO_EDGES; a long one is a 1. Each edge flips the\n   border colour.\nSPACE, or a silence, gives up with no carry. Returns through TAPE_RETURN.","comment":"NZ (unless D is $FF), kept in F': the first byte is the flag"},
        "1367": {"comment":"A' = the flag; F' = NZ and the carry (load or verify)"},
        "1368": {"comment":"D back"},
        "1369": {"comment":"No interrupts: exact timing"},
        "1370": {"comment":"White border, MIC bit set"},
        "1374": {"comment":"TAPE_RETURN as the return address"},
        "1378": {"comment":"The input now"},
        "1380": {"comment":"Bit 6 to bit 5"},
        "1381": {"comment":"C bit 5 = the input level"},
        "1383": {"comment":"And red"},
        "1386": {"comment":"Z"},
        "1387": {"synopsis":"Gives up (no carry) unless Z: the restart of the search."},
        "1388": {"synopsis":"Where LOAD starts checking the tape input for a pilot pulse. Klive traps it to load a block\nfrom the tape file at once.","comment":"An edge?"},
        "1391": {"comment":"None: again"},
        "1393": {"comment":"$0415 rounds"},
        "1396": {"synopsis":"About a second's wait (HL = $0415 rounds of B), then an edge again."},
        "1398": {"comment":"One round"},
        "1403": {"comment":"Two edges again"},
        "1406": {"comment":"None: from the start"},
        "1408": {"synopsis":"The pilot: 256 edges, each of the pilot's length (not shorter than B = $C6), else the search\nstarts again.","comment":"B = $9C: the timing start"},
        "1410": {"comment":"Two edges"},
        "1415": {"comment":"Too short (B up to $C6)?"},
        "1418": {"comment":"Then start again"},
        "1420": {"comment":"H counts 256 pilot pairs"},
        "1423": {"synopsis":"The sync: an edge shorter than the pilot's (B below $D4), then the next; the border colours\nchange (C XOR 3), the parity starts at 0.","comment":"B = $C9"},
        "1425": {"comment":"One edge"},
        "1430": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "1431": {"comment":"Still the pilot's?"},
        "1433": {"comment":"Then wait on"},
        "1435": {"comment":"The sync's second edge"},
        "1438": {"comment":"None: fail"},
        "1439": {"comment":"The border colours swapped: blue and yellow"},
        "1443": {"comment":"H = 0: the parity"},
        "1445": {"comment":"B = $B0: the timing start"},
        "1447": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "1449": {"synopsis":"A byte read: the first is the flag (LOAD_FLAG_TEST), the rest are loaded or verified.","comment":"F' back: NZ for the flag byte, carry for load"},
        "1450": {"comment":"The flag byte"},
        "1452": {"comment":"Verify"},
        "1454": {"comment":"Loaded"},
        "1459": {"synopsis":"The flag byte must equal A' (LD_BAD_HEADER returns otherwise); DE + 1, as the flag does not\ncount.","comment":"The carry (load or verify) parked in C"},
        "1461": {"comment":"The flag byte against A'"},
        "1462": {"synopsis":"A RET NZ that leaves LOAD when the header read is not the one asked for. Klive's fast load\ncomes here to report a wrong header."},
        "1463": {"comment":"C back, the carry restored"},
        "1466": {"comment":"DE + 1: the flag does not count"},
        "1469": {"synopsis":"Verifying: the byte must equal the one in memory.","comment":"The byte in memory"},
        "1472": {"comment":"Compared"},
        "1473": {"comment":"Different: fail"},
        "1474": {"synopsis":"IX one on."},
        "1476": {"synopsis":"DE one less."},
        "1477": {"comment":"F' kept"},
        "1478": {"comment":"B = $B2: the timing start"},
        "1480": {"synopsis":"L = 1: a marker that comes out of the top after 8 bits."},
        "1482": {"synopsis":"One bit: two edges (TAPE_TWO_EDGES); B past $CB means a 1. Shifted into L until the marker\ncomes out; then the parity H takes the byte, and the next, or the end when DE is 0: carry\nwhen the parity is 0.","comment":"Two edges"},
        "1485": {"comment":"None: fail"},
        "1486": {"comment":"$CB: the threshold between 0 and 1"},
        "1488": {"comment":"Carry for a 1"},
        "1489": {"comment":"Into L; the marker comes out after the eighth"},
        "1491": {"comment":"B = $B0"},
        "1493": {"comment":"More bits"},
        "1496": {"comment":"The parity"},
        "1499": {"comment":"More bytes?"},
        "1503": {"comment":"Carry when the parity is 0"},
        "1506": {"synopsis":"Where LOAD returns after a block has loaded. Klive's fast load resumes here."},
        "1507": {"synopsis":"Waits for two edges (TAPE_EDGE twice). Exit: carry and B = the time; no carry on SPACE or a\ntime-out."},
        "1511": {"synopsis":"Waits for an edge on the tape input (port $FE bit 6, moved to bit 5 against C) after a short\ndelay, counting B up. On the edge: C flipped, the border set from it (bits 0-2) with bit 3,\nand carry. No carry when B runs out (a silence) or SPACE is down.\nChanges: AF, B, C.","comment":"A short delay"},
        "1513": {"synopsis":"The fixed delay before sampling."},
        "1516": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "1517": {"synopsis":"One sample: B + 1 (0: a time-out); SPACE down is the end; an unchanged input samples again.","comment":"B + 1"},
        "1518": {"comment":"Time-out: no carry"},
        "1519": {"comment":"Half-row $7F"},
        "1521": {"comment":"Also the tape input (bit 6)"},
        "1523": {"comment":"SPACE into the carry"},
        "1524": {"comment":"SPACE: no carry"},
        "1525": {"comment":"Against C's level"},
        "1526": {"comment":"The input bit"},
        "1528": {"comment":"No change: again"},
        "1530": {"comment":"C flipped"},
        "1533": {"comment":"The border colour"},
        "1535": {"comment":"MIC bit"},
        "1539": {"comment":"Carry: an edge"},
        "1541": {"synopsis":"SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE (class $0B; T_ADDR - $E0 tells which: 0 SAVE, 1 LOAD, 2 VERIFY,\n3 MERGE):\n1. The name (a string, CLASS_A) into a 17-byte header in the workspace (34 for the others:\n   the second 17 take the headers read): the type byte, the name padded to 10 with spaces,\n   or $FF for an empty one (any name). SAVE needs 1-10 characters (report F); the others cut\n   a longer one to 10.\n2. What follows: DATA name() (an array, types 1 and 2), SCREEN$ (type 3, 6912 bytes from\n   $4000), CODE start,length (type 3), or a program (type 0, LINE n for SAVE), into the\n   header: length, start or LINE, and the program's length.\n3. SAVE_CONTROL for SAVE; otherwise LOAD_HEADER_LOOP.\nObserved: SAVE \"\" and SAVE \"abcdefghijk\" gave \"F Invalid file name\"; SAVE \"a\" CODE was\nrefused when checking."},
        "1542": {"comment":"T_ADDR's low byte - $E0: which command"},
        "1547": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1550": {"comment":"The name, a string"},
        "1553": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "1556": {"comment":"Yes: on to what follows"},
        "1558": {"comment":"17 bytes for SAVE"},
        "1564": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "1567": {"comment":"34 for the others"},
        "1569": {"synopsis":"The header's room (WORK_ROOM), IX at it.","comment":"Room in the workspace"},
        "1570": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "1573": {"comment":"11 bytes"},
        "1575": {"comment":"Spaces"},
        "1577": {"synopsis":"The name filled with spaces; its first byte $FF (no name)."},
        "1581": {"comment":"No name: $FF"},
        "1585": {"comment":"DE = the name, BC = its length"},
        "1588": {"comment":"HL = -10"},
        "1591": {"comment":"Length - 1"},
        "1592": {"comment":"Carry when longer than 10, or empty"},
        "1594": {"comment":"Up to 10: copied as it is"},
        "1596": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "1600": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "1602": {"comment":"SAVE: an empty or long name is report F"},
        "1604": {"synopsis":"An empty name: SAVE needs one (report F, error code $0E); the others keep $FF. Longer than\n10: cut to 10.","comment":"Empty?"},
        "1606": {"comment":"Then the $FF stays"},
        "1608": {"comment":"Cut to 10"},
        "1611": {"synopsis":"The name copied after the type byte.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "1614": {"comment":"Past the type byte"},
        "1615": {"comment":"DE = there, HL = the name"},
        "1616": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "1618": {"synopsis":"What follows the name: DATA, SCREEN$, CODE, or else a program.","comment":"What follows the name"},
        "1619": {"comment":"DATA?"},
        "1621": {"comment":"No"},
        "1626": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "1628": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "1631": {"comment":"Past DATA"},
        "1632": {"comment":"The array (LOOK_VARS)"},
        "1635": {"comment":"C bit 7: an array"},
        "1637": {"comment":"Found"},
        "1639": {"comment":"Not found: HL = 0"},
        "1645": {"comment":"LOAD?"},
        "1646": {"comment":"Then a new array"},
        "1648": {"comment":"Otherwise report 2"},
        "1650": {"synopsis":"The array must be followed by '(' (report C); its length and name into the header.","comment":"NZ: report C"},
        "1653": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "1656": {"comment":"Yes: no header"},
        "1658": {"comment":"The array's length into the header"},
        "1668": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "1669": {"synopsis":"The array's name byte at IX + 14."},
        "1672": {"comment":"Type 1"},
        "1674": {"comment":"A string array?"},
        "1678": {"comment":"Type 2"},
        "1679": {"synopsis":"Type 1 (numbers) or 2 (strings, C bit 6)."},
        "1682": {"synopsis":"Past ')', the statement ends.","comment":"DE = the array's place"},
        "1683": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "1684": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "1686": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "1688": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "1689": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "1692": {"comment":"HL = the array's place"},
        "1693": {"comment":"On"},
        "1696": {"synopsis":"SCREEN$: 6912 ($1B00) bytes from $4000, type 3. Not for MERGE.","comment":"SCREEN$?"},
        "1703": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "1705": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "1708": {"comment":"Past SCREEN$"},
        "1709": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "1712": {"comment":"Length $1B00"},
        "1720": {"comment":"Start $4000"},
        "1729": {"comment":"Type 3"},
        "1731": {"synopsis":"CODE: start and length; SAVE needs both; for the others a missing one is 0, taken from the\ntape. Not for MERGE.","comment":"CODE?"},
        "1738": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "1740": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "1743": {"comment":"Past CODE"},
        "1744": {"comment":"Nothing more?"},
        "1747": {"comment":"No: a start"},
        "1749": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "1753": {"comment":"Needs a start: report C"},
        "1756": {"comment":"Start 0"},
        "1759": {"comment":"And length 0"},
        "1761": {"synopsis":"The start (CLASS_6)."},
        "1764": {"comment":"A ','?"},
        "1769": {"comment":"No: SAVE?"},
        "1773": {"comment":"Needs a length: report C"},
        "1776": {"synopsis":"No length: 0.","comment":"Length 0"},
        "1781": {"synopsis":"',' and the length.","comment":"Past it"},
        "1785": {"synopsis":"The length and start into the header (TAKE_WORD twice); HL = the start.","comment":"The statement must end"},
        "1788": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "1791": {"comment":"The length"},
        "1797": {"comment":"BC = the start"},
        "1800": {"comment":"The start"},
        "1806": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "1808": {"synopsis":"Type 3, then SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD."},
        "1814": {"synopsis":"A program: LINE (SAVE only) or nothing; without LINE the header's line is $80xx (no\nauto-run).","comment":"LINE?"},
        "1818": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "1821": {"comment":"No auto-run"},
        "1827": {"synopsis":"LINE n: the auto-run line into the header (SAVE only, else report C).","comment":"SAVE?"},
        "1831": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "1834": {"comment":"Past LINE"},
        "1835": {"comment":"A number"},
        "1838": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "1841": {"comment":"BC = the line"},
        "1844": {"comment":"Into the header"},
        "1850": {"synopsis":"Type 0: the length (E_LINE - PROG - 1, the program and its variables) and the program's own\nlength (VARS - PROG) into the header; HL = PROG."},
        "1854": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "1857": {"comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "1861": {"comment":"One less"},
        "1862": {"comment":"The length"},
        "1870": {"comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "1873": {"comment":"Less PROG: the program's own length"},
        "1881": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "1882": {"synopsis":"SAVE: SAVE_CONTROL. The others: LOAD_HEADER_LOOP, with HL the destination (0 for a new\narray).","comment":"SAVE?"},
        "1886": {"comment":"Yes: SAVE_CONTROL"},
        "1889": {"comment":"The destination kept"},
        "1890": {"comment":"IX to the second half, for the headers read"},
        "1895": {"synopsis":"Reads headers (17 bytes, flag 0, LD_BYTES) into the second half until one of the wanted type\nand name arrives; each one's kind and name are printed on the upper screen (SCR_CT = 3), as\n\"Program: \", \"Bytes: \"... (TAPE_KIND_MSGS).\nObserved: LOAD \"abc\" CODE printed \"Bytes: xyz\" for a header before it and went on to the\nnext.","comment":"IX kept"},
        "1897": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "1900": {"comment":"Flag 0: a header"},
        "1901": {"comment":"Load"},
        "1905": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "1907": {"comment":"Failed: again"},
        "1909": {"comment":"Stream -2: the upper screen"},
        "1914": {"comment":"SCR_CT = 3: no scroll prompt"},
        "1918": {"comment":"C = $80: another type"},
        "1920": {"comment":"The type read"},
        "1923": {"comment":"The wanted type?"},
        "1928": {"comment":"C = $F6: -10, counting up to 0 with the name"},
        "1930": {"synopsis":"C = $F6 for the wanted type ($80 for another); a type over 3 is skipped.","comment":"Over 3?"},
        "1932": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "1934": {"comment":"DE = the kind messages"},
        "1938": {"comment":"\"Program: \" and so on"},
        "1942": {"comment":"DE = IX"},
        "1945": {"comment":"HL = IX - 16: the wanted name"},
        "1949": {"comment":"10 characters"},
        "1951": {"comment":"The wanted name's first byte"},
        "1952": {"comment":"$FF: any name?"},
        "1955": {"comment":"Then C + 10: a match whatever the name"},
        "1958": {"synopsis":"The name: each character printed (RST $10); C counts the matches up to 0; a wanted name of\n$FF (any) counts as all 10.","comment":"The next character read"},
        "1960": {"comment":"The same as the wanted one?"},
        "1964": {"comment":"One match more"},
        "1965": {"synopsis":"Prints the character."},
        "1966": {"comment":"All 10"},
        "1968": {"comment":"C negative: not all matched, or another type?"},
        "1970": {"comment":"Then the next header"},
        "1972": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "1975": {"comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "1976": {"comment":"The type"},
        "1979": {"comment":"CODE?"},
        "1983": {"comment":"LOAD?"},
        "1987": {"comment":"A program or an array"},
        "1990": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "1992": {"comment":"MERGE_LOAD"},
        "1995": {"synopsis":"VERIFY, and LOAD of CODE: a wanted length (when not 0) must not be shorter than the block's\n(report R), and only CODE may be longer; the start is the wanted one, or the header's when\n0. Then LOAD_BLOCK, verifying for VERIFY.\nObserved: LOAD \"\" CODE loaded 1,2,3,4 at 32768; LOAD \"abc\" CODE 40000 at 40000; VERIFY with\none byte different and LOAD \"\" CODE 50000,4 for an 8-byte block gave \"R Tape loading error\".","comment":"The destination kept"},
        "1996": {"comment":"HL = the wanted length"},
        "2002": {"comment":"DE = the block's length"},
        "2008": {"comment":"0: any"},
        "2012": {"comment":"The wanted less the block's"},
        "2014": {"comment":"Shorter: report R"},
        "2016": {"comment":"The same: fine"},
        "2018": {"comment":"Longer: CODE only"},
        "2023": {"comment":"Otherwise report R"},
        "2025": {"synopsis":"HL: the wanted start, or the header's.","comment":"HL = the wanted start"},
        "2026": {"comment":"0?"},
        "2030": {"comment":"Then the header's"},
        "2036": {"synopsis":"IX = the start; carry for load, clear for VERIFY.","comment":"IX = the start"},
        "2039": {"comment":"VERIFY?"},
        "2044": {"comment":"Carry: load"},
        "2047": {"comment":"VERIFY: no carry"},
        "2048": {"synopsis":"A = $FF: the data block's flag."},
        "2050": {"synopsis":"LD_BYTES; failing it is report R."},
        "2053": {"comment":"Loaded"},
        "2054": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $1A (report R, \"Tape loading error\")."},
        "2056": {"synopsis":"LOAD of a program or an array: room is checked for the new length (TEST_ROOM, against the\nold one's when there is one).","comment":"DE = the new length"},
        "2062": {"comment":"The destination kept"},
        "2063": {"comment":"An existing one?"},
        "2067": {"comment":"No: + 3 for an array's name and length"},
        "2070": {"comment":"HL = the room needed"},
        "2073": {"synopsis":"The old length: only a longer new one needs more room.","comment":"HL = the old length"},
        "2079": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = the new one"},
        "2080": {"comment":"The new less the old, less 1"},
        "2083": {"comment":"Not longer: no room needed"},
        "2085": {"synopsis":"TEST_ROOM for the difference + 5.","comment":"+ 5"},
        "2089": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "2091": {"comment":"Room?"},
        "2094": {"synopsis":"A program: LOAD_PROGRAM. An array: the old one removed (RECLAIM), and a new one made at the\nend of the variables (LOAD_NEW_ARRAY).","comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "2095": {"comment":"The type"},
        "2099": {"comment":"0: a program"},
        "2101": {"comment":"An old array?"},
        "2103": {"comment":"No: a new one"},
        "2105": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "2110": {"comment":"+ 3: the name and length"},
        "2113": {"comment":"IX kept in X_PTR"},
        "2117": {"comment":"The old array removed"},
        "2120": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "2124": {"synopsis":"The new array's name, length and room (MAKE_ROOM); then LOAD_BLOCK into it.","comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "2127": {"comment":"Less 1: the variables' $80"},
        "2128": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "2134": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "2135": {"comment":"+ 3"},
        "2138": {"comment":"A = the array's name"},
        "2142": {"comment":"Room at the end of the variables"},
        "2147": {"comment":"The name"},
        "2148": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "2150": {"comment":"The length"},
        "2154": {"comment":"IX = the array's data"},
        "2157": {"comment":"Load"},
        "2158": {"comment":"The data flag"},
        "2163": {"synopsis":"The program and variables replaced: the old ones removed (RECLAIM_DE_HL from PROG to\nE_LINE), room made for the new length, VARS set from the header's program length; an\nauto-run line (below $4000) goes into NEWPPC, NSPPC = 0. Then LOAD_BLOCK.\nObserved: a program header with line 10 loaded the line and ran it (the report named 10:1).","comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "2164": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "2167": {"comment":"Less 1: up to the variables' $80"},
        "2168": {"comment":"IX kept in X_PTR"},
        "2172": {"comment":"BC = the new length"},
        "2179": {"comment":"The old program and variables removed"},
        "2183": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "2185": {"comment":"Room for the new ones"},
        "2188": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "2192": {"comment":"HL to the room's start"},
        "2193": {"comment":"BC = the program's own length"},
        "2199": {"comment":"VARS = past it"},
        "2203": {"comment":"H = the auto-run line's high byte"},
        "2207": {"comment":"$40 or more: no auto-run"},
        "2211": {"comment":"L = its low byte"},
        "2214": {"comment":"NEWPPC = the line"},
        "2217": {"comment":"NSPPC = 0: its first statement"},
        "2221": {"synopsis":"LOAD_BLOCK into the room.","comment":"DE = the length"},
        "2222": {"comment":"IX = the room"},
        "2224": {"comment":"Load"},
        "2225": {"comment":"The data flag"},
        "2230": {"synopsis":"MERGE: the program is loaded into the workspace (with an $80 after it), then its lines\n(MERGE_LINES) and variables (MERGE_VARS) are put into place one by one, each replacing one\nwith the same number or name.\nObserved: MERGE of 20 PRINT 8 into 10 PRINT 7 listed both.","comment":"BC = the length"},
        "2236": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "2237": {"comment":"One more, for the $80"},
        "2238": {"comment":"Room in the workspace"},
        "2239": {"comment":"An $80 after it"},
        "2241": {"comment":"HL = the room's start"},
        "2242": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "2243": {"comment":"The start kept twice"},
        "2245": {"comment":"IX = the start"},
        "2250": {"comment":"Loaded"},
        "2253": {"comment":"HL = the merged program"},
        "2254": {"comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "2258": {"synopsis":"The next merged line, until the variables start (bits 6-7).","comment":"The merged line number's high byte"},
        "2259": {"comment":"Bits 6-7 set: the variables"},
        "2263": {"synopsis":"Compares the merged line's number with the program's: a bigger one moves on through the\nprogram (NEXT_ITEM).","comment":"The program line's high byte"},
        "2265": {"comment":"Compared"},
        "2267": {"comment":"Different"},
        "2269": {"comment":"The low bytes"},
        "2271": {"synopsis":"The low bytes.","comment":"DE and HL back"},
        "2273": {"comment":"Not bigger: put it in"},
        "2275": {"comment":"The merged line kept"},
        "2276": {"comment":"HL = the program line"},
        "2277": {"comment":"DE = the next one"},
        "2280": {"comment":"HL = the merged line"},
        "2283": {"synopsis":"Puts the line in (MERGE_ENTER): Z replaces the one with the same number.","comment":"The line in"},
        "2288": {"synopsis":"The merged variables, one by one, until $80.","comment":"The merged item's first byte"},
        "2289": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "2290": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "2293": {"comment":"The item kept"},
        "2294": {"comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "2297": {"synopsis":"Looks for a variable with the same first byte in the program's.","comment":"The program's variable"},
        "2298": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "2300": {"comment":"Then a new one"},
        "2302": {"comment":"The same first byte?"},
        "2305": {"synopsis":"The next one (NEXT_ITEM)."},
        "2306": {"comment":"DE = the next"},
        "2310": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "2313": {"synopsis":"A long name ($A0 type): the letters must match too.","comment":"The type bits"},
        "2315": {"comment":"A long name?"},
        "2317": {"comment":"No: the same"},
        "2319": {"comment":"DE = the merged item"},
        "2320": {"comment":"Kept again, with HL"},
        "2322": {"synopsis":"Letter by letter, to the one with bit 7."},
        "2324": {"comment":"Its next letter"},
        "2325": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "2326": {"comment":"No"},
        "2328": {"comment":"Bit 7: the last?"},
        "2329": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "2331": {"comment":"HL back: the same"},
        "2334": {"synopsis":"Not the same: on.","comment":"HL back"},
        "2337": {"synopsis":"The same: A = $FF, so Z (replace)."},
        "2339": {"synopsis":"Puts the variable in (MERGE_ENTER).","comment":"DE = the merged item"},
        "2340": {"comment":"HL = it, DE = the place"},
        "2341": {"comment":"A + 1: 0 (Z) for the same, NZ for a new one"},
        "2342": {"comment":"Carry: a variable"},
        "2348": {"synopsis":"Puts the item at HL (in the workspace) into the program before DE: with Z the item at DE is\nremoved first (replace). Room is made (MAKE_ROOM, PROG kept), the item copied from the\nworkspace, then removed from there (RECLAIM).","comment":"NZ: insert only"},
        "2350": {"comment":"F kept"},
        "2351": {"comment":"X_PTR = the merged item"},
        "2354": {"comment":"HL = the program's item"},
        "2355": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "2358": {"comment":"Removed"},
        "2361": {"comment":"DE = the place"},
        "2362": {"comment":"HL = the merged item, moved with X_PTR"},
        "2365": {"comment":"F back"},
        "2366": {"synopsis":"Inserts: the item's length (NEXT_ITEM), the room.","comment":"F kept: carry for a variable"},
        "2367": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "2368": {"comment":"BC = the merged item's length"},
        "2371": {"comment":"X_PTR = it"},
        "2374": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "2377": {"comment":"PROG kept, HL = the place"},
        "2378": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "2379": {"comment":"F back"},
        "2380": {"comment":"A variable"},
        "2382": {"comment":"A line: room just before the place"},
        "2383": {"comment":"The room"},
        "2389": {"synopsis":"A variable: room at HL.","comment":"The room"},
        "2392": {"synopsis":"PROG back, the item copied and removed from the workspace.","comment":"HL = the room's start"},
        "2393": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "2394": {"comment":"DE = PROG as it was"},
        "2395": {"comment":"PROG back"},
        "2399": {"comment":"DE = the merged item"},
        "2405": {"comment":"DE = the room, HL = the item"},
        "2406": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "2408": {"comment":"HL = the item"},
        "2409": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "2411": {"comment":"Removed from the workspace"},
        "2416": {"synopsis":"SAVE: \"Start tape, then press any key.\" in the lower screen (TAPE_MESSAGES), a key\n(WAIT_KEY), the header (17 bytes, flag 0, SA_BYTES), a gap of 50 interrupts, then the data\n(flag $FF).","comment":"The start kept"},
        "2417": {"comment":"Stream -3: the lower screen"},
        "2422": {"comment":"Message 0: \"Start tape, then press any key.\""},
        "2429": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5: the lower screen to be cleared"},
        "2433": {"comment":"A key"},
        "2436": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "2438": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "2441": {"comment":"Flag 0: the header"},
        "2445": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "2447": {"comment":"50"},
        "2449": {"synopsis":"The gap: 50 HALTs."},
        "2452": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "2458": {"comment":"Flag $FF: data"},
        "2460": {"comment":"IX = the start"},
        "2462": {"comment":"The data saved"},
        "2465": {"synopsis":"Tape messages, for PRINT_MESSAGE (read from $0977): entry 0 is empty ($80); then \"Start\ntape, then press any key.\", and, each after a $0D, \"Program: \", \"Number array: \", \"Character\narray: \" and \"Bytes: \"."},
        "2496": {"synopsis":"Read as a table from here (LOAD_HEADER_SHOW, DE = $09C0): entry 0 is the last byte of \"Start\ntape, then press any key.\", entries 1-4 the kinds of file, so type n prints entry n + 1."},
        "2548": {"synopsis":"The output routine of channels K, S and P (CHANNEL_DATA): prints A at the current channel's\nposition (FETCH_POS) on the upper or lower screen or into the printer buffer, and stores the\nnew position (STORE_POS):\n1. $20 and up: a character, block graphic, UDG or keyword (OUT_ABLE).\n2. $06-$17: the control codes, through CTRL_TABLE; $10-$17 take their operands from the next\n   calls (OUT_COLOUR, OUT_AT_TAB).\n3. Other codes print as '?'.\nObserved: AT 5,3 \"A\", TAB 10 \"B\", comma \"C\" put A, B and C at columns 3, 10 and 16 of line\n5; \"XY\", $08, \"Z\" printed XZ.","comment":"BC, HL = the position"},
        "2551": {"comment":"Printable?"},
        "2553": {"comment":"Yes: OUT_ABLE"},
        "2556": {"comment":"$00-$05: '?'"},
        "2560": {"comment":"$18-$1F: '?'"},
        "2564": {"comment":"$0A0B + code: the code's offset in CTRL_TABLE"},
        "2567": {"comment":"DE = the code"},
        "2571": {"comment":"E = the offset"},
        "2572": {"comment":"HL = the handler"},
        "2573": {"comment":"The handler, with the position in BC and HL"},
        "2574": {"comment":"BC, HL = the position, then the handler"},
        "2577": {"synopsis":"Control-code table: 18 offsets for codes $06-$17, read at $0A0B + code; each counts from its\nown byte. $06 OUT_COMMA, $08 OUT_BACK, $09 OUT_RIGHT, $0D OUT_ENTER, $10-$15 OUT_COLOUR,\n$16-$17 OUT_AT_TAB; $07, $0A-$0C, $0E and $0F OUT_QUEST."},
        "2595": {"synopsis":"$08: the position one column back (C + 1). Past the left edge: the previous line's last\ncolumn, but not above the top line (the top left then); the printer stays at its left\ncolumn.","comment":"One column back (C counts down)"},
        "2596": {"comment":"Past the left edge ($22)?"},
        "2601": {"comment":"The printer?"},
        "2605": {"comment":"Then the left column"},
        "2607": {"comment":"The line above, at its last column"},
        "2608": {"comment":"C = 2: the last column"},
        "2612": {"comment":"Above the top line: stay at the top left"},
        "2615": {"comment":"Back to the top line"},
        "2616": {"synopsis":"C = $21: the left column."},
        "2618": {"synopsis":"SET_PRINT_POS with BC."},
        "2621": {"synopsis":"$09: one column on, leaving the screen as it is: a space printed with P_FLAG = 1 (OVER 1)\nfor the moment.","comment":"P_FLAG kept"},
        "2625": {"comment":"P_FLAG = 1: OVER 1"},
        "2629": {"comment":"A space"},
        "2631": {"comment":"Printed over the old"},
        "2635": {"comment":"P_FLAG back"},
        "2639": {"synopsis":"ENTER ($0D): the next line's left column, scrolling when needed (OUT_SCROLL); for the\nprinter, the buffer printed (PRBUFF_OUT).","comment":"The printer?"},
        "2643": {"comment":"Then the buffer printed"},
        "2646": {"comment":"The left column"},
        "2648": {"comment":"Scroll if needed"},
        "2651": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "2652": {"comment":"Set"},
        "2655": {"synopsis":"The comma ($06): spaces to the next half-line column, 0 or 16 (OUT_FILL with A = 0 or 16).","comment":"BC = the position"},
        "2658": {"comment":"A = C, $21 - the column"},
        "2659": {"comment":"Less 2: 31 - the column"},
        "2661": {"comment":"16 for a column below 16, else 0"},
        "2663": {"comment":"Spaces to it"},
        "2665": {"synopsis":"An unused code prints as '?'.","comment":"'?'"},
        "2667": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "2669": {"synopsis":"AT's or TAB's first operand: kept in TVDATA's second byte ($5C0F); the next byte goes to\nOUT_OPERANDS.","comment":"The next byte to OUT_OPERANDS"},
        "2672": {"comment":"The first operand kept"},
        "2675": {"comment":"Set"},
        "2677": {"synopsis":"AT ($16) or TAB ($17): the code kept in TVDATA, and the output routine set to OUT_OPERAND_2\nfor the first operand.","comment":"The next byte to OUT_OPERAND_2"},
        "2682": {"synopsis":"$10-$15 (INK, PAPER, FLASH, BRIGHT, INVERSE, OVER): the code kept in TVDATA, and the output\nroutine set to OUT_OPERANDS for the operand.","comment":"The next byte to OUT_OPERANDS"},
        "2685": {"synopsis":"TVDATA = A, the control code."},
        "2688": {"synopsis":"Stores DE as the current channel's output routine (the first word at CURCHL), so the next\nbyte printed goes there.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = CURCHL"},
        "2691": {"comment":"Its output routine"},
        "2695": {"synopsis":"The last operand: the output routine back to SCREEN_OUTPUT; then by the code in TVDATA (L)\nwith the operand in D (and the first in H):\n1. $10-$15: SET_TEMP_ATTR sets the temporary colour or effect.\n2. AT ($16): line H, column D. A column over 31, or a line over 22, is report B\n   (OUT_AT_ERR); a line inside the lower screen while printing above it stops with report 5\n   (REPORT_5).\n3. TAB ($17): OUT_TAB.\nObserved: AT 22,0 in the upper screen stopped with error code 4 at REPORT_5.","comment":"SCREEN_OUTPUT again"},
        "2698": {"comment":"Set"},
        "2701": {"comment":"L = the code, H = the first operand"},
        "2704": {"comment":"D = this operand"},
        "2706": {"comment":"A colour code?"},
        "2708": {"comment":"SET_TEMP_ATTR"},
        "2711": {"comment":"TAB"},
        "2713": {"comment":"B = the line"},
        "2714": {"comment":"C = the column"},
        "2715": {"comment":"Column over 31?"},
        "2718": {"comment":"Report B"},
        "2720": {"comment":"C = $21 - column"},
        "2723": {"comment":"The printer?"},
        "2727": {"comment":"Then only the column"},
        "2729": {"comment":"Line over 22?"},
        "2732": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B): AT out of range."},
        "2735": {"comment":"A = 23 - the line"},
        "2737": {"comment":"B = $18 - the line"},
        "2738": {"comment":"The lower screen: OUT_SCROLL checks it"},
        "2745": {"comment":"Inside the lower screen: report 5"},
        "2751": {"synopsis":"SET_PRINT_POS with B, C: the new position."},
        "2754": {"synopsis":"TAB: A = the column (the operands' low byte).","comment":"A = TAB's column"},
        "2755": {"synopsis":"Prints spaces up to column A (0-31) of this line: (A - the current column) mod 32 of them,\nnone when already there. FLAGS bit 0 set, so no leading spaces are added.","comment":"C = $21 - the current column"},
        "2758": {"comment":"A + $21 - the column"},
        "2759": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "2760": {"comment":"Mod 32: the spaces"},
        "2762": {"comment":"None"},
        "2763": {"comment":"D = the count"},
        "2764": {"comment":"No leading space"},
        "2768": {"synopsis":"One space (PRINT_A_EXX), D times.","comment":"A space"},
        "2770": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "2777": {"synopsis":"A printable code: OUT_ANY prints it, and the new position is stored (STORE_POS follows)."},
        "2780": {"synopsis":"Stores the print position: B = line and C = column (as SET_PRINT_POS takes them), HL = the\ndisplay address. Into S_POSN and DF_CC for the upper screen.\nChanges: F.","comment":"The printer?"},
        "2786": {"comment":"The lower screen?"},
        "2792": {"comment":"S_POSN"},
        "2796": {"comment":"DF_CC"},
        "2800": {"synopsis":"The lower screen (TV_FLAG bit 0): into S_POSNL, ECHO_E and DF_CCL.","comment":"S_POSNL"},
        "2804": {"comment":"ECHO_E"},
        "2808": {"comment":"DF_CCL"},
        "2812": {"synopsis":"The printer (FLAGS bit 1): C into P_POSN, HL into PR_CC."},
        "2819": {"synopsis":"The current print position: BC (B = line, C = column, as SET_PRINT_POS takes them) and HL\n(its display or buffer address), from S_POSN and DF_CC (upper screen), S_POSNL and DF_CCL\n(lower screen, TV_FLAG bit 0), or P_POSN and PR_CC (printer, FLAGS bit 1).\nChanges: F, BC, HL.","comment":"The printer?"},
        "2825": {"comment":"S_POSN"},
        "2829": {"comment":"DF_CC"},
        "2832": {"comment":"The lower screen?"},
        "2836": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "2837": {"comment":"S_POSNL"},
        "2841": {"comment":"DF_CCL"},
        "2845": {"synopsis":"The printer: C = P_POSN, HL = PR_CC."},
        "2852": {"synopsis":"Prints character A ($20 and up) at BC, HL: below $80 from the character set (OUT_CHAR);\n$80-$8F a block graphic built in MEMBOT (OUT_GRAPHIC); $90-$A4 a UDG and $A5 up a keyword\n(OUT_UDG_TOKEN).","comment":"Below $80: a character"},
        "2856": {"comment":"$90 and up: a UDG or keyword"},
        "2860": {"comment":"B = the graphic"},
        "2861": {"comment":"Its pattern at MEMBOT"},
        "2864": {"comment":"BC, HL = the position again"},
        "2867": {"comment":"DE = the pattern"},
        "2872": {"synopsis":"Builds block graphic B ($80-$8F) as an 8-byte pattern at MEMBOT ($5C92): the top four rows\nfrom bits 0 (right half, $0F) and 1 (left half, $F0), the bottom four from bits 2 and 3.\nObserved: $83 printed four rows of $FF over four of $00.","comment":"HL = MEMBOT"},
        "2875": {"comment":"The top four rows"},
        "2878": {"synopsis":"Four rows from the next two bits of B.","comment":"The next bit into the carry"},
        "2880": {"comment":"$FF for a 1"},
        "2881": {"comment":"The right half"},
        "2883": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "2887": {"comment":"The left half"},
        "2889": {"comment":"Both"},
        "2890": {"comment":"4 rows"},
        "2892": {"synopsis":"A into C (4) bytes at HL."},
        "2898": {"synopsis":"$90-$A4: the UDG A - $90, from UDG (OUT_CHAR_BC); $A5 and up: OUT_TOKEN.\nObserved: $90 printed the pattern at UDG, $F5 printed \" PRINT\".","comment":"A keyword?"},
        "2900": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2902": {"comment":"A = the UDG's number"},
        "2904": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "2905": {"comment":"BC = UDG"},
        "2911": {"synopsis":"Prints keyword A - $A5 (PRINT_TOKEN), then fetches the position again.","comment":"PRINT_TOKEN"},
        "2914": {"comment":"The position again"},
        "2917": {"synopsis":"Prints A from the character set (CHARS + 8 x A); FLAGS bit 0 set for a space, cleared\notherwise (so a keyword after a space gets no extra space).","comment":"BC kept"},
        "2918": {"comment":"BC = CHARS"},
        "2922": {"synopsis":"Prints character A of the 8-byte table at BC.","comment":"HL kept in DE"},
        "2923": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "2926": {"comment":"Bit 0 clear"},
        "2928": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "2932": {"comment":"Set for a space"},
        "2934": {"synopsis":"DE = BC + 8 x A: the pattern.","comment":"HL = A"},
        "2937": {"comment":"Times 8"},
        "2940": {"comment":"+ the table"},
        "2941": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "2942": {"comment":"DE = the pattern, HL = the address"},
        "2943": {"synopsis":"Prints the 8-byte pattern at DE at the position BC, HL, then moves on a column:\n1. Past the last column (C = 1): the next line's left column; for the printer, the line goes\n   out first (PRBUFF_OUT); a new line calls OUT_SCROLL.\n2. Each row: (screen AND B) XOR pattern XOR C, B = $FF for OVER (P_FLAG bit 0) or 0, C = $FF\n   for INVERSE (bit 2) or 0. Screen rows step by 256 (INC D), the printer buffer's by 32.\n3. The screen cell's attribute (OUT_ATTR); FLAGS2 bit 1 set for the printer (its buffer\n   holds something).\nExit: C one less, HL one on.\nObserved: INVERSE 1 printed A's row $3C as $C3; with OVER 1 a B printed on a B left $00.","comment":"A = C - 1"},
        "2945": {"comment":"A = $21, the flags kept"},
        "2947": {"comment":"Not past the last column"},
        "2949": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "2950": {"comment":"C = $21: the left column"},
        "2951": {"comment":"The printer?"},
        "2958": {"comment":"The line out"},
        "2962": {"comment":"A = C"},
        "2963": {"synopsis":"C was $21: at a new line's start, OUT_SCROLL first.","comment":"At the left column?"},
        "2965": {"comment":"A new line: scroll if needed"},
        "2969": {"comment":"BC and HL kept"},
        "2971": {"comment":"P_FLAG"},
        "2974": {"comment":"B = $FF: OVER 1 keeps the old byte to XOR with"},
        "2976": {"comment":"Bit 0 (OVER) into the carry"},
        "2977": {"comment":"OVER 1: B stays $FF"},
        "2979": {"comment":"OVER 0: B = 0, the old byte dropped"},
        "2980": {"synopsis":"P_FLAG bit 2 (INVERSE) into C."},
        "2982": {"comment":"C = $FF for INVERSE"},
        "2984": {"comment":"8 rows"},
        "2986": {"comment":"No carry: the screen"},
        "2987": {"comment":"The printer?"},
        "2993": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 1: the buffer is not empty"},
        "2997": {"comment":"Carry: the printer"},
        "2998": {"synopsis":"A' = 8 rows; the printer's flag in carry.","comment":"DE = the address, HL = the pattern"},
        "2999": {"synopsis":"One row: the old byte AND B, XOR the pattern, XOR C.","comment":"The row count kept"},
        "3000": {"comment":"The old byte"},
        "3004": {"comment":"The new one"},
        "3005": {"comment":"The row count back"},
        "3006": {"comment":"The printer"},
        "3008": {"comment":"The next pixel row"},
        "3009": {"synopsis":"The next row and pattern byte."},
        "3010": {"comment":"One row less"},
        "3013": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "3014": {"comment":"Back to the last row"},
        "3015": {"comment":"The screen?"},
        "3019": {"comment":"Then its attribute"},
        "3022": {"comment":"HL and BC back"},
        "3024": {"comment":"One column on"},
        "3025": {"comment":"The next address"},
        "3027": {"synopsis":"The printer: the next row is 32 bytes on."},
        "3028": {"comment":"32 bytes on"},
        "3035": {"synopsis":"Sets the attribute of the cell whose last pixel row is at HL from ATTR_T, keeping the old\nbits where MASK_T has 1s. P_FLAG bit 6 (PAPER 9): the paper becomes 7 or 0, contrasting with\nthe ink; bit 4 (INK 9): the ink becomes 7 or 0, contrasting with the paper.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"The attribute address from the pixel address"},
        "3039": {"comment":"The third of the screen"},
        "3041": {"comment":"+ $5800"},
        "3044": {"comment":"E = ATTR_T, D = MASK_T"},
        "3048": {"comment":"ATTR_T, with the old attribute where MASK_T is 1"},
        "3052": {"comment":"PAPER 9?"},
        "3058": {"comment":"Paper 0"},
        "3060": {"comment":"Light ink (bit 2)? Paper 0, else 7"},
        "3064": {"comment":"Paper 7"},
        "3066": {"synopsis":"INK 9 (P_FLAG bit 4): ink 0 for light paper (bit 5), else 7.","comment":"INK 9?"},
        "3072": {"comment":"Ink 0"},
        "3074": {"comment":"Light paper?"},
        "3078": {"comment":"Ink 7"},
        "3080": {"synopsis":"Stores the attribute."},
        "3082": {"synopsis":"Prints message A of the table at DE (its entry A + 1: entry 0 is a filler), through\nPRINT_ENTRY, never with a space after it; a space before only as PRINT_ENTRY's rule gives it\n(A $20 or more).","comment":"HL kept"},
        "3083": {"comment":"H = 0"},
        "3085": {"comment":"The stack gets D = 0: a message, not a token"},
        "3088": {"synopsis":"Prints keyword A of KEYWORD_TABLE (0 = RND) with its spaces: one before when A is $20 or\nmore, the keyword starts with a letter and FLAGS bit 0 is clear; one after when A is 3 or\nmore and the keyword ends in a letter or $.","comment":"DE = KEYWORD_TABLE"},
        "3091": {"comment":"The token number kept, for the space after"},
        "3092": {"synopsis":"The part PRINT_MESSAGE and PRINT_TOKEN share:\n1. FIND_ENTRY finds the entry; no carry (A $20 or more, a letter first) prints a space\n   before it when FLAGS bit 0 is clear.\n2. The characters, bit 7 removed, up to the one with bit 7 set (PRINT_ENTRY_CHR).\n3. With the number from the stack in D (0 for a message), PRINT_TRAIL_SP decides on a space\n   after it.","comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "3095": {"comment":"A $20 or more and a letter first?"},
        "3097": {"comment":"A space"},
        "3099": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0 set: no space"},
        "3106": {"synopsis":"Prints the entry's characters, bit 7 removed, up to and including the one with bit 7 set.","comment":"The next character"},
        "3107": {"comment":"Bit 7 removed"},
        "3109": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "3112": {"comment":"Again, for its bit 7"},
        "3113": {"comment":"On"},
        "3114": {"comment":"Bit 7 into the carry, A = the character x 2"},
        "3115": {"comment":"Not the last: on"},
        "3117": {"comment":"D = 0 for a message, the entry number for a token"},
        "3118": {"comment":"A = the last character x 2: \"$\"?"},
        "3122": {"comment":"\"A\" or above: a letter?"},
        "3124": {"comment":"No: no space after"},
        "3125": {"synopsis":"A space after the entry when its number is 3 or more (PRINT_A_EXX).","comment":"A = the entry's number"},
        "3126": {"comment":"Below 3: no space after"},
        "3129": {"comment":"A space"},
        "3131": {"synopsis":"Prints A by RST $10 (PRINT_A) under the alternate register set, so the caller's BC, DE and\nHL are kept; DE' is kept too.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "3132": {"comment":"The alternate set: BC, DE and HL kept"},
        "3133": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "3137": {"synopsis":"DE = entry A + 1 of the table at DE: A + 1 strings skipped, each ended by bit 7. Carry when\nA < $20; otherwise A = the entry's first character less \"A\" (carry when below \"A\").\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"A kept"},
        "3138": {"comment":"HL = the table"},
        "3139": {"comment":"A + 1 strings to skip"},
        "3140": {"synopsis":"Past one string: to the byte after the one with bit 7 set.","comment":"Bit 7: the string's last?"},
        "3142": {"comment":"On"},
        "3143": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "3145": {"comment":"One string less"},
        "3146": {"comment":"More to skip"},
        "3148": {"comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "3149": {"comment":"A back"},
        "3150": {"comment":"Below $20: carry"},
        "3153": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "3154": {"comment":"Less \"A\": carry when below"},
        "3157": {"synopsis":"Checks that the line B the next character goes on is on the screen, scrolling when it is\nnot; returns through SET_PRINT_POS. Nothing for the printer.\n1. Upper screen: a line inside the lower screen stops with report 5; the line just below the\n   upper screen scrolls: an automatic listing stops there once the current line is shown\n   (BREG), returning from AUTO_LIST (SP = LIST_SP); otherwise SCR_CT counts down, and at 0\n   the \"scroll?\" prompt waits for a key (OUT_SCR_COUNT), then OUT_SCR_UPPER.\n2. Lower screen: OUT_SCR_LOWER grows it.\nObserved: printing 30 lines from a cleared screen stopped at the prompt's WAIT_KEY with\nSCR_CT set to 22.","comment":"The printer?"},
        "3161": {"comment":"Then nothing"},
        "3162": {"comment":"Return through SET_PRINT_POS"},
        "3166": {"comment":"A = the line"},
        "3167": {"comment":"The lower screen?"},
        "3171": {"comment":"Then OUT_SCR_LOWER"},
        "3174": {"comment":"Inside the lower screen?"},
        "3179": {"comment":"Not at the bottom: no scroll"},
        "3180": {"comment":"An automatic listing?"},
        "3186": {"comment":"E = BREG, as the listing left it"},
        "3189": {"comment":"The current line not listed yet: scroll"},
        "3192": {"comment":"Listed: end the listing, back past AUTO_LIST"},
        "3206": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 4 (report 5): out of screen."},
        "3208": {"synopsis":"SCR_CT one less; at 0, \"scroll?\": SCR_CT = $18 - B for the next time, the message in the\nlower screen (stream -3, SCROLL_MESSAGE), a key (WAIT_KEY). SPACE, STOP ($E2) or N stop with\nreport D (REPORT_D); any other key scrolls on, the colours and stream -2 back.","comment":"SCR_CT one less"},
        "3211": {"comment":"Not 0: scroll"},
        "3213": {"comment":"A = $18 - B"},
        "3216": {"comment":"SCR_CT for the next time"},
        "3219": {"comment":"ATTR_T and MASK_T kept"},
        "3223": {"comment":"P_FLAG kept"},
        "3227": {"comment":"Stream -3: the lower screen"},
        "3232": {"comment":"Message 0: \"scroll?\""},
        "3233": {"comment":"DE = SCROLL_MESSAGE"},
        "3236": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "3239": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5: the lower screen to be cleared"},
        "3243": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "3246": {"comment":"Bit 3: L mode"},
        "3248": {"comment":"Bit 5: no key yet"},
        "3250": {"comment":"The alternate set kept"},
        "3251": {"comment":"A key"},
        "3255": {"comment":"SPACE?"},
        "3257": {"comment":"Report D"},
        "3259": {"comment":"STOP?"},
        "3261": {"comment":"Report D"},
        "3263": {"comment":"\"N\" or \"n\"?"},
        "3267": {"comment":"Report D"},
        "3269": {"comment":"Stream -2: the upper screen again"},
        "3274": {"comment":"P_FLAG back"},
        "3278": {"comment":"ATTR_T and MASK_T back"},
        "3282": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the whole screen up a line (SCROLL_SCREEN), then swaps the attributes of line 23 and\nthe upper screen's last line, which the scroll left with each other's colours. Returns with\nB = DF_SZ + 1, C = $21: the upper screen's last line.","comment":"The whole screen up a line"},
        "3285": {"comment":"B = DF_SZ"},
        "3288": {"comment":"+ 1: the upper screen's last line"},
        "3289": {"comment":"C = $21: the left column"},
        "3291": {"comment":"Kept for the return"},
        "3292": {"comment":"HL = that line's display address"},
        "3295": {"comment":"Its attribute address"},
        "3299": {"comment":"The third of the screen"},
        "3301": {"comment":"+ $5800"},
        "3304": {"comment":"DE = line 23's attributes"},
        "3307": {"comment":"A = line 23's colour"},
        "3308": {"comment":"C = the upper line's colour"},
        "3309": {"comment":"32 cells"},
        "3311": {"comment":"HL = line 23, DE = the upper line"},
        "3312": {"synopsis":"Swaps 32 attributes: the upper line gets line 23's first colour, line 23 the other.","comment":"The upper line"},
        "3313": {"comment":"Line 23"},
        "3318": {"comment":"B, C: the upper screen's last line"},
        "3320": {"synopsis":"The scroll message for PRINT_MESSAGE: entry 0 empty ($80), entry 1 \"scroll?\"."},
        "3328": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0C (report D, \"BREAK - CONT repeats\")."},
        "3330": {"synopsis":"The lower screen: a line B below 2 stops with report 5; when B + DF_SZ - $19 is not negative\nthe line fits. Otherwise the lower screen grows by that many lines (OUT_SCR_GROW), with the\ntemporary colours of the lower screen for the scroll, and the upper print position moved up\nwhen it is overrun.\nObserved: four lines through stream 1 made DF_SZ 5.","comment":"Line 0 or 1?"},
        "3332": {"comment":"Report 5"},
        "3334": {"comment":"+ DF_SZ"},
        "3337": {"comment":"Less $19"},
        "3339": {"comment":"Not negative: it fits"},
        "3340": {"comment":"A = the lines more"},
        "3342": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "3343": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "3344": {"comment":"ATTR_T and MASK_T kept"},
        "3348": {"comment":"P_FLAG kept"},
        "3352": {"comment":"The lower screen's colours"},
        "3355": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "3356": {"synopsis":"One more line: DF_SZ + 1. When it reaches the upper print line, that moves up (S_POSN) and\nthe whole screen scrolls; otherwise only the lower screen's lines move up.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "3357": {"comment":"HL = DF_SZ"},
        "3360": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "3362": {"comment":"One more"},
        "3364": {"comment":"HL = S_POSN's line"},
        "3367": {"comment":"Reached the upper print line?"},
        "3368": {"comment":"No: only the lower lines move"},
        "3370": {"comment":"The upper print line one up"},
        "3371": {"comment":"B = $18: the whole screen"},
        "3373": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the bottom B lines (SCROLL_LINES_B), and again for each line more.","comment":"The bottom B lines up"},
        "3376": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "3377": {"comment":"One less"},
        "3378": {"comment":"More"},
        "3380": {"comment":"P_FLAG back"},
        "3384": {"comment":"ATTR_T and MASK_T back"},
        "3388": {"comment":"BC = S_POSN"},
        "3392": {"comment":"The upper screen for the moment"},
        "3396": {"comment":"Its print position set again"},
        "3399": {"comment":"The lower screen again"},
        "3403": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "3405": {"synopsis":"Sets the temporary colours from the permanent ones: ATTR_T and MASK_T from ATTR_P and\nMASK_P, and P_FLAG's temporary bits (0, 2, 4, 6) from its permanent bits (1, 3, 5, 7).\nFor the lower screen (TV_FLAG bit 0): ATTR_T = BORDCR, MASK_T = 0, the temporary bits\ncleared.\nChanges: AF, HL; ATTR_T, MASK_T, P_FLAG.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "3406": {"comment":"HL = ATTR_P and MASK_P"},
        "3409": {"comment":"The lower screen?"},
        "3413": {"comment":"No"},
        "3415": {"comment":"MASK_T = 0"},
        "3416": {"comment":"ATTR_T = BORDCR"},
        "3419": {"synopsis":"ATTR_T and MASK_T = HL."},
        "3422": {"comment":"HL = P_FLAG"},
        "3425": {"comment":"The lower screen: A = 0"},
        "3427": {"comment":"The upper: the permanent bits"},
        "3428": {"comment":"Down onto the temporary bits"},
        "3429": {"synopsis":"Copies A's bits 0, 2, 4, 6 into P_FLAG, keeping its others."},
        "3430": {"comment":"Bits 0, 2, 4, 6 from A, the others from P_FLAG"},
        "3433": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "3435": {"synopsis":"Clears the whole screen (CLEAR_SCREEN), then the lower screen: its DF_SZ lines in the lower\nscreen's colours, all but the bottom two of them given ATTR_P, and DF_SZ = 2. Channel K's\nroutines and the lower print position are reset (RESET_CHAN_K).","comment":"The whole screen"},
        "3438": {"synopsis":"Clears the lower screen and shrinks it back to two lines, as CLS_CMD does after\nCLEAR_SCREEN.","comment":"HL = TV_FLAG"},
        "3441": {"comment":"Bit 5 clear: no clearing pending"},
        "3443": {"comment":"Bit 0 set: the lower screen"},
        "3445": {"comment":"Its colours"},
        "3448": {"comment":"B = DF_SZ"},
        "3451": {"comment":"Its lines cleared"},
        "3454": {"comment":"Line 22's attributes: the fill goes down from below here"},
        "3457": {"comment":"A = ATTR_P"},
        "3460": {"comment":"B - 2 lines in all (DJNZ counts one more)"},
        "3463": {"synopsis":"One attribute line: C = 32 bytes."},
        "3465": {"synopsis":"ATTR_P into the next byte down."},
        "3470": {"synopsis":"The next line, while any are left."},
        "3472": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "3476": {"synopsis":"Opens channel K (stream -3), puts its output and input routines back to $09F4 and $10A8, and\nsets the lower screen's print position to its top line, left column (BC = $1721,\nSET_PRINT_POS).","comment":"Stream -3: channel K"},
        "3481": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL"},
        "3484": {"comment":"Its output routine, SCREEN_OUTPUT"},
        "3487": {"comment":"Carry clear: two words to store"},
        "3488": {"synopsis":"Stores DE as the next routine address; the CCF lets the loop run twice."},
        "3492": {"comment":"Then its input routine"},
        "3495": {"comment":"Twice"},
        "3498": {"comment":"The lower screen's top line, left column"},
        "3503": {"synopsis":"Clears the whole screen:\n1. COORDS ($5C7D) = 0, FLAGS2 bit 0 cleared, channel K reset (RESET_CHAN_K).\n2. Channel S (stream -2) opened with its temporary colours; all 24 lines cleared\n   (CLS_LINES).\n3. S's output routine put back to $09F4, SCR_CT = 1, and the upper print position set to the\n   top left (BC = $1821).","comment":"HL = 0"},
        "3506": {"comment":"COORDS = 0"},
        "3509": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 0 clear: the screen is clean"},
        "3513": {"comment":"Channel K reset"},
        "3516": {"comment":"Stream -2: channel S"},
        "3521": {"comment":"Its colours"},
        "3524": {"comment":"All 24 lines"},
        "3526": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "3529": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL"},
        "3532": {"comment":"Its output routine, SCREEN_OUTPUT"},
        "3538": {"comment":"SCR_CT = 1"},
        "3542": {"comment":"The top line, left column"},
        "3545": {"synopsis":"Sets the print position of the current channel: B = the line counting up from the bottom\n($18 the top line), C = the column counting down from the right ($21 the left column).\nFor the printer (FLAGS bit 1) only the column counts, in the buffer at $5B00. For the lower\nscreen (TV_FLAG bit 0) the line counts in the lower screen (B + DF_SZ - $18). Stores through\nSTORE_POS.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the printer buffer"},
        "3548": {"comment":"The printer?"},
        "3552": {"comment":"Then only the column"},
        "3554": {"comment":"A = the line"},
        "3555": {"comment":"The lower screen?"},
        "3561": {"comment":"Its line counts from the lower screen's top"},
        "3566": {"synopsis":"HL = the line's address (LINE_SCREEN_ADDR), B and C kept."},
        "3567": {"comment":"B = the line"},
        "3568": {"comment":"HL = its address"},
        "3572": {"synopsis":"HL + $21 - C: the column.","comment":"$21 - C: the column"},
        "3578": {"comment":"HL + the column"},
        "3579": {"comment":"Stored (STORE_POS)"},
        "3582": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the whole screen up a line: lines 1-23 move into 0-22 (SCROLL_LINES_B with B = $17),\nand line 23 is cleared.","comment":"23 lines"},
        "3584": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the bottom B lines up by one line: each of the 8 pixel rows, third by third\n(SCROLL_THIRD), then the attributes; the bottom line is then cleared (CLS_LINES with B = 1,\nwhich follows).","comment":"HL = the top line's address"},
        "3587": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "3589": {"synopsis":"One pixel row of every line in the area.","comment":"The count and address kept"},
        "3591": {"comment":"A = the lines left"},
        "3592": {"comment":"A third's top line?"},
        "3595": {"comment":"No"},
        "3597": {"synopsis":"The row of a third's top line goes to the third above's bottom line ($F8E0 = -$0720).","comment":"DE = the row"},
        "3598": {"comment":"Less $0720"},
        "3601": {"comment":"DE = the third above's bottom line"},
        "3603": {"comment":"32 bytes"},
        "3606": {"comment":"One line less"},
        "3607": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "3609": {"synopsis":"The rest of the third: rows move up 32 bytes (LDIR).","comment":"DE = the next row"},
        "3610": {"comment":"Less 32: the line above"},
        "3615": {"comment":"B = the lines left"},
        "3616": {"comment":"The lines left in this third"},
        "3618": {"comment":"Times 32"},
        "3621": {"comment":"C = the bytes"},
        "3625": {"comment":"Moved up"},
        "3627": {"comment":"HL + $0700: the next third's top line"},
        "3630": {"comment":"More thirds?"},
        "3634": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "3635": {"comment":"The next pixel row"},
        "3636": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "3637": {"comment":"One row less"},
        "3638": {"comment":"All 8"},
        "3640": {"comment":"The attributes' addresses and count"},
        "3646": {"comment":"DE = a line above"},
        "3648": {"comment":"Moved up"},
        "3650": {"comment":"Then the bottom line cleared"},
        "3652": {"synopsis":"Clears the bottom B lines of the screen: their pixels to 0 and their attributes to ATTR_P,\nor to BORDCR for the lower screen (TV_FLAG bit 0).\nExit: C = $21.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "3653": {"comment":"HL = the top line's address"},
        "3656": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "3658": {"synopsis":"One pixel row of every line: 8 rounds, H one up each.","comment":"The count and address kept"},
        "3660": {"comment":"A = the lines"},
        "3661": {"synopsis":"The part of the row in one third of the screen (LDIR).","comment":"The lines in this third"},
        "3663": {"comment":"Times 32"},
        "3666": {"comment":"C = the bytes"},
        "3670": {"comment":"Less the first"},
        "3671": {"comment":"DE = HL"},
        "3673": {"comment":"The first byte 0"},
        "3675": {"comment":"DE = the next"},
        "3676": {"comment":"The rest copied from it"},
        "3678": {"comment":"HL + $0701: the next third"},
        "3682": {"comment":"The lines left"},
        "3683": {"comment":"In the next thirds"},
        "3685": {"comment":"B = them"},
        "3686": {"comment":"More thirds"},
        "3688": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "3689": {"comment":"The next pixel row"},
        "3690": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "3691": {"comment":"One row less"},
        "3692": {"comment":"All 8"},
        "3694": {"comment":"DE = the attributes, BC = their count"},
        "3697": {"comment":"HL = DE"},
        "3699": {"comment":"DE one on"},
        "3700": {"comment":"A = ATTR_P"},
        "3703": {"comment":"The lower screen?"},
        "3709": {"comment":"Then A = BORDCR"},
        "3712": {"synopsis":"The attributes: A into the first, then LDIR over the rest."},
        "3713": {"comment":"Less the first"},
        "3714": {"comment":"The rest"},
        "3716": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "3717": {"comment":"C = $21"},
        "3720": {"synopsis":"For CLS_LINES, with HL one third (2K) past the display row it started at and B lines.\nExit: DE = that row's attribute address, BC = B x 32 (the attribute bytes to fill), HL = the\nold DE.","comment":"The attribute area's high byte from H"},
        "3724": {"comment":"Less 1: the third before"},
        "3725": {"comment":"+ $5000"},
        "3728": {"comment":"DE = the attribute address, HL = the old DE"},
        "3729": {"comment":"HL = the line count in H, C in L"},
        "3731": {"comment":"Times 32 by the shifts: B x 32 in HL, C's part dropped"},
        "3736": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "3739": {"synopsis":"HL = the display address of the first pixel row of line 24 - B (B counting up from the\nbottom, as SET_PRINT_POS takes it).\nExit: D = that line number.\nChanges: AF, D, HL.","comment":"A = 24 - B: the line"},
        "3742": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "3743": {"comment":"Its low three bits"},
        "3746": {"comment":"Times 32"},
        "3748": {"comment":"L = the line's offset in its third"},
        "3749": {"comment":"A = the line"},
        "3750": {"comment":"Its third"},
        "3752": {"comment":"+ $4000"},
        "3754": {"comment":"H = it"},
        "3756": {"synopsis":"COPY: the screen's 176 pixel rows go to the printer one by one (PRINTER_ROW), with\ninterrupts off; then the motor stops and the printer buffer is emptied (PRINTER_OFF).\nObserved: with no printer attached (port $FB reads $FF) COPY ended at once with 0 OK.","comment":"No interrupts while printing"},
        "3757": {"comment":"176 pixel rows"},
        "3759": {"comment":"HL = the screen"},
        "3762": {"synopsis":"One pixel row (PRINTER_ROW).","comment":"The address kept"},
        "3763": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "3764": {"comment":"One row printed"},
        "3767": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "3768": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "3769": {"comment":"The next pixel row down"},
        "3770": {"comment":"A character line's last pixel row?"},
        "3773": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "3775": {"comment":"The next character line"},
        "3779": {"comment":"Carry when no third was crossed"},
        "3780": {"comment":"A = $FF then"},
        "3781": {"comment":"$F8: H back 8 rows"},
        "3785": {"synopsis":"The next row's address in the screen's layout: H + 1 within a character line; at its end L +\n32, H back by 8 unless a third is crossed.","comment":"All 176"},
        "3787": {"comment":"The motor off"},
        "3789": {"synopsis":"Prints the printer buffer: its eight rows at $5B00 go out through $0EF4 with interrupts off,\nthen 4 is written to port $FB and it goes on into CLEAR_PRBUFF.","comment":"No interrupts while printing"},
        "3790": {"comment":"HL = the printer buffer"},
        "3793": {"comment":"8 rows"},
        "3795": {"synopsis":"One of the buffer's 8 rows.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "3796": {"comment":"One row printed"},
        "3799": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "3800": {"comment":"All 8"},
        "3802": {"synopsis":"4 to port $FB (the ZX Printer's motor off), interrupts on, then CLEAR_PRBUFF.","comment":"4: the motor off"},
        "3806": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "3807": {"synopsis":"Empties the printer buffer at $5B00 (256 bytes) and PR_CC's low byte, clears FLAGS2 bit 1,\nand sets the left column (C = $21) through SET_PRINT_POS.\nAt start-up FLAGS bit 1 is set, so this sets the printer's position.","comment":"HL = the printer buffer"},
        "3810": {"comment":"PR_CC's low byte 0"},
        "3813": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "3814": {"comment":"B = 0: 256 bytes"},
        "3815": {"synopsis":"Zeroes the 256 bytes.","comment":"Zeroed"},
        "3819": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 1: the buffer is empty"},
        "3823": {"comment":"The left column"},
        "3825": {"comment":"SET_PRINT_POS"},
        "3828": {"synopsis":"Sends one pixel row of 32 bytes at HL to the printer through port $FB: the motor slows (bit\n1) for the last two rows (B below 3); each bit waits for the printer (bit 0 of the port\nread) and goes out in bit 7. BREAK stops the motor and is report D. When the port read has\nbit 6 set (no printer) it returns at once.\nExit: HL past the row.","comment":"A = the rows left"},
        "3829": {"comment":"Fewer than 3?"},
        "3831": {"comment":"$FF then"},
        "3832": {"comment":"Bit 1: the slow motor"},
        "3834": {"comment":"The motor on"},
        "3836": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "3837": {"synopsis":"BREAK (BREAK_KEY): motor off, buffer emptied, report D.","comment":"BREAK?"},
        "3840": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "3842": {"comment":"The motor off"},
        "3846": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "3847": {"comment":"The buffer emptied"},
        "3850": {"comment":"Report D"},
        "3852": {"synopsis":"The printer's state: bit 6 set (none attached) returns; bit 7 clear waits.","comment":"The printer's state"},
        "3854": {"comment":"Bit 6 into the sign, bit 7 into the carry"},
        "3855": {"comment":"No printer: return"},
        "3856": {"comment":"Not ready: wait"},
        "3858": {"comment":"32 bytes"},
        "3860": {"synopsis":"The row's next byte.","comment":"E = the next byte"},
        "3862": {"comment":"8 bits"},
        "3864": {"synopsis":"Its next bit into bit 7 of D.","comment":"D's bit 7 out"},
        "3866": {"comment":"E's next bit into the carry"},
        "3868": {"comment":"Into D's bit 7"},
        "3870": {"synopsis":"Waits for bit 0 of the port, then sends D.","comment":"The port"},
        "3872": {"comment":"Bit 0 into the carry"},
        "3873": {"comment":"Not ready: wait"},
        "3875": {"comment":"A = D"},
        "3876": {"comment":"The bit sent"},
        "3878": {"comment":"All 8"},
        "3880": {"comment":"One byte less"},
        "3881": {"comment":"All 32"},
        "3884": {"synopsis":"The line editor, for the edit line or INPUT's line (FLAGX bit 5): edits the line the cursor\n(K_CUR) is in until ENTER, one key per pass of ED_LOOP:\n1. Waits for a key (WAIT_KEY: channel K's KEY_INPUT has already handled CAPS LOCK, E and G\n   mode, and turned colour keys into a code and its operand) and clicks (TONE_OUT, DE =\n   PIP).\n2. Codes $18 and up and below $07 are inserted before the cursor (INSERT_CHAR); $10-$17 with\n   their operands (ED_CONTROL); $07-$0F are editing keys, run through EDIT_KEY_TABLE.\n3. Each key returns to ED_LOOP, except ENTER (KEY_ENTER), which returns to the caller.\n   ERR_SP points at ED_ERROR meanwhile, the old ERR_SP kept above it, so an error while\n   editing gives a rasp and editing goes on.\nObserved: PRINT 123, LEFT, DELETE, RIGHT left \"PRINT 13\" with the cursor at the end; DELETE\nat the start and RIGHT at the end did nothing.","comment":"Keep the old ERR_SP"},
        "3888": {"comment":"ED_ERROR is where an error returns","synopsis":"Sets up the error return again (ED_ERROR comes back here) and goes into ED_LOOP."},
        "3891": {"comment":"Pushed"},
        "3892": {"comment":"ERR_SP = its slot"},
        "3896": {"synopsis":"One key: WAIT_KEY, the click, then the key's action. ED_LOOP's own address is pushed as the\naction's return, so every action but ENTER comes back here.","comment":"A key"},
        "3899": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3900": {"comment":"The click: DE = PIP..."},
        "3902": {"comment":"E = PIP"},
        "3905": {"comment":"... HL = $00C8"},
        "3908": {"comment":"The click"},
        "3911": {"comment":"The key back"},
        "3912": {"comment":"Every action returns to ED_LOOP"},
        "3916": {"comment":"$18 and up: a character or a token"},
        "3920": {"comment":"$00-$06: inserted as they are"},
        "3924": {"comment":"$07-$0F: an editing key"},
        "3928": {"comment":"BC = 2 bytes"},
        "3931": {"comment":"D = the code"},
        "3932": {"comment":"$10-$15 take one operand, $16-$17 two"},
        "3936": {"comment":"BC = 3"},
        "3937": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 7 clear: AT and TAB end the editing"},
        "3944": {"comment":"The first operand"},
        "3947": {"comment":"E = it"},
        "3948": {"synopsis":"Inserts a control code ($10-$17) with its operand bytes, read by WAIT_KEY: 2 bytes in all,\nor 3 for $16-$17. MODE bit 0 is cleared.\nObserved: E then 2 inserted $11 $02 (PAPER 2), E then CAPS SHIFT+3 inserted $10 $03 (INK 3),\nE then 8 inserted $13 $00.","comment":"The (last) operand"},
        "3951": {"comment":"D, E kept"},
        "3952": {"comment":"HL = K_CUR"},
        "3955": {"comment":"MODE bit 0 clear: E mode ends"},
        "3959": {"comment":"Room for BC bytes"},
        "3962": {"comment":"B = the code, C = the first operand"},
        "3963": {"comment":"HL to the room"},
        "3964": {"comment":"The code, then the operand(s)"},
        "3967": {"comment":"The last operand into the last byte"},
        "3969": {"synopsis":"Inserts A before the cursor: one byte of room at K_CUR (MAKE_ROOM_ONE), A in it, the cursor\nafter it. MODE bit 0 is cleared, so E mode lasts one key.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL; K_CUR.","comment":"MODE bit 0 clear: E mode ends"},
        "3973": {"comment":"HL = K_CUR"},
        "3976": {"comment":"One byte of room"},
        "3979": {"synopsis":"A into the last byte of the room (DE), and K_CUR = the byte after it.","comment":"Stored"},
        "3980": {"comment":"DE = the byte after it"},
        "3981": {"comment":"K_CUR = it"},
        "3986": {"synopsis":"Runs editing key A ($07-$0F): jumps to EDIT_KEY_TABLE's entry for it, with HL = K_CUR.","comment":"DE = the code"},
        "3989": {"comment":"$0F99 + A: the code's offset byte"},
        "3993": {"comment":"E = the offset"},
        "3994": {"comment":"HL = the action"},
        "3995": {"comment":"For the RET"},
        "3996": {"comment":"HL = K_CUR"},
        "3999": {"comment":"Into the action"},
        "4000": {"synopsis":"Editing-key table: 9 offsets for codes $07-$0F, read at $0F99 + code; each counts from its\nown byte. $07 KEY_EDIT, $08 KEY_LEFT, $09 KEY_RIGHT, $0A KEY_DOWN, $0B KEY_UP, $0C\nKEY_DELETE, $0D KEY_ENTER, $0E KEY_EXTEND, $0F KEY_GRAPHICS."},
        "4009": {"synopsis":"EDIT ($07): copies the current line (E_PPC) into the edit line: the edit line is emptied\n(CLEAR_INPUT), and the line printed into it through channel R (stream -1) by PRINT_LINE,\nE_PPC one lower meanwhile so the line gets no '>'. The cursor goes after the line number\n(E_LINE + 4).\nWith INPUT's line, or no program, it only empties the line. Stops with report 4 when the\nline and 10 bytes more do not fit.\nObserved: with lines 10 and 20 and E_PPC = 10, the edit line became \"  10\" and PRINT 1, the\ncursor after the number.","comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "4012": {"comment":"INPUT?"},
        "4016": {"comment":"Then only empty the line"},
        "4019": {"comment":"HL = the line, or the one after (FIND_LINE)"},
        "4022": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "4025": {"comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "4027": {"comment":"No line: just empty the edit line"},
        "4030": {"comment":"The line kept"},
        "4031": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "4035": {"comment":"Its length + 10 must fit"},
        "4039": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "4041": {"comment":"Room?"},
        "4044": {"comment":"The edit line emptied"},
        "4047": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL"},
        "4050": {"comment":"The channel kept, HL = the line"},
        "4051": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4052": {"comment":"Stream -1: channel R prints into the edit line"},
        "4057": {"comment":"HL = the line"},
        "4058": {"comment":"HL to the byte before it"},
        "4059": {"comment":"E_PPC one lower: no '>' marker"},
        "4062": {"comment":"Printed into the edit line"},
        "4065": {"comment":"E_PPC back"},
        "4068": {"comment":"The cursor after the 4-character number"},
        "4075": {"comment":"K_CUR = there"},
        "4078": {"comment":"HL = the old channel"},
        "4079": {"comment":"The old channel back"},
        "4083": {"synopsis":"Cursor down ($0A): the line after the current one becomes the current line (E_PPC_NEXT), and\nthe listing is shown again (ED_RELIST). With INPUT's line: KEY_DOWN_INPUT.\nObserved: lines 10 and 20, UP then DOWN moved E_PPC from 20 to 10 and back to 20.","comment":"INPUT?"},
        "4087": {"comment":"Then KEY_DOWN_INPUT"},
        "4089": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "4092": {"comment":"The next line becomes it"},
        "4095": {"comment":"Listed again"},
        "4097": {"synopsis":"Cursor down while INPUT runs: ERR_NR = $10 (report H, \"STOP in INPUT\") and the editing ends\n(KEY_ENTER).","comment":"ERR_NR = $10: report H"},
        "4101": {"comment":"Ended"},
        "4103": {"synopsis":"Cursor left ($08): K_CUR goes back over the item before it (ED_PREV_ITEM); nothing at the\nstart of the line.","comment":"HL = the item before"},
        "4106": {"comment":"K_CUR = it"},
        "4108": {"synopsis":"Cursor right ($09): K_CUR one on; nothing at the line's $0D.","comment":"The character at the cursor"},
        "4109": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "4111": {"comment":"Then nothing"},
        "4112": {"comment":"One on"},
        "4113": {"synopsis":"K_CUR = HL."},
        "4117": {"synopsis":"DELETE ($0C): removes the byte before the cursor (ED_PREV_ITEM, then RECLAIM with BC = 1);\nnothing at the start of the line.","comment":"HL = the byte before"},
        "4120": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "4123": {"comment":"Removed"},
        "4126": {"synopsis":"AT or TAB ($16, $17) while FLAGX bit 7 is clear: their two operand keys are read and\ndropped, and the editing ends as for ENTER.","comment":"The first operand dropped"},
        "4129": {"comment":"The second dropped"},
        "4132": {"synopsis":"ENTER ($0D): leaves the editor. ED_LOOP's return and ED_ERROR's are dropped, and ERR_SP is\nput back; with no error (ERR_NR bit 7 set) it returns to EDITOR's caller.\nObserved: ENTER after EDIT stored line 10 again and the main loop went on.","comment":"ED_LOOP's return dropped"},
        "4133": {"comment":"ED_ERROR's dropped"},
        "4134": {"synopsis":"The rest of leaving: ERR_SP = the old value. After an error the stack goes back to it and\nits slot's RET takes the error on; otherwise a plain return.","comment":"HL = the old ERR_SP"},
        "4135": {"comment":"Back"},
        "4138": {"comment":"No error?"},
        "4143": {"comment":"An error: the stack back to its slot"},
        "4145": {"synopsis":"Finds the item before the cursor: HL = its address, walking from the line's start\n(INPUT_START) so that a control code's operands count with it ($10-$15 one byte, $16-$17\ntwo).\nAt the start of the line it drops its caller's return address, so the editing action is\nskipped and ED_LOOP goes on.","comment":"Carry: INPUT_START returns at once"},
        "4146": {"comment":"DE = the line's start, HL = K_CUR"},
        "4149": {"comment":"Carry when the cursor is at the start"},
        "4151": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4152": {"comment":"HL = K_CUR + 1"},
        "4153": {"comment":"Cursor at the start: back to ED_LOOP"},
        "4155": {"comment":"The return back"},
        "4156": {"comment":"BC = K_CUR + 1"},
        "4158": {"synopsis":"One item: HL = the byte after it, past any operands.","comment":"HL = the item"},
        "4160": {"comment":"The byte after it"},
        "4161": {"comment":"The item's code"},
        "4162": {"comment":"Its top bits"},
        "4164": {"comment":"A control code $10-$1F?"},
        "4168": {"comment":"Past its first operand"},
        "4169": {"comment":"The code again"},
        "4170": {"comment":"$16 or $17: a second operand"},
        "4172": {"comment":"0 for $16 and $17"},
        "4174": {"comment":"Not: one operand"},
        "4176": {"comment":"Past the second"},
        "4177": {"synopsis":"Stops when the next item reaches the cursor (HL = BC = K_CUR + 1)."},
        "4178": {"comment":"The next item reached the cursor?"},
        "4180": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4181": {"comment":"DE = the next item, HL = this one"},
        "4182": {"comment":"Not yet: on"},
        "4185": {"synopsis":"Cursor up ($0B): the line before the current one becomes the current line (E_PPC), and the\nlisting is shown again; nothing while INPUT runs.","comment":"INPUT?"},
        "4189": {"comment":"Then nothing"},
        "4190": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "4193": {"comment":"DE = the line before it"},
        "4196": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "4197": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "4200": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC's high byte"},
        "4203": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "4206": {"synopsis":"Lists the program again (AUTO_LIST) and makes stream 0 current again.","comment":"The listing"},
        "4209": {"comment":"Stream 0"},
        "4214": {"synopsis":"Code $0E: with FLAGX bit 7 clear it ends the editing as ENTER does (KEY_ENTER);\nwith it set it is inserted (INSERT_CHAR).","comment":"FLAGX bit 7 clear?"},
        "4218": {"comment":"Then the editing ends"},
        "4220": {"synopsis":"Code $0F: inserted (INSERT_CHAR). KEY_INPUT turns the GRAPHICS key into a mode change first,\nso the editor gets it only from other input.","comment":"Inserted"},
        "4223": {"synopsis":"Where an error while editing returns. Not from channel K (FLAGS2 bit 4 clear): the editor is\nleft with the error (ED_LEAVE). Otherwise ERR_NR = $FF, a rasp (TONE_OUT, DE = RASP, HL =\n$1A90) and editing goes on (ED_SET_ERR).","comment":"From channel K?"},
        "4227": {"comment":"No: leave with the error"},
        "4229": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no error"},
        "4235": {"comment":"E = RASP"},
        "4238": {"comment":"The rasp's pitch"},
        "4241": {"comment":"The rasp"},
        "4244": {"comment":"On editing"},
        "4247": {"synopsis":"Empties the line being input, keeping its $0D: the bytes INPUT_RANGE gives are removed\n(RECLAIM_DE_HL), K_CUR goes to the $0D, and MODE = 0. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "4248": {"comment":"DE = the line's start, HL = its end"},
        "4251": {"comment":"Less 1: keeping the $0D"},
        "4252": {"comment":"Removed"},
        "4255": {"comment":"K_CUR = the $0D"},
        "4258": {"comment":"MODE = 0"},
        "4262": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4264": {"synopsis":"Channel K's input routine, called through CHAN_INPUT: returns a key from LAST_K when FLAGS\nbit 5 says there is one.\n1. Shows the edit line again first when TV_FLAG bit 3 asks (EDIT_LINE_SHOW); clears the\n   lower screen when TV_FLAG bit 5 is set.\n2. Codes $20 and up, and $07-$0D, come back with carry. CAPS LOCK ($06) toggles FLAGS2 bit\n   3, E ($0E) and G ($0F) toggle MODE 1 and 2; each comes back with Z and no carry (no key).\n3. $00-$05 come back as FLASH, BRIGHT or INVERSE ($12-$14) with 0 or 1, and $10-$1F as PAPER\n   ($11, from E mode digits) or INK ($10, with CAPS SHIFT) with 0-7: the code now, the\n   operand from K_DATA on the next call (KI_PARAM).\nExit: carry and A = the key; Z, no carry for none.\nObserved: CAPS LOCK twice set and cleared FLAGS2 bit 3; E and GRAPHICS gave MODE 1 and 2,\npressed again 0.","comment":"Show the edit line again?"},
        "4268": {"comment":"EDIT_LINE_SHOW"},
        "4271": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "4276": {"comment":"No key waiting?"},
        "4277": {"comment":"A = LAST_K"},
        "4280": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "4284": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4285": {"comment":"The lower screen to be cleared?"},
        "4289": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "4292": {"comment":"The key back"},
        "4293": {"comment":"$20 and up: a key"},
        "4297": {"comment":"$10-$1F: PAPER or INK"},
        "4301": {"comment":"$06-$0F"},
        "4305": {"comment":"$00-$05: FLASH, BRIGHT, INVERSE with bit 0 as the operand"},
        "4306": {"comment":"C = bit 0: the operand"},
        "4309": {"comment":"A = the key"},
        "4310": {"comment":"0-1 FLASH, 2-3 BRIGHT, 4-5 INVERSE"},
        "4311": {"comment":"+ $12: the code $12-$14"},
        "4313": {"comment":"With its operand"},
        "4315": {"synopsis":"$06: CAPS LOCK, FLAGS2 bit 3 toggled; $07-$0F: KI_MODE.","comment":"$07-$0F"},
        "4317": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS2"},
        "4320": {"comment":"Bit 3: CAPS LOCK"},
        "4322": {"comment":"Toggled"},
        "4324": {"comment":"The edit line again"},
        "4326": {"synopsis":"$07-$0D come back as keys; $0E and $0F set MODE 1 or 2, or 0 when it was that already."},
        "4328": {"comment":"$07-$0D: a key"},
        "4329": {"comment":"$0E 1 (E), $0F 2 (G)"},
        "4331": {"comment":"HL = MODE"},
        "4334": {"comment":"The same mode?"},
        "4335": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "4338": {"comment":"Then MODE 0"},
        "4340": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG bit 3 set (the mode changed: show the edit line again), and Z, no carry: no key.","comment":"The edit line again"},
        "4344": {"comment":"Z, no carry: no key"},
        "4346": {"synopsis":"$10-$1F: C = the colour (bits 0-2), A = INK ($10) for $18-$1F, PAPER ($11) for $10-$17.","comment":"B = the code"},
        "4347": {"comment":"The colour"},
        "4349": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "4350": {"comment":"INK"},
        "4352": {"comment":"$18-$1F?"},
        "4356": {"comment":"$10-$17: PAPER"},
        "4357": {"synopsis":"K_DATA = C, the operand, and channel K's input routine becomes KI_NEXT_PARAM for the next\ncall.","comment":"K_DATA = the operand"},
        "4360": {"comment":"Then KI_NEXT_PARAM"},
        "4365": {"synopsis":"The second call after a control code: A = K_DATA, and the input routine back to KEY_INPUT.","comment":"A = K_DATA"},
        "4368": {"comment":"Then KEY_INPUT again"},
        "4371": {"synopsis":"Stores DE as channel K's input routine (the word at CHANS + 2).","comment":"HL = CHANS"},
        "4374": {"comment":"HL to channel K's input word"},
        "4376": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "4379": {"synopsis":"Carry: a key in A."},
        "4381": {"synopsis":"Shows the edit line (or INPUT's line) in the lower screen, from the lower print position:\n1. COLOURS_TO_TEMP; TV_FLAG bits 3 and 5 cleared; ERR_SP pointed at ELS_FULL for the time.\n2. The line's text (PRINT_TEXT, from INPUT_START), then the cursor when it is at the very\n   end (PRINT_CURSOR).\n3. Spaces up to ECHO_E, the old end, so a shorter line leaves nothing behind (ELS_PAD_LOOP).\n4. The print position put back to where the line starts, ECHO_E = the new end, and X_PTR's\n   high byte cleared (the '?' marker shows once).\nObserved: a 41-character line grew the lower screen to 3 lines; after 30 DELETEs the line's\nold second row was blank.","comment":"The lower screen's colours"},
        "4384": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3 clear"},
        "4388": {"comment":"And bit 5"},
        "4392": {"comment":"S_POSNL kept, the line's start"},
        "4396": {"comment":"ERR_SP kept"},
        "4400": {"comment":"ELS_FULL as the error return"},
        "4404": {"comment":"ERR_SP = its slot"},
        "4408": {"comment":"Keep ECHO_E, the old end"},
        "4412": {"comment":"Carry: INPUT_START returns at once"},
        "4413": {"comment":"DE = the line's start"},
        "4416": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "4417": {"comment":"The text printed"},
        "4420": {"comment":"DE = the end"},
        "4421": {"comment":"The cursor if it is at the end"},
        "4424": {"comment":"Keep S_POSNL, the new end"},
        "4427": {"comment":"Kept, HL = the old ECHO_E"},
        "4428": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "4429": {"comment":"The colours again"},
        "4432": {"synopsis":"Pads with spaces until the print position reaches the old end (D, E: ECHO_E's line and\ncolumn).","comment":"S_POSNL's line"},
        "4435": {"comment":"Less the old end's"},
        "4436": {"comment":"Past the old end's line?"},
        "4440": {"comment":"The column"},
        "4441": {"comment":"On its line: past its column?"},
        "4446": {"synopsis":"A space (SCREEN_OUTPUT), and again.","comment":"A space"},
        "4448": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "4449": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4455": {"synopsis":"Where an error while showing the line returns (ERR_SP): a rasp (TONE_OUT, DE = RASP, HL =\n$1A90), ERR_NR = $FF, and the end is where printing stopped.","comment":"D = 0"},
        "4457": {"comment":"E = RASP"},
        "4460": {"comment":"The rasp's pitch"},
        "4463": {"comment":"The rasp"},
        "4466": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no error"},
        "4470": {"comment":"DE = S_POSNL: where it stopped"},
        "4476": {"synopsis":"Padding done: DE = the new end.","comment":"DE = the new end"},
        "4477": {"comment":"The old ECHO_E dropped"},
        "4478": {"synopsis":"ERR_SP back, the print position back to the line's start (SET_PRINT_POS), ECHO_E = DE.","comment":"HL = the old ERR_SP"},
        "4479": {"comment":"Back"},
        "4482": {"comment":"BC = the line's start"},
        "4483": {"comment":"The end kept"},
        "4484": {"comment":"The print position back to the start"},
        "4487": {"comment":"HL = the end"},
        "4488": {"comment":"ECHO_E = it"},
        "4491": {"comment":"X_PTR's high byte 0: no error marker"},
        "4496": {"synopsis":"The line being input: DE = E_LINE and HL = WORKSP - 1 for the edit line; when FLAGX bit 5 is\nset, DE = WORKSP and HL = STKBOT (INPUT's line in the workspace). Carry clear.","comment":"HL = WORKSP"},
        "4499": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "4500": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "4501": {"synopsis":"INPUT_RANGE's second part: DE = E_LINE, or WORKSP when FLAGX bit 5 is set; with carry set on\nentry it returns there, HL kept (ED_PREV_ITEM uses it).","comment":"DE = E_LINE"},
        "4505": {"comment":"INPUT?"},
        "4509": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "4510": {"comment":"DE = WORKSP"},
        "4514": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "4515": {"comment":"HL = STKBOT"},
        "4519": {"synopsis":"Walks the line at HL up to its $0D, removing each number marker ($0E) and the hidden 5-byte\nnumber after it (RECLAIM, BC = 6). The main loop uses it on the edit line after a syntax\nerror.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "4520": {"comment":"A number marker?"},
        "4522": {"comment":"6 bytes"},
        "4525": {"comment":"Then removed"},
        "4528": {"comment":"The byte now at HL"},
        "4529": {"comment":"On"},
        "4530": {"comment":"The $0D?"},
        "4532": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "4535": {"synopsis":"NEW: starts the machine again from RAM_FILL with A = $FF and DE = RAMTOP, so only RAM below\nRAMTOP is filled and checked. P_RAMT, RASP/PIP and UDG wait in the alternate registers to be\nput back.\nObserved: NEW typed in K mode (A, ENTER) comes here, and a RAMTOP poked to $7FFF survives.","comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "4536": {"comment":"A = $FF: NEW"},
        "4538": {"comment":"DE = RAMTOP"},
        "4542": {"comment":"The alternate set"},
        "4543": {"comment":"BC' = P_RAMT"},
        "4547": {"comment":"DE' = RASP and PIP"},
        "4551": {"comment":"HL' = UDG"},
        "4555": {"synopsis":"Start-up after START (A = 0, DE = $FFFF) and NEW (A = $FF, DE = RAMTOP):\n1. B = A, a white border, I = $3F; the RAM filled (RAM_FILL_LOOP) and checked (RAM_CHECK) up\n   to DE.\n2. A cold start sets P_RAMT to the last good byte, copies the 21 user-defined graphics below\n   it and sets RASP; NEW puts back the values it saved.\n3. RAMTOP, the machine stack, ERR_SP, IM 1 and IY (SET_RAMTOP); then the channels, streams,\n   the memory areas, the colours and the screen; the copyright line is printed and the main\n   loop entered at MAIN_RESET_EDIT.\nObserved: a cold start reaches RAM_TOP_FOUND after 82 frames on the 48K.","comment":"B = A: 0 for START, $FF for NEW"},
        "4556": {"comment":"Border white, MIC and EAR off"},
        "4562": {"comment":"I = $3F (IM 1 takes no vector from it)"},
        "4564": {"comment":"Six NOPs"},
        "4570": {"comment":"HL = the top"},
        "4572": {"synopsis":"Writes $02 from DE down to $4000 (A = $3F: the loop stops when H reaches $3F).","comment":"The fill"},
        "4574": {"comment":"Down"},
        "4575": {"comment":"Until H reaches $3F"},
        "4578": {"synopsis":"Walks up from $4000 checking the fill: each byte is decremented twice and must become 1 and\nthen 0. Stops at the first byte that fails, or when HL passes DE.","comment":"Clear the carry"},
        "4579": {"comment":"Past DE?"},
        "4581": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4582": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "4583": {"comment":"Past DE: all of it is RAM"},
        "4585": {"comment":"0 after one decrement: not RAM"},
        "4588": {"comment":"1 after the second: RAM"},
        "4591": {"synopsis":"HL = the last good byte. The alternate registers' values (NEW's saved P_RAMT, RASP/PIP and\nUDG) are stored; B + 1 picks the path: 0 (NEW) keeps them and goes to SET_RAMTOP, anything\nelse (the cold start) sets them anew.","comment":"HL = the last good byte"},
        "4592": {"comment":"The alternate set"},
        "4593": {"comment":"P_RAMT"},
        "4597": {"comment":"RASP and PIP"},
        "4601": {"comment":"UDG"},
        "4605": {"comment":"$FF (NEW) becomes 0"},
        "4606": {"comment":"NEW: RAMTOP as it was"},
        "4608": {"comment":"Cold start: P_RAMT = the last good byte"},
        "4611": {"comment":"The 21 UDGs: a copy of the letters A to U from the character set ($3E08-$3EAF)"},
        "4614": {"comment":"168 bytes"},
        "4617": {"comment":"DE = the top, HL = the character set"},
        "4618": {"comment":"Copied down"},
        "4620": {"comment":"HL = the byte before the copy"},
        "4622": {"comment":"UDG = the first byte of the copy"},
        "4625": {"comment":"HL = the byte below the UDGs"},
        "4626": {"comment":"BC = $0040"},
        "4629": {"comment":"RASP = $40, PIP = 0"},
        "4633": {"synopsis":"RAMTOP = HL (the byte below the UDGs on a cold start, the old RAMTOP on NEW). CHARS = $3C00\n(the character set at $3D00 less 256). The machine stack goes just below RAMTOP, whose byte\ngets $3E, and ERR_SP two bytes below SP. Then IM 1, IY = $5C3A (ERR_NR, the base the ROM\nreaches system variables from) and interrupts on.","comment":"RAMTOP = HL"},
        "4636": {"comment":"CHARS = $3C00"},
        "4642": {"comment":"HL = RAMTOP"},
        "4645": {"comment":"$3E under the stack"},
        "4647": {"comment":"Below it"},
        "4648": {"comment":"The machine stack"},
        "4649": {"comment":"Two below"},
        "4651": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "4654": {"comment":"Interrupt mode 1"},
        "4656": {"comment":"IY = ERR_NR"},
        "4660": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "4661": {"comment":"CHANS = $5CB6, the byte after the system variables"},
        "4667": {"comment":"Copy CHANNEL_DATA there"},
        "4670": {"comment":"21 bytes"},
        "4673": {"comment":"DE = CHANS, HL = the data"},
        "4674": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "4676": {"comment":"HL = past it"},
        "4677": {"comment":"DATADD = the channel area's $80"},
        "4681": {"comment":"PROG = VARS = the byte after it, which gets $80: no program, no variables"},
        "4690": {"comment":"E_LINE: an empty edit line ($0D, then $80)"},
        "4700": {"comment":"WORKSP = STKBOT = STKEND: no workspace, an empty calculator stack"},
        "4709": {"comment":"$38: white paper, black ink, for ATTR_P, ATTR_T and BORDCR"},
        "4720": {"comment":"REPDEL = $23, REPPER = $05"},
        "4726": {"comment":"KSTATE ($5C00) and KSTATE + 4 = $FF: both key sets unused"},
        "4732": {"comment":"Copy STREAM_DATA to STRMS"},
        "4738": {"comment":"14 bytes"},
        "4743": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 1 set, so CLEAR_PRBUFF sets the printer's position"},
        "4747": {"comment":"The printer buffer emptied"},
        "4750": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "4754": {"comment":"CLS"},
        "4757": {"comment":"Message 0 of START_MESSAGES: the copyright line"},
        "4761": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4764": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5 set"},
        "4768": {"comment":"On to the main loop"},
        "4770": {"synopsis":"The main loop's re-entry point, taken after a line is stored (STORE_LINE ends at $15AC) and\nafter ENTER on an empty line: DF_SZ = 2, the automatic listing (AUTO_LIST), then\nMAIN_RESET_EDIT.","comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "4774": {"comment":"The automatic listing"},
        "4777": {"synopsis":"Where start-up enters the main loop: an empty edit line and workspace (CLEAR_EDIT_WS), then\nMAIN_ENTRY.","comment":"An empty edit line and workspace"},
        "4780": {"synopsis":"The main loop, one pass per line entered:\n1. Edits a line in the lower screen (EDITOR, stream 0) and checks its syntax\n   (CHECK_LINE). A syntax error goes back to the editor with the line, its hidden\n   numbers stripped.\n2. MAIN_LINE_OK: a numbered line is stored (STORE_LINE), an empty one goes to MAIN_LOOP, a\n   direct command runs (RUN_EDIT_LINE).\n3. REPORT prints how the command ended and comes back here.\nThe code injection and tape load flows wait for the machine to get here.","comment":"Stream 0 (channel K): the editor works in the lower screen"},
        "4782": {"comment":"Made current"},
        "4785": {"comment":"Edit a line; the ERR_SP slot then holds $12B4"},
        "4788": {"comment":"Check its syntax; an error in it returns to $12B7 (the slot holds $12B7)"},
        "4791": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no error?"},
        "4797": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 4 clear: the error did not come from channel K; report it"},
        "4803": {"comment":"A syntax error: strip the hidden numbers, clear ERR_NR and edit the line again (the editor shows the ? marker)"},
        "4815": {"synopsis":"The line's syntax is right. A numbered line (EDIT_LINE_NO gives BC <> 0) is stored\n(STORE_LINE); an empty line goes back to MAIN_LOOP; anything else is a direct command, run\nby RUN_EDIT_LINE, the upper screen cleared first when FLAGS2 bit 0 says it holds a listing.","comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "4818": {"comment":"CH_ADD = it"},
        "4821": {"comment":"BC = its line number, or 0"},
        "4824": {"comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "4826": {"comment":"A line number: store the line"},
        "4829": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "4830": {"comment":"An empty line?"},
        "4834": {"comment":"A listing on the upper screen?"},
        "4838": {"comment":"Then CLS"},
        "4841": {"comment":"Clear the lower screen"},
        "4844": {"comment":"SCR_CT = $19 less the upper print line (S_POSN's high byte)"},
        "4849": {"comment":"SCR_CT"},
        "4852": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 set: run, not check"},
        "4856": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no error"},
        "4860": {"comment":"NSPPC = 1: from the first statement"},
        "4864": {"comment":"Run it; the ERR_SP slot holds this CALL's return, REPORT, so an error ends there too"},
        "4867": {"synopsis":"Ends a direct command, and through the ERR_SP slot every error in one (ERROR_L's RET):\n1. Waits for an interrupt (HALT); prints the printer buffer when it holds anything (FLAGS2\n   bit 1, PRBUFF_OUT).\n2. PRINT_REPORT prints the report on the bottom line as \"<code> <message>,\n   <line>:<statement>\", the code from ERR_NR + 1 (0 when ERR_NR is $FF).\n3. Sets the CONTINUE position (SET_OLDPPC) and goes back to MAIN_ENTRY.\nObserved: PRINT 1 gives \"0 OK, 0:1\", PRINT 1/0 \"6 Number too big, 0:1\", RUN on 10 STOP \"9\nSTOP statement, 10:1\".","comment":"Wait for an interrupt"},
        "4868": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared"},
        "4872": {"comment":"The printer buffer used?"},
        "4876": {"comment":"Then printed"},
        "4879": {"comment":"A = ERR_NR"},
        "4882": {"comment":"+ 1: the report's number"},
        "4883": {"synopsis":"Prints report A (0-$1B); REPORT_G enters here. FLAGX, X_PTR's high byte and DEFADD are\ncleared, stream 0 is pointed at channel K again, the edit line and workspace emptied\n(CLEAR_EDIT_WS) and the lower screen cleared.","comment":"Kept"},
        "4884": {"comment":"HL = 0"},
        "4887": {"comment":"FLAGX = 0"},
        "4890": {"comment":"X_PTR's high byte 0"},
        "4893": {"comment":"DEFADD = 0"},
        "4896": {"comment":"HL = 1"},
        "4899": {"comment":"STRMS' word for stream 0 = 1: channel K"},
        "4902": {"comment":"An empty edit line and workspace"},
        "4905": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 5 clear: not INPUT"},
        "4909": {"comment":"The lower screen cleared"},
        "4912": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5: to be cleared again"},
        "4916": {"comment":"The report's number"},
        "4917": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "4918": {"comment":"10 and above print as letters: + 7 makes 10 \"A\""},
        "4924": {"synopsis":"Prints the report's code character (PRINT_A_DIGIT), a space, then its message.","comment":"Printed"},
        "4927": {"comment":"A space"},
        "4930": {"comment":"A = the number"},
        "4931": {"comment":"The message for the number, from REPORT_MESSAGES"},
        "4937": {"comment":"Message 0"},
        "4938": {"comment":"\", \" (entry 1 of COMMA_MESSAGES)"},
        "4944": {"comment":"The line number, PPC ($FFFE for a direct command prints as 0)"},
        "4951": {"comment":"':'"},
        "4954": {"comment":"The statement number, SUBPPC"},
        "4959": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4962": {"comment":"Empty the edit line, keeping its $0D"},
        "4965": {"comment":"Report 0: no CONTINUE position"},
        "4971": {"comment":"Reports 9 (STOP statement) and L (BREAK into program) continue after the statement"},
        "4975": {"comment":"Report L?"},
        "4979": {"synopsis":"SUBPPC + 1: CONTINUE goes on at the next statement."},
        "4982": {"synopsis":"Copies the CONTINUE position into OLDPPC and OSPPC: NEWPPC and NSPPC when a jump was pending\n(NSPPC bit 7 clear), PPC and SUBPPC otherwise.\nObserved: after 10 STOP, OLDPPC = 10 and OSPPC = 2.","comment":"3 bytes"},
        "4985": {"comment":"DE = OSPPC"},
        "4988": {"comment":"HL = NSPPC"},
        "4991": {"comment":"No jump pending?"},
        "4995": {"comment":"HL = SUBPPC"},
        "4996": {"synopsis":"Copies the three bytes (LDDR)."},
        "4998": {"synopsis":"NSPPC = $FF (no jump pending), FLAGS bit 3 cleared, and back to MAIN_ENTRY for the next\nline."},
        "5009": {"synopsis":"Report messages: in the keyword table's form, for PRINT_MESSAGE. Entry 0 is empty ($80),\nentries 1-28 are the texts of reports 0-9 and A-R, \"OK\" to \"Tape loading error\".\nPRINT_REPORT prints the one for the report's number. START_MESSAGES follows straight on."},
        "5430": {"synopsis":"A table of its own from here (PRINT_REPORT, DE = $1536): entry 0 is the last byte of \"Tape\nloading error\", entry 1 is \", \", whose final space is START_MESSAGES' entry 0."},
        "5432": {"synopsis":"Start-up messages, for PRINT_MESSAGE: entry 0 is a lone space, entry 1 the copyright line\n(the $7F character, then \" 1982 Sinclair Research Ltd\"), which start-up prints as message 0."},
        "5461": {"synopsis":"Stops with report G (No room for line), BC = 0. STORE_LINE puts this address in the ERR_SP\nslot, so an error while it stores a line ends here.\nObserved: the slot holds this address during STORE_LINE.","comment":"Report G's number"},
        "5463": {"comment":"BC = 0"},
        "5466": {"comment":"PRINT_REPORT"},
        "5469": {"synopsis":"Puts a numbered edit line into the program as line BC, in number order:\n1. E_PPC = BC, and REPORT_G goes into the ERR_SP slot, so running out of room ends in report\n   G.\n2. A line with the number already is removed (FIND_LINE, NEXT_ITEM, RECLAIM).\n3. With no text (only the $0D) that is all: the line is deleted.\n4. Otherwise room for the text and 4 bytes is opened before the line found (STORE_NEW), the\n   text copied from the edit line (CH_ADD, just past the number, to its $0D), and the number\n   (high byte first) and the text's length (low byte first, the $0D counted) put in front of\n   it.\nEnds at MAIN_LOOP.\nObserved: 10 PRINT 1 was stored as 00 0A 09 00 F5 31 0E 00 00 01 00 00 0D; 5 PRINT 5 went in\nfront of it; 10 STOP replaced line 10 (00 0A 02 00 E2 0D); 5 alone deleted line 5 and left\nE_PPC = 5.","comment":"E_PPC = the line number"},
        "5473": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD, the text's start"},
        "5476": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "5477": {"comment":"An error while storing: report G"},
        "5480": {"comment":"In the ERR_SP slot"},
        "5481": {"comment":"The text's length: from CH_ADD to the $0D before WORKSP's $80"},
        "5485": {"comment":"HL = the length, the $0D included"},
        "5487": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5488": {"comment":"HL = the number"},
        "5490": {"comment":"HL = the line, or the one after"},
        "5493": {"comment":"Not there: nothing to remove"},
        "5495": {"comment":"BC = the old line's length"},
        "5498": {"comment":"Removed"},
        "5501": {"synopsis":"BC = the text's length; just the $0D means no text (STORE_DONE). Otherwise the room:\nMAKE_ROOM one byte below the line found, so pointers at that line (VARS when it goes last)\nmove up too, with PROG kept and put back."},
        "5502": {"comment":"The length"},
        "5503": {"comment":"Only the $0D?"},
        "5505": {"comment":"Then no text: done"},
        "5507": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "5508": {"comment":"Room for the number and the length too"},
        "5512": {"comment":"HL = the byte below the line found"},
        "5513": {"comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "5517": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5518": {"comment":"The room"},
        "5521": {"comment":"HL = PROG as it was"},
        "5522": {"comment":"PROG back"},
        "5525": {"comment":"BC = the text's length"},
        "5526": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5527": {"comment":"DE = the room's last byte"},
        "5528": {"comment":"From the edit line's $0D down"},
        "5531": {"comment":"HL = the edit line's $0D"},
        "5533": {"comment":"The text copied"},
        "5535": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "5538": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = below the text"},
        "5539": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "5540": {"comment":"The length, low byte first, below the text..."},
        "5544": {"comment":"... and the number, high byte first, below that"},
        "5547": {"synopsis":"Drops REPORT_G's address and goes to MAIN_LOOP, which lists the program.","comment":"REPORT_G's address dropped"},
        "5548": {"comment":"MAIN_LOOP"},
        "5551": {"synopsis":"Channel data, copied to CHANS at start-up: four 5-byte channels (output routine, input\nroutine, letter), then $80 to end the area. K: $09F4 and $10A8; S: $09F4 and CHAN_NO_INPUT;\nR: $0F81 and CHAN_NO_INPUT; P: $09F4 and CHAN_NO_INPUT."},
        "5572": {"synopsis":"The input routine of channels S, R and P: stops with error code $12 (report J), as input\nfrom them is not possible."},
        "5574": {"synopsis":"Stream table, copied to STRMS at start-up: a word per stream from -3 to 3, its channel's\noffset in the channel area plus one: K (1) for -3, 0 and 1; S (6) for -2 and 2; R (11) for\n-1; P (16) for 3."},
        "5588": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key from the current channel: calls its input routine (CHAN_INPUT) until one\ncomes (carry). Sets TV_FLAG bit 3 first unless bit 5 is set. An input routine giving NZ and\nno carry stops with error code 7 (report 8, \"End of file\").\nExit: A = the key.","comment":"Bit 5: the lower screen to be cleared?"},
        "5594": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3: show the edit line"},
        "5598": {"synopsis":"Calls the input routine: carry is a key, Z means none yet.","comment":"The input routine"},
        "5601": {"comment":"Carry: a key"},
        "5602": {"comment":"Z: none yet"},
        "5604": {"comment":"Otherwise report 8"},
        "5606": {"synopsis":"Calls the current channel's input routine, the second word at CURCHL, with the alternate\nregister set in use (CALL_AT_HL).","comment":"The alternate set"},
        "5607": {"comment":"HL' kept"},
        "5608": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL"},
        "5611": {"comment":"HL to the input routine's word"},
        "5615": {"synopsis":"Prints A + \"0\" through the current channel (PRINT_A_CHAN).","comment":"E = \"0\""},
        "5617": {"comment":"+ A"},
        "5618": {"synopsis":"PRINT_A's work: calls the current channel's output routine (the first word at CURCHL) with\nthe alternate register set in use, so the caller's BC, DE and HL are untouched; HL' is kept\ntoo.","comment":"The alternate set"},
        "5619": {"comment":"HL' kept"},
        "5620": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL: the output routine's word"},
        "5623": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine whose address is the word at HL: the output routine from PRINT_A_CHAN, or\nthe input routine when the code at $15E6 comes here with HL two bytes on. Then HL' back and\nthe main register set again.","comment":"DE = the routine"},
        "5626": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "5627": {"comment":"Called"},
        "5630": {"comment":"HL' back"},
        "5631": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "5633": {"synopsis":"Makes stream A (-3 to 15) current: its STRMS word less one is its channel's offset in CHANS,\nand CURCHL = that channel. A stream with a zero word stops with error code $17 (report O).\nThen CHAN_SET_FLAGS: FLAGS2 bit 4 cleared, and the channel's letter picks the flags to set\nthrough CHAN_LETTERS.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL; CURCHL.","comment":"A x 2"},
        "5636": {"comment":"STRMS + 6 + 2A: stream -3 is the first word"},
        "5639": {"comment":"DE = the stream's word"},
        "5642": {"comment":"No channel?"},
        "5646": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $17 (report O): a stream with no channel. Also jumped to from\nelsewhere."},
        "5648": {"synopsis":"CURCHL = CHANS + the offset - 1.","comment":"Less 1"},
        "5649": {"comment":"HL = CHANS"},
        "5652": {"comment":"+ the offset: the channel"},
        "5653": {"synopsis":"STREAM_SELECT's second half, also called on its own with HL = a channel's address already in\nCURCHL: clears FLAGS2 bit 4 and sets the flags its letter asks for: CHAN_K_FLAGS,\nCHAN_S_FLAGS or CHAN_P_FLAGS; another letter (R) sets none.","comment":"CURCHL = it"},
        "5656": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 4 clear: not channel K"},
        "5660": {"comment":"HL to the channel's letter"},
        "5664": {"comment":"C = the letter"},
        "5665": {"comment":"HL = CHAN_LETTERS"},
        "5668": {"comment":"Looked up"},
        "5671": {"comment":"Not there: no flags"},
        "5672": {"comment":"DE = the offset"},
        "5675": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "5676": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: a CALL here calls the routine at HL."},
        "5677": {"synopsis":"Channel letters and offsets for CHAN_SET_FLAGS (TABLE_LOOKUP): K to CHAN_K_FLAGS, S to\nCHAN_S_FLAGS, P to CHAN_P_FLAGS; 0 ends it. Each offset counts from its own byte."},
        "5684": {"synopsis":"Channel K's flags: TV_FLAG bit 0 set (the lower screen), FLAGS bit 5 cleared, FLAGS2 bit 4\nset; then as for S (CHAN_KS_COMMON)."},
        "5698": {"synopsis":"Channel S's flags: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared (the upper screen)."},
        "5702": {"synopsis":"K and S: FLAGS bit 1 cleared (not the printer), then the temporary colours\n(COLOURS_TO_TEMP)."},
        "5709": {"synopsis":"Channel P's flags: FLAGS bit 1 set (the printer)."},
        "5714": {"synopsis":"Makes room for one byte before HL (MAKE_ROOM with BC = 1).","comment":"One byte"},
        "5717": {"synopsis":"Opens BC bytes of room before HL: checks they fit (TEST_ROOM, report 4 when not), moves the\npointer variables past HL up by BC (MOVE_POINTERS), then everything from HL to the old\nSTKEND up by BC.\nExit: DE = the room's last byte (HL + BC - 1), HL = the given HL - 1, BC = 0.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "5718": {"comment":"Room?"},
        "5721": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5722": {"comment":"The pointers moved"},
        "5725": {"comment":"HL = the old STKEND"},
        "5728": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = the new"},
        "5729": {"comment":"Everything moved up"},
        "5732": {"synopsis":"Adds BC to each of the 14 pointer variables from VARS to STKEND ($5C4B-$5C66) that point\npast HL.\nExit: HL as given, DE = the old STKEND, BC = the bytes from HL to the old STKEND, both\nincluded.\nChanges: F, BC, DE.","comment":"AF kept"},
        "5733": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "5734": {"comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "5737": {"comment":"14 pointers"},
        "5739": {"synopsis":"One pointer: DE = its value.","comment":"DE = the pointer"},
        "5742": {"comment":"HL = the given HL"},
        "5743": {"comment":"Clear the carry"},
        "5744": {"comment":"Below the pointer?"},
        "5746": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5747": {"comment":"HL = the pointer's high byte"},
        "5748": {"comment":"Not past HL?"},
        "5750": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "5751": {"comment":"+ BC"},
        "5754": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "5758": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "5759": {"synopsis":"The next pointer, 14 in all.","comment":"The next pointer"},
        "5760": {"comment":"One less"},
        "5761": {"comment":"All 14"},
        "5763": {"comment":"HL = the old STKEND"},
        "5764": {"comment":"DE = the given HL"},
        "5765": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "5767": {"comment":"Less the given HL"},
        "5769": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "5771": {"comment":"+ 1: both included"},
        "5772": {"comment":"HL = the old STKEND"},
        "5773": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = the given HL"},
        "5775": {"synopsis":"Two zero bytes: LINE_NO_PREV reads them as line number 0 when there is no line."},
        "5777": {"synopsis":"HL is not a line (bits 6-7 of its first byte set: the variables): tries the line at DE, and\nthen ZERO_WORD's 0.","comment":"HL = the line at DE"},
        "5778": {"comment":"DE = ZERO_WORD"},
        "5781": {"synopsis":"DE = the number of the line at HL (high byte first); when HL is not a line, the number of\nthe line at DE, or 0 (LINE_NO_PREV).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"The first byte"},
        "5782": {"comment":"Bits 6-7: not a line?"},
        "5786": {"comment":"D = the number's high byte"},
        "5788": {"comment":"E = its low byte"},
        "5790": {"synopsis":"The rest of WORK_ROOM: opens the room before STKBOT - 1 (MAKE_ROOM), so that byte's copy\nlands in the room; WORKSP is put back (MOVE_POINTERS moves it when the workspace is empty).","comment":"HL = STKBOT"},
        "5793": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "5794": {"comment":"The room before it"},
        "5797": {"comment":"HL past the room"},
        "5799": {"comment":"BC = the old WORKSP"},
        "5800": {"comment":"WORKSP back"},
        "5804": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "5805": {"comment":"DE = past the room, HL = its last byte"},
        "5806": {"comment":"HL past the room"},
        "5808": {"synopsis":"Empties the edit line to a single $0D (K_CUR on it) followed by $80, then the workspace and\nthe calculator stack (CLEAR_WS).\nChanges: HL; K_CUR, WORKSP, STKBOT, STKEND, MEM.","comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "5811": {"comment":"The $0D"},
        "5813": {"comment":"K_CUR on it"},
        "5817": {"comment":"The $80"},
        "5820": {"comment":"WORKSP after it"},
        "5823": {"synopsis":"Empties the workspace and the calculator stack: STKBOT = WORKSP, then CALC_RESET.\nChanges: HL; STKBOT, STKEND, MEM.","comment":"HL = WORKSP"},
        "5826": {"comment":"STKBOT = it"},
        "5829": {"synopsis":"Empties the calculator stack: STKEND = STKBOT, MEM = MEMBOT ($5C92).\nExit: HL = STKBOT.\nChanges: HL; STKEND, MEM.","comment":"HL = STKBOT"},
        "5832": {"comment":"STKEND = it"},
        "5835": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5836": {"comment":"HL = MEMBOT"},
        "5839": {"comment":"MEM = it"},
        "5842": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5844": {"comment":"DE = E_LINE: no caller in this ROM"},
        "5848": {"comment":"Removes from E_LINE up to HL (RECLAIM_DE_HL)"},
        "5851": {"synopsis":"Past the offset byte to the next pair."},
        "5852": {"synopsis":"Looks C up in a table of (code, offset) byte pairs at HL, ended by a zero code.\nExit: carry and HL = the matching offset byte; no carry when C is not there.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The code"},
        "5853": {"comment":"0: the end, no carry"},
        "5855": {"comment":"This one?"},
        "5856": {"comment":"HL to its offset"},
        "5857": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5859": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "5861": {"synopsis":"CLOSE #s: the stream's channel letter is looked up (CLOSE_CHANNEL, which changes nothing for\nK, S and P), then the stream word is put back: streams -3 to 3 to their channels at start-up\n(STREAM_DATA), 4-15 to 0 (closed). 16 or more is report O.\nObserved: after OPEN #4,\"s\", CLOSE #4 left stream 4's word 0 and PRINT #4 gave report O;\nafter OPEN #2,\"k\" (word 1), CLOSE #2 put it back to 6.","comment":"HL = the stream's word, BC = its value"},
        "5864": {"comment":"The channel's letter looked up"},
        "5867": {"comment":"0: closed"},
        "5870": {"comment":"$A3E2 + the word's address: carry for streams 4 and up"},
        "5873": {"comment":"HL = the word's address, DE = it"},
        "5874": {"comment":"Streams 4 and up: carry"},
        "5875": {"comment":"Then 0"},
        "5877": {"comment":"Otherwise the start-up word: STREAM_DATA's ($15D4 + ...)"},
        "5880": {"comment":"HL = the word in STREAM_DATA"},
        "5881": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "5884": {"synopsis":"Stores BC as the stream's word.","comment":"HL = the stream's word"},
        "5885": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5889": {"synopsis":"Looks the stream's channel letter up in CLOSE_LETTERS and jumps to its entry; all three\nentries lead to CLOSE_DONE, so nothing more is done. HL kept.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "5890": {"comment":"HL = CHANS"},
        "5893": {"comment":"+ the stream's value"},
        "5894": {"comment":"HL to the channel's letter"},
        "5897": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "5898": {"comment":"DE = the stream's word"},
        "5899": {"comment":"HL = CLOSE_LETTERS"},
        "5902": {"comment":"Looked up"},
        "5905": {"comment":"C = the offset"},
        "5908": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "5909": {"comment":"Into it"},
        "5910": {"synopsis":"CLOSE's channel letters for TABLE_LOOKUP: K, S and P, each offset leading to CLOSE_DONE."},
        "5916": {"synopsis":"HL back, and return."},
        "5918": {"synopsis":"The STRMS word of stream A (0-15; 16 or more is report O): HL = its address, BC = its value.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"A = the stream"},
        "5921": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "5923": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5925": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $17 (report O, \"Invalid stream\").\nObserved: FORMAT \"a\" gave \"O Invalid stream, 0:1\"."},
        "5927": {"synopsis":"HL = STRMS + 2 x (A + 3): the stream's word (stream -3 is the first).","comment":"+ 3: stream -3 first"},
        "5929": {"comment":"Times 2"},
        "5930": {"comment":"HL = STRMS"},
        "5936": {"comment":"HL = the stream's word"},
        "5937": {"comment":"BC = its value"},
        "5940": {"comment":"HL back to its low byte"},
        "5942": {"synopsis":"OPEN #s,c$: a stream already open on another channel than K, S or P is report O; the channel\n(OPEN_CHANNEL) gives the stream's word: K 1, S 6, P 16.\nObserved: OPEN #4,\"s\" set stream 4's word to 6 and PRINT #4 printed on the screen; OPEN\n#4,\"P\" then set it to 16; OPEN #16,\"s\" gave report O.","comment":"The stream number on top"},
        "5945": {"comment":"HL = the stream's word, BC = its value"},
        "5948": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "5950": {"comment":"Then open it"},
        "5952": {"comment":"DE = the word's address"},
        "5953": {"comment":"HL = CHANS"},
        "5956": {"comment":"+ the value"},
        "5957": {"comment":"HL to its letter"},
        "5960": {"comment":"A = the letter"},
        "5961": {"comment":"HL = the word's address"},
        "5962": {"comment":"K?"},
        "5966": {"comment":"S?"},
        "5970": {"comment":"P?"},
        "5972": {"comment":"Another: report O"},
        "5974": {"synopsis":"The stream's word = DE.","comment":"DE = the new value"},
        "5977": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5981": {"synopsis":"The channel's name, one letter, either case: its offset from OPEN_LETTERS (DE = 1, 6 or 16);\nan empty name, another letter or a longer name is report F.\nObserved: OPEN #5,\"q\", OPEN #5,\"ss\" and OPEN #5,\"\" gave \"F Invalid file name\".","comment":"The word's address kept"},
        "5982": {"comment":"DE = the name, BC = its length"},
        "5985": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "5987": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5989": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0E (report F, \"Invalid file name\")."},
        "5991": {"synopsis":"The first letter, upper case (AND $DF), looked up.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "5992": {"comment":"The first letter"},
        "5993": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "5995": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "5996": {"comment":"HL = OPEN_LETTERS"},
        "5999": {"comment":"Looked up"},
        "6002": {"comment":"Not there: report F"},
        "6004": {"comment":"C = the offset"},
        "6007": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "6008": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "6009": {"comment":"Into it"},
        "6010": {"synopsis":"OPEN's channel letters for TABLE_LOOKUP: K to OPEN_K, S to OPEN_S, P to OPEN_P; 0 ends it."},
        "6017": {"synopsis":"K: offset 1.","comment":"K: 1"},
        "6021": {"synopsis":"S: offset 6.","comment":"S: 6"},
        "6025": {"synopsis":"P: offset 16.","comment":"P: 16"},
        "6027": {"synopsis":"The name must be one letter long (report F otherwise); D = 0.","comment":"Less 1"},
        "6028": {"comment":"One letter?"},
        "6030": {"comment":"No: report F"},
        "6032": {"comment":"D = 0"},
        "6033": {"comment":"HL = the word's address"},
        "6035": {"synopsis":"CAT, ERASE, FORMAT and MOVE: the syntax table's routine for all four; jumps to REPORT_O_2.","comment":"Report O"},
        "6037": {"synopsis":"The automatic listing, after a line is entered (MAIN_LOOP) and after cursor up or down:\n1. LIST_SP = SP; TV_FLAG = $10 (bit 4: an automatic listing); the whole screen cleared, then\n   the lower screen's lines; FLAGS2 bit 0 set (the screen holds a listing).\n2. The top line: S_TOP = E_PPC when the current line is above S_TOP (AL_TOP_CURRENT);\n   otherwise S_TOP moves on a line at a time until the current line starts less than $02C0\n   bytes (22 lines of 32) after the top line.\n3. LIST_ALL from S_TOP's line (the line before it when S_TOP's is gone); TV_FLAG bit 4\n   cleared.\nObserved: with 30 REM lines 20-600 and E_PPC 600, rows 0-21 showed lines 180-600, '>' on\n600; after 25 cursor ups, E_PPC = S_TOP = 100, at row 0 with the '>'.","comment":"LIST_SP = SP"},
        "6041": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 4: an automatic listing"},
        "6045": {"comment":"The whole screen cleared"},
        "6048": {"comment":"The lower screen"},
        "6052": {"comment":"B = DF_SZ"},
        "6055": {"comment":"Its lines cleared"},
        "6058": {"comment":"The upper screen"},
        "6062": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 0: a listing on the screen"},
        "6066": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "6069": {"comment":"DE = S_TOP"},
        "6074": {"comment":"Below S_TOP?"},
        "6076": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6077": {"comment":"The current line above S_TOP?"},
        "6079": {"comment":"S_TOP kept"},
        "6080": {"comment":"HL = the current line"},
        "6083": {"comment":"$02C0: 22 lines of 32 characters"},
        "6086": {"comment":"HL = the current line's address, DE = $02C0"},
        "6087": {"comment":"Less $02C0"},
        "6089": {"comment":"Kept, HL = S_TOP"},
        "6090": {"comment":"HL = S_TOP's line"},
        "6093": {"comment":"BC = the current line's address less $02C0"},
        "6094": {"synopsis":"Is the current line within $02C0 bytes of S_TOP's line? If not, S_TOP = the next line's\nnumber, and again.","comment":"Kept"},
        "6095": {"comment":"DE = the next line"},
        "6098": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "6099": {"comment":"HL + it: carry once past the limit"},
        "6100": {"comment":"Close enough: list"},
        "6102": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "6103": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "6106": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6107": {"comment":"S_TOP = it"},
        "6111": {"comment":"Again"},
        "6113": {"synopsis":"S_TOP = E_PPC: the current line goes at the top.","comment":"S_TOP = E_PPC"},
        "6116": {"synopsis":"HL = S_TOP's line, or the one before it (FIND_LINE), and LIST_ALL from there.","comment":"HL = S_TOP"},
        "6119": {"comment":"HL = its line"},
        "6122": {"comment":"Found"},
        "6124": {"comment":"Otherwise the one before"},
        "6125": {"synopsis":"LIST_ALL from HL, then TV_FLAG bit 4 cleared.","comment":"Listed"},
        "6128": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 4 clear"},
        "6133": {"synopsis":"LLIST: LIST to stream 3 (the printer).","comment":"Stream 3"},
        "6137": {"synopsis":"LIST [n]: lists from line n (0 without it) to stream 2, or to the stream after '#': E_PPC =\nn (masked to 16383), which makes it the current line, then LIST_ALL from the first line n or\nmore.\nObserved: with lines 10, 20, 30, LIST 20 listed 20 (with '>') and 30 and left E_PPC 20; LIST\nlisted all three.","comment":"Stream 2"},
        "6139": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG = 0; when running, stream A opened (STREAM_SELECT); a '#' stream changes it\n(STREAM_ALTER).","comment":"TV_FLAG = 0"},
        "6143": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "6146": {"comment":"Then the stream opened"},
        "6149": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "6150": {"comment":"A '#' stream?"},
        "6153": {"comment":"No: an optional number"},
        "6155": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "6156": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "6160": {"comment":"','?"},
        "6162": {"comment":"Neither: 0"},
        "6164": {"synopsis":"After '#s' a ';' or ',' and the line number (CLASS_6).","comment":"Past it"},
        "6165": {"comment":"A number"},
        "6170": {"synopsis":"No line number after the stream: 0.","comment":"0"},
        "6175": {"synopsis":"No '#': an optional line number (FETCH_NUM).","comment":"An optional number"},
        "6178": {"synopsis":"The statement ends; E_PPC = the line (TAKE_WORD, AND $3F on the high byte), FIND_LINE, then\nLIST_ALL.","comment":"The statement must end"},
        "6181": {"comment":"BC = the line"},
        "6185": {"comment":"Up to 16383"},
        "6187": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "6189": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "6192": {"comment":"HL = its line, or the one after"},
        "6195": {"synopsis":"Lists from the line at HL, E = 1 to begin with: each line by PRINT_LINE and its $0D (RST\n$10).\nFor LIST (TV_FLAG bit 4 clear) it goes to the end of the program, where PRINT_LINE returns\nfrom here.\nFor the automatic listing, at the bottom of the upper screen (S_POSN's line = DF_SZ) it\nstops once the current line has been listed (E = 0); otherwise S_TOP moves on a line\n(E_PPC_NEXT) and listing goes on, the screen scrolling.","comment":"E = 1"},
        "6197": {"synopsis":"One line: PRINT_LINE, then its $0D; the tests that end the listing.","comment":"One line"},
        "6200": {"comment":"The line's $0D: to the next line"},
        "6201": {"comment":"An automatic listing?"},
        "6205": {"comment":"No: on to the end"},
        "6207": {"comment":"DF_SZ"},
        "6210": {"comment":"Less S_POSN's line"},
        "6213": {"comment":"Not yet at the bottom of the upper screen?"},
        "6215": {"comment":"E: 0 once the current line is listed"},
        "6216": {"comment":"The current line listed: done"},
        "6217": {"comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "6219": {"comment":"Not yet: S_TOP on by one line"},
        "6222": {"comment":"S_TOP = the next line"},
        "6225": {"comment":"DE and HL back"},
        "6227": {"comment":"On"},
        "6229": {"synopsis":"Prints the program line at HL through the current channel (LIST, the automatic listing,\nKEY_EDIT):\n1. Its number in four characters, leading zeros as spaces (PRINT_LINE_NO), then '>' when it\n   is the current line (E_PPC).\n2. Its text (PRINT_TEXT), up to its $0D, which is left in A.\nPast the program (HL at the variables: first byte $40 or more) it drops its return address,\nso it returns from its caller instead.\nExit: HL = the next line; E = 1 up to and including the current line, 0 after it (kept in\nBREG too); A = $0D.","comment":"BC = E_PPC"},
        "6233": {"comment":"This line against it"},
        "6238": {"comment":"The current line: D = '>'"},
        "6243": {"comment":"Other lines: E = 1 when before the current one"},
        "6245": {"synopsis":"BREG = E, the before-or-at-the-current-line flag; then the line, or a return from the\ncaller past the program.","comment":"BREG = E"},
        "6248": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "6249": {"comment":"$40 or more: the variables"},
        "6251": {"comment":"The caller's return"},
        "6252": {"comment":"Past the program: return from the caller"},
        "6253": {"comment":"Back"},
        "6254": {"comment":"The number"},
        "6257": {"comment":"HL to the text"},
        "6260": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0 clear: a space before a keyword"},
        "6264": {"comment":"A '>'?"},
        "6268": {"comment":"The '>'"},
        "6269": {"synopsis":"Prints a line's text from HL to its $0D, with no space before a first keyword (FLAGS bit 0\nset). EDIT_LINE_SHOW enters here for the edit line."},
        "6273": {"synopsis":"Starts in K mode (FLAGS bit 2 clear), or L for INPUT's line (FLAGX bit 5); FLAGS2 bit 2\n(inside quotes) cleared.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "6274": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "6275": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 2 clear: not in quotes"},
        "6279": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "6282": {"comment":"K mode"},
        "6284": {"comment":"INPUT?"},
        "6290": {"comment":"Then L mode"},
        "6292": {"synopsis":"One character: a flashing '?' first where X_PTR points (a syntax error), and the cursor\nwhere K_CUR points (PRINT_CURSOR); hidden numbers skipped (SKIP_NUMBER); the character\nthrough PRINT_LIST_CHR.","comment":"HL = X_PTR"},
        "6296": {"comment":"The error's place?"},
        "6300": {"comment":"'?'"},
        "6302": {"comment":"Flashing"},
        "6305": {"synopsis":"The cursor, then the character at DE.","comment":"The cursor, if here"},
        "6308": {"comment":"HL = the character's address"},
        "6309": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6310": {"comment":"Past a hidden number"},
        "6313": {"comment":"On"},
        "6314": {"comment":"$0D?"},
        "6318": {"comment":"DE = the next"},
        "6319": {"comment":"Printed (PRINT_LIST_CHR)"},
        "6322": {"comment":"Again"},
        "6324": {"synopsis":"The $0D: done, DE back."},
        "6326": {"synopsis":"When A is the number marker $0E, moves HL past the hidden 5-byte number after it; A = the\nbyte there.\nChanges: A, HL.","comment":"The marker?"},
        "6329": {"comment":"Six bytes on"},
        "6335": {"comment":"A = the byte there"},
        "6337": {"synopsis":"Prints A flashing: ATTR_T bit 7 (FLASH) set and MASK_T's cleared, P_FLAG 0, for this one\ncharacter (SCREEN_OUTPUT); then all three back. Keeps the main registers (EXX).","comment":"The alternate set"},
        "6338": {"comment":"L = ATTR_T, H = MASK_T"},
        "6341": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6342": {"comment":"MASK_T bit 7 clear"},
        "6344": {"comment":"FLASH on"},
        "6346": {"comment":"Set"},
        "6349": {"comment":"HL = P_FLAG"},
        "6352": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "6353": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6354": {"comment":"P_FLAG = 0"},
        "6356": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "6359": {"comment":"H = the old P_FLAG"},
        "6360": {"comment":"Back"},
        "6363": {"comment":"HL = the old ATTR_T, MASK_T"},
        "6364": {"comment":"Back"},
        "6367": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "6369": {"synopsis":"When DE = K_CUR, prints the cursor letter flashing (PRINT_FLASH): E or G for MODE 1 or 2;\notherwise K, or L when FLAGS bit 2 is set (L mode), or C instead of L with CAPS LOCK (FLAGS2\nbit 3). FLAGS bit 3 is set for L or C, cleared for K.\nObserved: the edit line showed PRINT 123L, then K at its start, E and G in those modes.","comment":"HL = K_CUR"},
        "6373": {"comment":"Here?"},
        "6375": {"comment":"No"},
        "6376": {"comment":"A = MODE"},
        "6379": {"comment":"Times 2"},
        "6381": {"comment":"MODE 0"},
        "6383": {"comment":"2 gives 'E', 4 'G'"},
        "6387": {"synopsis":"MODE 0: K, L or C.","comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "6390": {"comment":"Bit 3 clear: K"},
        "6392": {"comment":"'K'"},
        "6394": {"comment":"L mode?"},
        "6398": {"comment":"Bit 3 set"},
        "6400": {"comment":"'L'"},
        "6401": {"comment":"CAPS LOCK?"},
        "6407": {"comment":"'C'"},
        "6409": {"synopsis":"Prints the letter (PRINT_FLASH), DE kept."},
        "6415": {"synopsis":"DE = the number of the line after the one in the word at HL (FIND_LINE for that number + 1,\nthen LINE_NO), stored back (SET_LINE_WORD). KEY_DOWN uses it on E_PPC.","comment":"DE = the number"},
        "6418": {"comment":"The word's high byte kept"},
        "6419": {"comment":"HL = the number"},
        "6420": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "6421": {"comment":"HL = that line, or the next"},
        "6424": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "6427": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6428": {"synopsis":"Stores DE as the line number in the word whose high byte is at HL, unless FLAGX bit 5 is set\n(INPUT).","comment":"INPUT?"},
        "6433": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "6437": {"synopsis":"A zero digit before the first: E is printed instead ($20, a space), or nothing when E is\n$FF.","comment":"A = E"},
        "6439": {"comment":"$FF: nothing"},
        "6440": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "6442": {"synopsis":"Prints the digit of HL for the power of ten -BC: HL is left with the rest. A zero before the\nfirst digit is E (DIGIT_ZERO); a digit goes through PRINT_A_DIGIT, which leaves E = \"0\", so\nlater zeros print as 0.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "6443": {"synopsis":"Counts how many times the power fits.","comment":"HL less the power"},
        "6444": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "6445": {"comment":"Until below 0"},
        "6447": {"comment":"Added back"},
        "6449": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "6450": {"comment":"0: DIGIT_ZERO"},
        "6452": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "6455": {"synopsis":"Prints A (RST $10) and keeps FLAGS bit 2, the K/L mode the cursor shows: digits and codes\nbelow $21 leave it; THEN ($CB), and \":\" outside quotes and outside INPUT, clear it (K); a\nquote toggles FLAGS2 bit 2 (inside quotes); anything else sets it (L).","comment":"A digit?"},
        "6458": {"comment":"A digit: no change"},
        "6460": {"comment":"Below $21?"},
        "6464": {"comment":"K mode for now"},
        "6468": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "6472": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "6476": {"comment":"\":\" in INPUT's line: L"},
        "6482": {"comment":"\":\" inside quotes: L; outside: K"},
        "6490": {"synopsis":"A quote: FLAGS2 bit 2 toggled.","comment":"A quote?"},
        "6494": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6495": {"comment":"A = FLAGS2"},
        "6498": {"comment":"Bit 2 toggled"},
        "6503": {"comment":"A back"},
        "6504": {"synopsis":"FLAGS bit 2 set: L mode."},
        "6508": {"synopsis":"Prints A."},
        "6510": {"synopsis":"Finds line HL: HL = the first line whose number is HL or more (or the variables area when\nnone), DE = the line before it (PROG when it is the first).\nExit: Z when the line is there.","comment":"The number kept"},
        "6511": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "6514": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "6516": {"synopsis":"Compares the line at HL with BC (CMP_LINE_NO); returns when it is not smaller, else on to\nthe next (NEXT_ITEM).","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6517": {"comment":"This line's number against it"},
        "6520": {"comment":"Not smaller: found"},
        "6521": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6522": {"comment":"DE = the next line"},
        "6525": {"comment":"HL = it, DE = this one"},
        "6528": {"synopsis":"Compares the line number at HL (high byte first) with BC: Z when equal, carry when smaller.\nHL kept.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"The high bytes"},
        "6530": {"comment":"Different: done"},
        "6532": {"comment":"The low bytes"},
        "6533": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6536": {"comment":"No caller in this ROM: past a line's number and length"},
        "6539": {"synopsis":"Finds statement D of the line at HL (CH_ADD = HL), counting ':' and THEN outside quotes;\nwith E a token, stops at that token first.\nExit: Z when statement D is reached (CH_ADD before it); NC and A = E when the token is\nfound; carry at the line's ENTER.","comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "6542": {"comment":"C = 0: outside quotes"},
        "6544": {"synopsis":"One statement fewer to go; none: Z, found."},
        "6546": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "6547": {"comment":"The token?"},
        "6550": {"comment":"No carry: found"},
        "6552": {"synopsis":"The next byte."},
        "6554": {"synopsis":"Hidden numbers skipped (SKIP_NUMBER), CH_ADD kept; a quote toggles C bit 0 (inside quotes)."},
        "6557": {"comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "6560": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "6564": {"comment":"Toggled"},
        "6565": {"synopsis":"':' or THEN: a statement starts, unless inside quotes.","comment":"':'?"},
        "6569": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "6573": {"synopsis":"Outside quotes? Then the count."},
        "6577": {"synopsis":"ENTER ends the search: D - 1 and carry.","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "6581": {"comment":"One less"},
        "6582": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "6584": {"synopsis":"Finds the item after the one at HL, a program line or a variable, by its first byte:\n1. Below $40: a line, number and length word first (NI_LINE).\n2. Bit 5 clear ($40-$5F, $80-$9F, $C0-$DF): a length word after the letter (NI_LENGTH).\n3. $60-$7F: 5 bytes after the letter; $E0-$FF: 18 ($12); $A0-$DF with bit 5: a name ended by\n   bit 7, then 5 bytes (NI_NUMBER, NI_NAME).\nFalls into DIFFERENCE.\nExit: DE = the next item, HL = this one, BC = the length.","comment":"This item kept"},
        "6585": {"comment":"Its first byte"},
        "6586": {"comment":"A line?"},
        "6590": {"comment":"A length word?"},
        "6594": {"comment":"Doubled: bit 7 into the carry, bit 6 into the sign"},
        "6595": {"comment":"$60-$7F and $E0-$FF: no name to walk"},
        "6598": {"comment":"$A0-$BF: carry cleared"},
        "6599": {"synopsis":"C = 5, or $12 when the doubled first byte left carry set ($E0-$FF)."},
        "6604": {"comment":"$E0-$FF: 18"},
        "6606": {"synopsis":"Walks a long name: up to the byte with bit 7 set.","comment":"Bit 7 into the carry"},
        "6607": {"comment":"On"},
        "6608": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "6609": {"comment":"Until the name's last letter"},
        "6611": {"comment":"Then + BC"},
        "6613": {"synopsis":"A line: past its number high byte..."},
        "6614": {"synopsis":"... and to its length word: BC = the length."},
        "6615": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "6618": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6619": {"synopsis":"HL + BC: the next item."},
        "6620": {"comment":"DE = this item"},
        "6621": {"synopsis":"BC = HL - DE; then HL and DE swapped (HL = the old DE).\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6622": {"comment":"HL less DE"},
        "6624": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "6626": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6627": {"comment":"Swapped"},
        "6629": {"synopsis":"Removes the bytes from DE up to, not including, HL (DIFFERENCE, then RECLAIM)."},
        "6632": {"synopsis":"Removes BC bytes at HL: moves the pointer variables past them down by BC (MOVE_POINTERS with\n-BC), then everything after them down.\nExit: HL = the old HL, now the first byte after the removed ones; BC = 0.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "6633": {"comment":"BC = -BC"},
        "6640": {"comment":"The pointers moved down"},
        "6643": {"comment":"DE = HL, the first byte to remove"},
        "6644": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "6645": {"comment":"HL = the first byte after them"},
        "6646": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6647": {"comment":"Everything after them moved down"},
        "6649": {"comment":"HL = the old HL"},
        "6651": {"synopsis":"Reads the edit line's line number into BC through the calculator (CH_ADD left after it, the\ncalculator stack emptied at the end); 0 when there is none. 10000 or more stops with report\nC (REPORT_C).","comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "6654": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "6655": {"comment":"CH_ADD = it"},
        "6658": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "6659": {"comment":"HL = MEMBOT"},
        "6662": {"comment":"STKEND = it: the calculator stack there for the moment"},
        "6665": {"comment":"The digits"},
        "6668": {"comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6673": {"comment":"Carry when BC is 10000 or more ($D8F0 = -10000)"},
        "6677": {"synopsis":"Report C when the number did not fit 16 bits (FP_TO_BC's carry) or is 10000 or more (the\ncarry of adding -10000)."},
        "6680": {"comment":"The calculator stack emptied"},
        "6683": {"synopsis":"Prints BC as a decimal number with no leading zeros (E = $FF), for the report's line and\nstatement numbers. A number with B bit 7 set prints as 0.","comment":"DE and HL kept"},
        "6685": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "6686": {"comment":"B bit 7?"},
        "6688": {"comment":"Then 0"},
        "6690": {"comment":"HL = BC"},
        "6692": {"comment":"No leading zeros"},
        "6696": {"synopsis":"Prints the line number at HL (high byte first) in four characters, leading zeros as spaces\n(E = $20).\nExit: HL = the number's low byte.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "6697": {"comment":"DE = the number"},
        "6700": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6701": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "6702": {"comment":"Spaces for leading zeros"},
        "6704": {"synopsis":"The thousands, hundreds and tens (DIGIT_OUT), then the units.","comment":"Thousands"},
        "6710": {"comment":"Hundreds"},
        "6716": {"comment":"Tens"},
        "6721": {"comment":"A = the units"},
        "6722": {"synopsis":"The last digit: A (0 for a number with B bit 7 set, such as PPC $FFFE)."},
        "6725": {"comment":"HL and DE back"},
        "6728": {"synopsis":"Syntax offsets: 50 bytes, one for each command keyword in token order, $CE (DEF FN) to $FF\n(COPY). Each is a relative pointer: the keyword's entry in SYNTAX_ENTRIES is at this byte's\naddress plus its value. STMT_START reads it as $1A48 + (keyword - $CE)."},
        "6778": {"synopsis":"Syntax entries: each command's operands, items SYNTAX_ITEM reads in turn: operand classes\n($00-$0B, CLASS_TABLE), characters and keywords the line must have; classes 0, 3 and 5 are\nfollowed by the command routine's address and end the entry, as do 2, 7 and $0B.\nLET 1 = 2; GO TO 6, 0 GO_TO_CMD; IF 6 THEN 5 IF_CMD; GO SUB 6, 0 GO_SUB_CMD; STOP 0\nSTOP_CMD; RETURN 0 RETURN_CMD; FOR 4 = 6 TO 6, 5 FOR_CMD; NEXT 4, 0 NEXT_CMD; PRINT 5\nPRINT_CMD; INPUT 5 INPUT_CMD; DIM 5 DIM_CMD; REM 5 REM_CMD; NEW 0 NEW_CMD; RUN 3 RUN_CMD;\nLIST 5 LIST_CMD; POKE 8, 0 POKE_CMD; RANDOMIZE 3 RANDOMIZE_CMD; CONTINUE 0 CONTINUE_CMD;\nCLEAR 3 CLEAR_CMD; CLS 0 CLS_CMD; PLOT 9, 0 PLOT_CMD; PAUSE 6, 0 PAUSE_CMD; READ 5 READ_CMD;\nDATA 5 DATA_CMD; RESTORE 3 RESTORE_CMD; DRAW 9, 5 DRAW_CMD; COPY 0 COPY_CMD; LPRINT 5\nLPRINT_CMD; LLIST 5 LLIST_CMD; SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY, MERGE $0B; BEEP 8, 0 BEEP_CMD; CIRCLE 9,\n5 CIRCLE_CMD; INK to OVER 7; OUT 8, 0 OUT_CMD; BORDER 6, 0 BORDER_CMD; DEF FN 5 DEF_FN_CMD;\nOPEN # 6 , $0A, 0 OPEN_CMD; CLOSE # 6, 0 CLOSE_CMD; FORMAT $0A, 0; MOVE $0A , $0A, 0; ERASE\n$0A, 0; CAT 0, all four CAT_ETC_CMD.\nThe keywords and addresses are read from the bytes; the keywords spelt from KEYWORD_TABLE."},
        "6935": {"synopsis":"Checks the edit line's syntax: FLAGS bit 7 cleared (check, do not run), the line number read\n(EDIT_LINE_NO), SUBPPC = 0, ERR_NR = $FF, then the statements one by one (STMT_START). A\nsyntax error stops with RST $08, X_PTR at it; it returns through the ERR_SP slot to\nMAIN_ENTRY's test at $12B7.\nObserved: GO TO \"a\" was refused, the edit line showing GO TO \"a\" with the ? marker.","comment":"FLAGS bit 7 clear: checking"},
        "6939": {"comment":"The line number read"},
        "6942": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "6943": {"comment":"SUBPPC = 0"},
        "6946": {"comment":"A = $FF"},
        "6947": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no error"},
        "6952": {"synopsis":"The statement loop: past the ':' (or THEN) to the next statement."},
        "6953": {"synopsis":"One statement, checked or run (FLAGS bit 7):\n1. The workspace emptied (CLEAR_WS), SUBPPC + 1 (128 statements is report C).\n2. ENTER ends the line (LINE_END); another ':' is an empty statement.\n3. The command keyword ($CE DEF FN to $FF COPY, else report C) picks its entry in\n   SYNTAX_ENTRIES through SYNTAX_OFFSETS, and SYNTAX_ITEM works through it, with STMT_RET as\n   the return when the command's routine finishes.\nObserved: PRINT 1: PRINT 2 ran both and reported 0:2.","comment":"The workspace emptied"},
        "6956": {"comment":"SUBPPC + 1"},
        "6959": {"comment":"Statement 128: report C"},
        "6962": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "6963": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "6965": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "6969": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "6973": {"comment":"The command returns to STMT_RET"},
        "6977": {"comment":"C = the keyword"},
        "6978": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6980": {"comment":"$CE (DEF FN) and up: a command"},
        "6985": {"comment":"C = the index"},
        "6986": {"comment":"$1A48 + index: the entry's offset"},
        "6990": {"comment":"C = the offset"},
        "6991": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "6994": {"synopsis":"SYNTAX_ITEM again from T_ADDR: the return address every item leaves.","comment":"HL = the entry's next item"},
        "6997": {"synopsis":"Reads the entry's next item at HL, T_ADDR following it:\n- below $20, an operand class: its routine from CLASS_TABLE, entered with A = the line's\n  current character, NZ, and SYNTAX_NEXT as the return;\n- $20 and up, a character or keyword the line must have next (SYNTAX_CHAR).","comment":"The item"},
        "6999": {"comment":"T_ADDR = the one after"},
        "7002": {"comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT as the return"},
        "7006": {"comment":"C = the item"},
        "7007": {"comment":"A class?"},
        "7011": {"comment":"HL for CLASS_TABLE"},
        "7017": {"comment":"C = the offset"},
        "7018": {"comment":"HL = the class's routine"},
        "7019": {"comment":"For the RET"},
        "7020": {"comment":"A = the current character"},
        "7021": {"comment":"B = $FF: NZ"},
        "7022": {"comment":"Into the class"},
        "7023": {"synopsis":"The character or keyword (in C) must be the line's next, else report C; then past it.","comment":"The current character"},
        "7024": {"comment":"The one wanted?"},
        "7025": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7028": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7030": {"synopsis":"Where a command returns to: BREAK_KEY first (report L for BREAK); then, with no jump (NSPPC\nbit 7 set), the next statement (STMT_NEXT); otherwise the jump: to the edit line (NEWPPC's\nbit 15 set, RUN_EDIT_LINE) or a program line (LINE_NEW).\nObserved: CAPS SHIFT + SPACE during 30 GO TO 30 gave \"L BREAK into program, 30:1\".","comment":"BREAK?"},
        "7033": {"comment":"No"},
        "7035": {"comment":"BREAK: report L"},
        "7037": {"synopsis":"A jump pending (NSPPC bit 7 clear)?","comment":"A jump pending?"},
        "7041": {"comment":"No: the next statement"},
        "7043": {"comment":"HL = NEWPPC"},
        "7046": {"comment":"Bit 15: the edit line?"},
        "7048": {"comment":"No: a program line"},
        "7050": {"synopsis":"Runs the edit line as a direct command: PPC = $FFFE (reports print it as 0), NXTLIN = WORKSP\n- 1 (so the line after it is none), CH_ADD = E_LINE - 1, from statement NSPPC (NEXT_LINE).","comment":"$FFFE"},
        "7053": {"comment":"PPC = it"},
        "7056": {"comment":"HL = WORKSP"},
        "7059": {"comment":"Less 1: NXTLIN"},
        "7060": {"comment":"DE = E_LINE"},
        "7064": {"comment":"Less 1: CH_ADD"},
        "7065": {"comment":"A = NSPPC"},
        "7068": {"comment":"Run from there"},
        "7070": {"synopsis":"Goes to line NEWPPC, statement NSPPC: the line found (FIND_LINE) when it is there; a missing\nline asked for with a statement stops with report N; a missing line otherwise runs the next\none, or, past the program, stops with report 0 (error code $FF).\nObserved: RUN on 10 PRINT 5: GO TO 30 / 20 PRINT 6 printed 5 and reported \"0 OK, 10:2\".","comment":"HL = the line, or the one after"},
        "7073": {"comment":"A = NSPPC"},
        "7076": {"comment":"Found: run it"},
        "7078": {"comment":"A statement asked for?"},
        "7079": {"comment":"Then report N"},
        "7081": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "7082": {"comment":"The next item's first byte"},
        "7083": {"comment":"A line?"},
        "7085": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "7086": {"comment":"Yes: run it from the start"},
        "7088": {"comment":"Past the program: report 0"},
        "7090": {"synopsis":"REM: the rest of the line is skipped (LINE_END), the return to SYNTAX_NEXT dropped.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "7091": {"synopsis":"The end of a line: when checking, done. When running, the next line (NXTLIN), from its first\nstatement, unless it is past the program (bits 6-7 of its first byte), which returns, ending\nthe run.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "7094": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "7095": {"comment":"HL = NXTLIN"},
        "7098": {"comment":"Bits 6-7: past the program?"},
        "7101": {"comment":"Then the run ends"},
        "7102": {"comment":"A = 0: the first statement"},
        "7103": {"synopsis":"Runs the line at HL from statement A (at least 1): PPC = its number, NXTLIN = the line after\nit.","comment":"0 becomes 1"},
        "7107": {"comment":"DE = the line number"},
        "7110": {"comment":"PPC = it"},
        "7115": {"comment":"DE = the line's length"},
        "7118": {"comment":"HL = it, DE = the text's start - 1"},
        "7119": {"comment":"HL = the $0D"},
        "7120": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "7121": {"synopsis":"NXTLIN = HL, CH_ADD = DE (before the text), NSPPC = $FF; statement D: the first at once\n(STMT_LOOP), a later one found by FIND_STATEMENT, or report N when the line has fewer.","comment":"NXTLIN = it"},
        "7124": {"comment":"HL = the text's start - 1"},
        "7125": {"comment":"CH_ADD = it"},
        "7128": {"comment":"D = the statement"},
        "7129": {"comment":"E = 0: no token"},
        "7131": {"comment":"NSPPC = $FF: no jump pending"},
        "7135": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "7136": {"comment":"SUBPPC = it"},
        "7139": {"comment":"The first: run it"},
        "7142": {"comment":"D back"},
        "7143": {"comment":"Statement D found?"},
        "7146": {"comment":"Yes: run it"},
        "7148": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $16 (report N, \"Statement lost\")."},
        "7150": {"synopsis":"The end of a statement's operands. Running: returns, and the command's routine runs.\nChecking: the two returns are dropped and the statement must end here (STMT_NEXT).","comment":"Checking?"},
        "7153": {"comment":"No: the command runs"},
        "7154": {"comment":"Both returns dropped"},
        "7156": {"synopsis":"After a statement: ENTER ends the line (LINE_END), ':' starts the next (STMT_LOOP), anything\nelse is report C.","comment":"The current character"},
        "7157": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "7161": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "7166": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "7169": {"synopsis":"Operand classes: 12 bytes, one for each class 0-$0B, each a relative pointer to the class's\nroutine (this byte's address plus its value): CLASS_0 to CLASS_B."},
        "7181": {"synopsis":"Class 3, an optional number (RUN, RESTORE, RANDOMIZE, CLEAR): FETCH_NUM, then as class 0.","comment":"The number, if any"},
        "7184": {"synopsis":"Class 0: no more operands; Z set, then CLASS_5: the statement must end (STATEMENT_END)\nbefore the routine runs.","comment":"Z: the statement must end"},
        "7185": {"synopsis":"Class 5: the command's routine, whose address follows at T_ADDR, runs now, when checking and\nwhen running; it checks its own operands. (Class 0 enters with Z, which ends the statement\nfirst.)","comment":"The SYNTAX_NEXT return dropped"},
        "7186": {"comment":"Z: STATEMENT_END first"},
        "7189": {"comment":"DE = CH_ADD's pointer, kept"},
        "7190": {"comment":"HL = T_ADDR: the routine's address"},
        "7193": {"comment":"BC = the command's routine"},
        "7196": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "7197": {"comment":"Onto the stack"},
        "7198": {"comment":"Into the command's routine"},
        "7199": {"synopsis":"Class 1, a variable to assign to (LET): looks it up (LOOK_VARS). FLAGX = 0; a missing simple\nvariable is new (FLAGX bit 1), a missing array report 2.","comment":"The variable"},
        "7202": {"synopsis":"FLAGX = 0 and the found/not-found test: class 4's way in.","comment":"FLAGX = 0"},
        "7206": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "7208": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 1: a new variable"},
        "7212": {"comment":"Not an array: DEST and STRLEN set"},
        "7214": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 1 (report 2, \"Variable not found\"): a missing array."},
        "7216": {"synopsis":"Found: subscripts or slicing (VAR_SUBSCRIPTS); for a string when running, its start and\nlength (STK_FETCH) and FLAGX bit 0 from A.","comment":"Subscripts or slices"},
        "7219": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6: a number?"},
        "7223": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7225": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "7226": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "7229": {"comment":"Running: the string's start and length"},
        "7232": {"comment":"HL = FLAGX"},
        "7235": {"comment":"A's bit 0 added"},
        "7236": {"comment":"FLAGX"},
        "7237": {"comment":"HL = the string's start"},
        "7238": {"synopsis":"STRLEN = BC, DEST = HL: what LET_ASSIGN uses.","comment":"STRLEN = BC"},
        "7242": {"comment":"DEST = HL"},
        "7246": {"synopsis":"Class 2, the value LET assigns: VAL_FETCH, then STATEMENT_END. Ends the entry.","comment":"The SYNTAX_NEXT return dropped"},
        "7247": {"comment":"The value"},
        "7250": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "7254": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the expression (SCAN_EXPR); it must be the type FLAGS bit 6 had before (the\nvariable's), else report C. When running, LET_ASSIGN stores it.","comment":"A = FLAGS: the variable's type"},
        "7257": {"synopsis":"VAL_FETCH with A already holding the FLAGS value whose bit 6 the result must match.","comment":"Kept"},
        "7258": {"comment":"The expression"},
        "7261": {"comment":"A = the old FLAGS"},
        "7262": {"comment":"D = FLAGS now"},
        "7265": {"comment":"Compared"},
        "7266": {"comment":"Bit 6: types differ?"},
        "7268": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "7270": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "7272": {"comment":"Then LET_ASSIGN stores it"},
        "7276": {"synopsis":"Class 4, a FOR or NEXT variable: as class 1, but it must be a one-letter number variable\n(the bits LOOK_VARS leaves in C), else report C.","comment":"The variable"},
        "7279": {"comment":"Flags kept"},
        "7280": {"comment":"A = the name's bits"},
        "7281": {"comment":"All bits but 5 and 6 set"},
        "7283": {"comment":"Bits 5 and 6 both set?"},
        "7284": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7286": {"comment":"Flags back"},
        "7287": {"comment":"On as class 1"},
        "7289": {"synopsis":"Past one character, then CLASS_8.","comment":"Past the character"},
        "7290": {"synopsis":"Class 8, two numbers separated by ',' (POKE, BEEP, OUT, PLOT).","comment":"The first number"},
        "7293": {"comment":"','?"},
        "7295": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7297": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7298": {"synopsis":"Class 6, a number: the expression (SCAN_EXPR) must be numeric (FLAGS bit 6 set), else report\nC.\nObserved: GO TO \"a\" was refused.","comment":"The expression"},
        "7301": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6: a number?"},
        "7305": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7306": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\")."},
        "7308": {"synopsis":"Class $0A, a string: the expression must be a string (FLAGS bit 6 clear), else report C.","comment":"The expression"},
        "7311": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6: a number?"},
        "7315": {"comment":"No, a string: done"},
        "7316": {"comment":"Else report C"},
        "7318": {"synopsis":"Class 7, the colour commands INK to OVER: the item (COL_TEMP_ITEM, chosen by T_ADDR) is set\nas a temporary colour, then the statement ends, and when running the temporary colours\nbecome the permanent ones (ATTR_P, MASK_P, and P_FLAG's permanent bits from the temporary).\nEnds the entry.","comment":"FLAGS bit 7: running?"},
        "7322": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared: the main screen"},
        "7326": {"comment":"Running: COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "7329": {"comment":"The SYNTAX_NEXT return dropped"},
        "7330": {"comment":"A = T_ADDR's low byte"},
        "7333": {"comment":"Less $13: the colour command's code"},
        "7335": {"comment":"The colour item"},
        "7338": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "7341": {"comment":"HL = ATTR_T and MASK_T"},
        "7344": {"comment":"ATTR_P and MASK_P = them"},
        "7347": {"comment":"HL = P_FLAG"},
        "7350": {"comment":"A = P_FLAG"},
        "7351": {"comment":"Temporary bits moved onto the permanent ones"},
        "7352": {"comment":"Odd bits from it, even bits kept"},
        "7356": {"comment":"P_FLAG"},
        "7358": {"synopsis":"Class 9, PLOT, DRAW and CIRCLE: when running, the temporary colours with MASK_T's top five\nbits set and P_FLAG bit 6 cleared; then colour items in the statement (COL_ITEMS) and two\nnumbers (CLASS_8).","comment":"Checking?"},
        "7361": {"comment":"Yes: the items only"},
        "7363": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared: the main screen"},
        "7367": {"comment":"The temporary colours"},
        "7370": {"comment":"HL = MASK_T"},
        "7373": {"comment":"A = MASK_T"},
        "7374": {"comment":"Top five bits set"},
        "7376": {"comment":"MASK_T"},
        "7377": {"comment":"P_FLAG bit 6 cleared"},
        "7381": {"comment":"A = the current character"},
        "7382": {"synopsis":"Colour items (COL_ITEMS), then the two numbers.","comment":"The colour items"},
        "7385": {"comment":"Then the two numbers"},
        "7387": {"synopsis":"Class $0B, SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE: TAPE_COMMAND. Ends the entry.","comment":"SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY or MERGE"},
        "7390": {"synopsis":"An optional number: at ENTER or ':' there is none, and running stacks 0 (USE_ZERO);\notherwise CLASS_6.","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "7392": {"comment":"Then no number"},
        "7394": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "7396": {"comment":"No: a number (CLASS_6)"},
        "7398": {"synopsis":"Running: 0 onto the calculator stack.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "7401": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7402": {"comment":"Running: 0 stacked"},
        "7406": {"synopsis":"STOP: stops with error code 8 (report 9). The syntax table's routine for STOP."},
        "7408": {"synopsis":"IF: when running, the condition's value comes off the calculator stack; false (IS_ZERO)\nskips the rest of the line (LINE_END); otherwise, and when checking, the statement after\nTHEN goes on (IF_THEN).\nObserved: IF 0 THEN PRINT 1: PRINT 2 reported 0:1; IF 1 THEN PRINT 1: PRINT 2 reported 0:3.","comment":"The SYNTAX_NEXT return dropped"},
        "7409": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "7412": {"comment":"Yes: the statement after THEN"},
        "7414": {"comment":"The condition removed from the stack"},
        "7417": {"comment":"HL = the condition's value"},
        "7418": {"comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "7421": {"comment":"False: the rest of the line skipped"},
        "7424": {"synopsis":"The statement after THEN: STMT_START.","comment":"True: on with the statement after THEN"},
        "7427": {"synopsis":"FOR: the loop variable, which the value has been assigned to (LET_ASSIGN), becomes an\n19-byte FOR variable (bit 7 of its first byte set; 13 bytes of room made when it was a plain\none): its value, the limit, the step (STEP's number, or 1), the line (PPC) and the statement\nafter FOR. When the loop is already over (NEXT_LOOP), the matching NEXT is found and running\ngoes on after it (FOR_SEARCH).\nObserved: FOR i=1 TO 3: PRINT i;: NEXT i printed 123; STEP -1 from 3 to 1 printed 321; the\nvariable was E9, value, limit, step, FE FF (line -2) and 3.","comment":"STEP?"},
        "7429": {"comment":"No: a step of 1"},
        "7431": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7432": {"comment":"The step"},
        "7435": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "7438": {"comment":"On with the values"},
        "7440": {"synopsis":"No STEP: 1.","comment":"The statement must end"},
        "7443": {"comment":"Running: a step of 1 stacked"},
        "7446": {"synopsis":"The calculator stack: the limit and the step under the value, which is assigned\n(LET_ASSIGN); MEM = the variable's value.","comment":"The value moved above the limit and step"},
        "7453": {"comment":"The value assigned"},
        "7456": {"comment":"MEM = the variable's value"},
        "7459": {"comment":"HL = its name byte"},
        "7460": {"comment":"A = the name byte"},
        "7461": {"comment":"Bit 7: a FOR variable now"},
        "7463": {"comment":"Six bytes"},
        "7466": {"comment":"HL = past the value"},
        "7467": {"comment":"Carry: it was a FOR variable already?"},
        "7468": {"comment":"Yes: the room is there"},
        "7470": {"comment":"13 bytes more"},
        "7472": {"comment":"Room for limit, step, line, statement"},
        "7475": {"comment":"One on"},
        "7476": {"synopsis":"Copies the limit and the step (10 bytes) after the value, then the line and statement.","comment":"Kept"},
        "7477": {"comment":"Limit and step off the stack"},
        "7481": {"comment":"HL = where they go"},
        "7482": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = the limit"},
        "7483": {"comment":"Ten bytes: the limit and the step"},
        "7485": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "7487": {"comment":"HL = PPC"},
        "7490": {"comment":"DE = the line, HL = where it goes"},
        "7491": {"comment":"The line stored"},
        "7494": {"comment":"D = SUBPPC"},
        "7497": {"comment":"The statement after FOR"},
        "7498": {"comment":"Past the line"},
        "7499": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "7500": {"comment":"Is the loop already over?"},
        "7503": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "7504": {"comment":"B = STRLEN's low byte: the variable's name"},
        "7507": {"comment":"HL = PPC"},
        "7510": {"comment":"NEWPPC = PPC"},
        "7513": {"comment":"A = SUBPPC"},
        "7516": {"comment":"Negated"},
        "7518": {"comment":"D = it, for FIND_STATEMENT's count"},
        "7519": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "7522": {"comment":"E = NEXT's token"},
        "7524": {"synopsis":"The loop is over before it starts: from CH_ADD, the next NEXT ($F3) with the loop's letter,\nthrough the lines (LOOK_PROG); none is report I. Running goes on at the statement after it\n(NEWPPC, NSPPC).\nObserved: FOR i=5 TO 1: PRINT \"x\";: NEXT i: PRINT \"y\" printed y.","comment":"Name kept"},
        "7525": {"comment":"BC = NXTLIN"},
        "7529": {"comment":"The next NEXT"},
        "7532": {"comment":"NXTLIN = the line after the one searched"},
        "7536": {"comment":"Name back"},
        "7537": {"comment":"None: report I"},
        "7539": {"comment":"The NEXT's variable"},
        "7540": {"comment":"Lower case"},
        "7542": {"comment":"The loop's variable?"},
        "7543": {"comment":"Yes: found"},
        "7545": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7546": {"comment":"Search on"},
        "7548": {"synopsis":"Found: NSPPC = the statement after the NEXT.","comment":"Past the variable's name"},
        "7549": {"comment":"A = 1"},
        "7551": {"comment":"Less D"},
        "7552": {"comment":"NSPPC = it"},
        "7556": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $11 (report I, \"FOR without NEXT\").\nObserved: FOR k=5 TO 1: PRINT k with no NEXT gave report I."},
        "7558": {"synopsis":"Looks for token E from HL to the end of the program, statement by statement\n(FIND_STATEMENT), NEWPPC following the line. Exit: no carry when found; carry past the\nprogram.","comment":"The current character"},
        "7559": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "7561": {"comment":"Yes: search the rest of the line"},
        "7563": {"synopsis":"The next line: NEWPPC = its number, BC = the line after it; past the program, carry.","comment":"The next line"},
        "7564": {"comment":"Its number's high byte"},
        "7565": {"comment":"A variable, not a line?"},
        "7567": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "7568": {"comment":"Yes: past the program"},
        "7569": {"comment":"B = the number's high byte"},
        "7571": {"comment":"C = the low byte"},
        "7572": {"comment":"NEWPPC = the line number"},
        "7577": {"comment":"C = the length's low byte"},
        "7579": {"comment":"B = the length's high byte"},
        "7580": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "7581": {"comment":"HL = the line after it"},
        "7582": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "7584": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "7585": {"comment":"D = 0: from the line's first statement"},
        "7587": {"synopsis":"Searches the line's statements for the token.","comment":"The line after kept"},
        "7588": {"comment":"Looks for the token in the line"},
        "7591": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "7592": {"comment":"Found: no carry"},
        "7593": {"comment":"Else the next line"},
        "7595": {"synopsis":"NEXT: the variable (DEST) must be a FOR variable (report 1; report 2 when it does not\nexist). Its value + step is stored back (MEM = the variable); when the loop is not over\n(NEXT_LOOP) it jumps to the line and statement kept in it (GO_TO_2).\nObserved: LET j=1: NEXT j gave report 1, NEXT q report 2.","comment":"FLAGX bit 1: the variable missing?"},
        "7599": {"comment":"Yes: report 2"},
        "7602": {"comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "7605": {"comment":"Bit 7: a FOR variable?"},
        "7607": {"comment":"No: report 1"},
        "7609": {"comment":"HL = its value"},
        "7610": {"comment":"MEM = it"},
        "7613": {"comment":"Value + step into memory 0"},
        "7620": {"comment":"Is the loop over?"},
        "7623": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7624": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "7627": {"comment":"15 bytes: value, limit and step"},
        "7630": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "7631": {"comment":"E = its low byte"},
        "7633": {"comment":"D = its high byte"},
        "7635": {"comment":"H = the statement"},
        "7636": {"comment":"HL = the line, D = the statement"},
        "7637": {"comment":"Jump there"},
        "7640": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 0 (report 1, \"NEXT without FOR\")."},
        "7642": {"synopsis":"Carry when the loop is over: the value past the limit, above it for a step of 0 or more,\nbelow it for a negative step. Uses the variable at MEM: memory 0 the value, 1 the limit, 2\nthe step.","comment":"Limit, value and step: past the limit?"},
        "7655": {"comment":"No carry: not over"},
        "7657": {"synopsis":"The end-calc ($38) the jump-true at $1DE4 lands on: the calculator ends here and the Z80\ngoes on at NEXT_LOOP_OVER."},
        "7658": {"synopsis":"The loop is over: carry set."},
        "7660": {"synopsis":"The next READ item: past the ','.","comment":"Past the ','"},
        "7661": {"synopsis":"READ: for each variable (CLASS_1), when running, the next DATA item: the one at DATADD after\na ',', or the first of the next DATA statement (LOOK_PROG for $E4); none is report E. It is\nevaluated with the variable's type and assigned (VAL_FETCH), and DATADD moves past it;\nCH_ADD comes back to the READ statement (kept in X_PTR).\nObserved: 10 READ a,b$: PRINT a;b$: READ c / 20 DATA 5,\"q\" printed 5q and then gave \"E Out\nof DATA, 10:3\".","comment":"The variable"},
        "7664": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "7667": {"comment":"Yes: on to the next ','"},
        "7669": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "7670": {"comment":"X_PTR = it, the READ statement's place"},
        "7673": {"comment":"HL = DATADD"},
        "7676": {"comment":"The byte there"},
        "7677": {"comment":"','?"},
        "7679": {"comment":"Yes: the item after it"},
        "7681": {"comment":"E = DATA's token"},
        "7683": {"comment":"The next DATA statement"},
        "7686": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "7688": {"comment":"No DATA left: report E"},
        "7690": {"synopsis":"The item: CH_ADD just past DATADD's byte, VAL_FETCH; DATADD = after it.","comment":"CH_ADD past it: the item"},
        "7693": {"comment":"Evaluated and assigned"},
        "7696": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "7697": {"comment":"DATADD = it, past the item"},
        "7700": {"comment":"HL = X_PTR"},
        "7703": {"comment":"X_PTR's high byte = 0: unused"},
        "7707": {"comment":"CH_ADD back in the READ statement"},
        "7710": {"synopsis":"',': another variable; otherwise the statement ends.","comment":"The current character"},
        "7711": {"comment":"','?"},
        "7713": {"comment":"Yes: another variable"},
        "7715": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "7719": {"synopsis":"DATA: checking, each item is an expression (SCAN_EXPR) up to the end of the statement;\nrunning, the statement is skipped (DATA_RUN).","comment":"Checking?"},
        "7722": {"comment":"No: skipped"},
        "7724": {"synopsis":"One item, then ',' or the statement's end.","comment":"An item"},
