        "7911": {"comment":"ERR_SP = it"},
        "7915": {"comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "7916": {"comment":"Return"},
        "7917": {"synopsis":"GO SUB: keeps the place to return to below the ERR_SP slot: the next statement (SUBPPC + 1,\none byte) and the line (PPC); the error address goes back on top and ERR_SP moves down to\nit. Then GO TO, and room for 20 more bytes must be left (GO_SUB_ROOM, report 4).\nObserved: 10 GO SUB 100: PRINT \"b\" / 20 STOP / 100 PRINT \"a\";: RETURN printed ab.","comment":"DE = the return address"},
        "7918": {"comment":"H = SUBPPC"},
        "7921": {"comment":"The statement after GO SUB"},
        "7922": {"comment":"HL = the error address; H and L stacked"},
        "7923": {"comment":"Only the statement's byte stays"},
        "7924": {"comment":"BC = PPC"},
        "7928": {"comment":"The line"},
        "7929": {"comment":"The error address"},
        "7930": {"comment":"ERR_SP = it"},
        "7934": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "7935": {"comment":"GO TO the line"},
        "7938": {"synopsis":"TEST_ROOM with BC = 20.","comment":"20 bytes"},
        "7941": {"synopsis":"Checks that BC more bytes fit: STKEND + BC + $50 must stay below the machine stack. Returns\nwith carry when they do; stops with report 4 otherwise (NO_ROOM).\nChanges: F, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "7944": {"comment":"Plus BC"},
