        "8438": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 7 clear: not LINE"},
        "8442": {"synopsis":"Running: the answer is edited in the workspace. FLAGX bit 5 set (INPUT), bit 6 for a number.\nA string (not LINE) starts as \"\" with the cursor between the quotes; otherwise the answer\nstarts empty, just its ENTER.\nObserved: waiting for INPUT n, the workspace held 0D and FLAGX $62; for INPUT a$, 22 22 0D\nwith the cursor on the second quote and FLAGX $22; for INPUT LINE b$, 0D and FLAGX $A2.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "8445": {"comment":"Then the next item"},
        "8448": {"comment":"The workspace emptied"},
        "8451": {"comment":"HL = FLAGX"},
        "8454": {"comment":"Bit 6 clear"},
        "8456": {"comment":"Bit 5: INPUT mode"},
        "8458": {"comment":"One byte: the ENTER"},
        "8461": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "8463": {"comment":"Then no type, no quotes"},
        "8465": {"comment":"A = FLAGS"},
        "8468": {"comment":"Bit 6: a number"},
        "8470": {"comment":"A number: only the ENTER"},
        "8472": {"comment":"A string: the quotes too"},
        "8474": {"synopsis":"FLAGX bit 6 = FLAGS bit 6: a number answer.","comment":"FLAGX bit 6 from FLAGS bit 6"},
        "8475": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "8476": {"synopsis":"Room for the answer (WORK_ROOM), its ENTER, and the quotes for a string.","comment":"BC bytes made: DE = the first, HL = the last"},
        "8477": {"comment":"The last one ENTER"},
        "8479": {"comment":"A = the byte count"},
        "8480": {"comment":"Bit 1 into carry"},
        "8482": {"comment":"No carry: no quotes"},
        "8484": {"comment":"A quote"},
        "8486": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "8487": {"comment":"HL back one"},
        "8488": {"comment":"A quote before the ENTER"},
        "8489": {"synopsis":"K_CUR = the cursor's place. LINE: the editor at once (INPUT_LINE_EDIT).","comment":"K_CUR = HL, the cursor's place"},
        "8492": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 7: LINE?"},
        "8496": {"comment":"Yes: the editor only"},
        "8498": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "8501": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "8502": {"comment":"HL = ERR_SP"},
        "8505": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "8506": {"synopsis":"Where an error in the answer returns (its address is pushed here): the answer is edited\nagain. When the channel is K, ERR_SP points at this return.\nObserved: the answer ! was shown again with the ? marker.","comment":"HL = this address"},
        "8509": {"comment":"Pushed: an error comes back here"},
        "8510": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 4: channel K?"},
        "8514": {"comment":"No: ERR_SP kept"},
        "8516": {"comment":"ERR_SP = this return"},
        "8520": {"synopsis":"The answer's hidden numbers removed (STRIP_NUMBERS), ERR_NR = $FF, the editor (EDITOR); then\nthe answer checked as an expression of the right type (IN_ASSIGN with FLAGS bit 7 clear).","comment":"HL = WORKSP, the answer"},
        "8523": {"comment":"Its hidden numbers removed"},
        "8526": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF, no error"},
        "8530": {"comment":"The answer edited"},
        "8533": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 clear: checking"},
        "8537": {"comment":"The answer checked"},
        "8540": {"comment":"On"},
        "8542": {"synopsis":"INPUT LINE: the editor only.","comment":"The answer edited"},
        "8545": {"synopsis":"K_CUR's high byte 0 (no cursor), and on channel K the answer shown again (EDIT_LINE_SHOW),\nthe position after it.","comment":"K_CUR high byte 0: no cursor"},
        "8549": {"comment":"Channel K?"},
        "8552": {"comment":"No: not shown again"},
        "8554": {"comment":"The answer shown"},
        "8557": {"comment":"BC = ECHO_E, the position after it"},
        "8561": {"comment":"The print position set there"},
        "8564": {"synopsis":"FLAGX bits 5 and 7 cleared. INPUT LINE: the workspace's text is the string (INPUT_LINE_STR).\nOtherwise the answer is evaluated and assigned (IN_ASSIGN running), CH_ADD back in the INPUT\nstatement (kept in X_PTR meanwhile).","comment":"HL = FLAGX"},
        "8567": {"comment":"Bit 5 clear: INPUT mode over"},
        "8569": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "8571": {"comment":"Bit 7 cleared"},
        "8573": {"comment":"LINE: the text as a string"},
        "8575": {"comment":"INPUT_RETRY dropped"},
        "8576": {"comment":"HL = the old ERR_SP"},
        "8577": {"comment":"ERR_SP back"},
        "8580": {"comment":"HL = the INPUT statement's CH_ADD"},
        "8581": {"comment":"Kept in X_PTR"},
        "8584": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 set: running"},
        "8588": {"comment":"The answer evaluated and assigned"},
        "8591": {"comment":"HL = X_PTR"},
        "8594": {"comment":"X_PTR's high byte 0: cleared"},
        "8598": {"comment":"CH_ADD back in the statement"},
        "8601": {"comment":"The next item"},
        "8603": {"synopsis":"The answer as a string: WORKSP to STKBOT - 1, stacked (STK_STO_STR) and assigned\n(LET_ASSIGN).\nObserved: INPUT LINE b$ answered 1+2 printed 1+2!.","comment":"HL = STKBOT"},
        "8606": {"comment":"DE = WORKSP"},
        "8610": {"comment":"Less one: the ENTER left out"},
        "8611": {"comment":"HL = the text's length"},
        "8613": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "8615": {"comment":"Stacked as a string"},
        "8618": {"comment":"Assigned to the variable"},
        "8621": {"comment":"The next item"},
        "8623": {"synopsis":"A prompt item (PRINT_ITEM).","comment":"The prompt item printed"},
        "8626": {"synopsis":"After a separator, the next item; otherwise INPUT is done.","comment":"A separator?"},
        "8629": {"comment":"Yes: the next item"},
        "8632": {"comment":"No: INPUT done"},
        "8633": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the answer in the workspace (CH_ADD = WORKSP) with the type in FLAGX bit 6 and\nassigns it (VAL_FETCH_A); it must end with ENTER, else report C. STOP as the answer is\nreport H when running.","comment":"HL = WORKSP"},
        "8636": {"comment":"CH_ADD = the answer's start"},
        "8639": {"comment":"Its first character"},
        "8640": {"comment":"STOP?"},
        "8642": {"comment":"Yes: report H when running"},
        "8644": {"comment":"A = FLAGX: the type in bit 6"},
        "8647": {"comment":"The answer evaluated and assigned"},
        "8650": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "8651": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "8653": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8654": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "8656": {"synopsis":"STOP: report H (error code $10) when running.\nObserved: STOP answered to INPUT n gave \"H STOP in INPUT, 10:1\".","comment":"Checking?"},
        "8659": {"comment":"Then no error"},
        "8660": {"comment":"Report H"},
        "8662": {"synopsis":"Z when the current channel is K (its letter, CURCHL + 4).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"HL = CURCHL"},
        "8665": {"comment":"Four bytes on"},
        "8669": {"comment":"A = the channel's letter"},
        "8670": {"comment":"'K'?"},
        "8673": {"synopsis":"Past a ';' or ','; then the next colour item.","comment":"Past the separator"},
        "8674": {"synopsis":"The colour items a PLOT, DRAW or CIRCLE statement may start with (INK 2; PAPER 6; ...): each\nby PRINT_COLOUR, separated by ';' or ','; anything else that is not a colour item is report\nC. Returns at the first item that is not a colour item.\nObserved: PLOT INK 2;PAPER 6;30,30 gave the cell the attribute $32 and left ATTR_P $38.","comment":"A colour item?"},
        "8677": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "8678": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "8679": {"comment":"','?"},
