        "8917": {"comment":"Until the pixel is in bit 0"},
        "8919": {"comment":"Only that bit"},
        "8921": {"comment":"Stacked: 1 or 0"},
        "8924": {"synopsis":"PLOT: the pixel at x, y (TAKE_TWO_BYTES, PLOT_SUB), then the temporary colours back\n(COLOURS_TO_TEMP).\nObserved: PLOT 0,0 lit the bottom left pixel; PLOT 0,176 gave report B.","comment":"C = x, B = y"},
        "8927": {"comment":"The pixel plotted"},
        "8930": {"comment":"The temporary colours back"},
        "8933": {"synopsis":"Plots pixel x = C, y = B: COORDS = them; the pixel set, or with OVER 1 (P_FLAG bit 0)\ntoggled, or with INVERSE 1 (bit 2) cleared, or with both left as it is; then the cell's\nattribute (OUT_ATTR).\nObserved: PLOT 3,0 then PLOT OVER 1;3,0 left it clear; PLOT INVERSE 1;3,0 cleared it.","comment":"COORDS = x, y"},
        "8937": {"comment":"HL = the byte, A = the place"},
        "8940": {"comment":"B = the place + 1"},
        "8942": {"comment":"A mask with bit 0 clear"},
