        "8991": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8992": {"synopsis":"CIRCLE x,y,r (the colour items and x, y by CLASS_9): r = |r|. Under 1 it plots x, y only.\nOtherwise the circle is drawn as chords: CHORD_COUNT picks their number from the radius (a\nmultiple of 4, at most 252) and the rotation from one to the next (memories 3 and 4); the\nfirst point is set in COORDS and ARC_LOOP draws them with DRAW_LINE.\nObserved: CIRCLE 128,88,40 lit (168,88), (128,128) and (128,48) and left COORDS 168,83;\nCIRCLE 20,20,0.5 plotted (20,20) only.","comment":"The current character"},
        "8993": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8995": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "8998": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8999": {"comment":"The radius"},
        "9002": {"comment":"The statement must end here"},
        "9005": {"comment":"The value r made |r|"},
        "9009": {"comment":"r below 1?"},
        "9010": {"comment":"Exponent $81 or more: r 1 or more?"},
        "9012": {"comment":"Yes: the circle"},
        "9014": {"comment":"The value r dropped"},
        "9017": {"comment":"Only x, y plotted (PLOT_CMD)"},
        "9019": {"synopsis":"The angle, memory 5 = 2 x pi (pi/2 with its exponent set to $83); CHORD_COUNT.","comment":"Pi / 2 stacked"},
        "9022": {"comment":"pi/2 x 4: 2 x pi"},
        "9024": {"comment":"Memory 5 = 2 x pi"},
