        "9095": {"comment":"The statement must end here"},
        "9098": {"comment":"A straight line"},
        "9101": {"synopsis":"DRAW's angle a: memory 5 = a; sin(a/2) = 0 (a = 0, a multiple of 2 pi) is a straight line;\notherwise DRAW_ARC_CALC goes on with the arc's size.","comment":"Past the ','"},
        "9102": {"comment":"The angle"},
        "9105": {"comment":"The statement must end here"},
        "9108": {"comment":"Memory 5 = a; sin(a / 2) tested"},
        "9120": {"comment":"Zero: a straight line"},
        "9123": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $239C lands on, so the listing cannot decode them after\nRST $28: st-mem-0, delete, st-mem-1, delete, duplicate, abs, get-mem-1, exchange, get-mem-1,\nabs, addition, get-mem-0, division, abs, get-mem-0, exchange, re-stack, end-calc. The Z80\ngoes on at DRAW_ARC_SIZE."},
        "9141": {"synopsis":"A short arc (the value's exponent below $81): a straight line instead (LINE_DRAW).","comment":"A = the value's exponent"},
        "9142": {"comment":"Below $81: under 1?"},
        "9144": {"comment":"No: an arc"},
        "9146": {"comment":"Two values dropped"},
        "9150": {"comment":"A straight line"},
        "9153": {"synopsis":"The arc's chords: CHORD_COUNT for their number, the first chord and the start point in the\nmemories; then ARC_START with the first.","comment":"The chords' count"},
        "9156": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "9157": {"comment":"The first chord and the start point"},
        "9213": {"comment":"A = the deleted value's exponent"},
        "9214": {"comment":"Below $81: under 1?"},
        "9216": {"comment":"B = the chord count back"},
        "9217": {"comment":"Under 1 (exponent below $81): a straight line"},
        "9224": {"comment":"A = COORDS x"},
        "9227": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9235": {"comment":"A = COORDS y"},
        "9238": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9247": {"comment":"B = the chord count back"},
        "9248": {"synopsis":"The chords one by one: B counts them; the last goes to the exact end (ARC_END).","comment":"One chord fewer"},
        "9249": {"comment":"Only one: ARC_END"},
        "9251": {"comment":"Otherwise the first chord (ARC_START)"},
        "9253": {"synopsis":"The next chord: its (x, y) rotated by the step (memories 3 and 4: cos and sin), into\nmemories 1 and 2."},
        "9273": {"synopsis":"The chord's end in pixels, relative to COORDS, then DRAW_LINE.","comment":"Count kept"},
        "9281": {"comment":"A = COORDS x"},
        "9284": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9296": {"comment":"A = COORDS y"},
        "9299": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9305": {"comment":"The chord drawn (DRAW_LINE)"},
        "9309": {"comment":"The next chord, until the last"},
        "9311": {"synopsis":"The last chord: to the arc's end point exactly, from COORDS."},
        "9316": {"comment":"A = COORDS x"},
        "9319": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9326": {"comment":"A = COORDS y"},
        "9329": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9335": {"synopsis":"A straight line (DRAW_LINE), then the temporary colours back (COLOURS_TO_TEMP).","comment":"The line drawn (DRAW_LINE)"},
        "9338": {"comment":"Then COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "9341": {"synopsis":"The number of chords for an arc or circle: from the size on the calculator stack, rounded\ndown to a multiple of 4 and plus 4, at most $FC (CHORD_COUNT_MAX), stacked; then the angle\n(memory 5) per chord: memory 4 = sin(a/n), memory 3 = cos(a/n), memory 1 = sin(a/2n).\nExit: B = the number."},
        "9354": {"comment":"A = the size (FP_TO_BYTE)"},
        "9357": {"comment":"Over 255: the most"},
        "9359": {"comment":"Down to a multiple of 4"},
        "9361": {"comment":"Plus 4"},
        "9363": {"comment":"Not past 255: kept"},
        "9365": {"synopsis":"At most $FC chords."},
        "9367": {"synopsis":"A = the number, kept and stacked; the memories from it."},
        "9368": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9397": {"comment":"B = the number"},
        "9399": {"synopsis":"Draws a straight line from COORDS by x, y (TAKE_TWO_BYTES: C = |x|, B = |y|, E and D their\nsigns): along the longer of the two a pixel at a time, a step along the shorter one each\ntime the running sum passes the longer, each pixel by PLOT_SUB. A point off the screen is\nreport B.\nObserved: DRAW 250,0 from 10,10 stopped at x 255 with report B.","comment":"C = |x|, B = |y|; E, D their signs"},
        "9402": {"comment":"A = |x|"},
        "9403": {"comment":"Smaller than |y|?"},
        "9404": {"comment":"No: DL_X_LARGER"},
        "9406": {"comment":"L = |x|, the shorter"},
        "9407": {"comment":"Both signs kept, for a diagonal step"},
        "9409": {"comment":"E = 0: no x step on a straight one"},
        "9410": {"comment":"To DL_STEPS"},
        "9412": {"synopsis":"|x| the larger: it counts the steps (nothing at all for 0, 0).","comment":"|x| 0 too?"},
        "9413": {"comment":"Then nothing to draw"},
        "9414": {"comment":"L = |y|, the shorter"},
        "9415": {"comment":"B = |x|, the longer"},
        "9416": {"comment":"Both signs kept, for a diagonal step"},
        "9417": {"comment":"D = 0: no y step on a straight one"},
        "9419": {"synopsis":"H = the steps, B the count; the running sum starts at half of them.","comment":"H = the longer"},
        "9421": {"comment":"Halved: the sum's start"},
        "9422": {"synopsis":"One step: the sum plus the shorter side; past the longer side, a diagonal step.","comment":"Plus the shorter"},
        "9423": {"comment":"Past 255: a diagonal step"},
        "9425": {"comment":"Below the longer?"},
        "9426": {"comment":"Yes: a straight step"},
        "9428": {"synopsis":"A diagonal step: both signs (BC').","comment":"The longer taken off"},
        "9429": {"comment":"C = the sum"},
        "9430": {"comment":"The alternate set"},
        "9431": {"comment":"BC' = both signs"},
        "9432": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "9435": {"synopsis":"A straight step: the longer axis's sign only.","comment":"C = the sum"},
        "9436": {"comment":"The straight step's signs"},
        "9438": {"comment":"BC' = them"},
        "9439": {"synopsis":"The new point: COORDS + the step; an x off the screen is report B (DL_RANGE), a y off it is\nPIXEL_BYTE's report B.","comment":"HL = COORDS: L = x, H = y"},
        "9442": {"comment":"The y step"},
        "9443": {"comment":"Plus y"},
        "9444": {"comment":"B = the new y"},
        "9445": {"comment":"The x step"},
        "9446": {"comment":"Plus 1, so that x = -1 gives 0"},
        "9447": {"comment":"Plus x"},
        "9448": {"comment":"Carry: x past 254"},
        "9450": {"comment":"Zero: x = -1, report B"},
        "9452": {"synopsis":"Plots it (PLOT_SUB) and on to the next step.","comment":"Back to the new x"},
        "9453": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "9454": {"comment":"PLOT_SUB"},
        "9457": {"comment":"The main set back"},
        "9458": {"comment":"A = the sum"},
        "9459": {"comment":"The next step, until B is 0"},
        "9461": {"comment":"The signs dropped"},
        "9463": {"synopsis":"Report B unless the point is in range.","comment":"Zero: x = 255, in range"},
        "9465": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B, \"Integer out of range\"); TAKE_BYTE_SIGN jumps here for\na number over 255."},
        "9467": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the expression at CH_ADD, by operator priority, checking (FLAGS bit 7 clear) or\nrunning. Leaves FLAGS bit 6 set for a number, clear for a string, and when running the value\non the calculator stack; CH_ADD at the character after it.\n1. A 0 priority goes on the machine stack: the bottom of the pending operations.\n2. SCAN_OPERAND reads an operand, or a prefix (unary minus, NOT, a function) that pushes its\n   operation and reads the next operand.\n3. SCAN_OPERATOR takes the operator after it (OPERATORS, PRIORITIES); every pending\n   operation of no lower priority runs first, then the new one is pushed and the next\n   operand read. A character that is not an operator has priority 0: everything pending runs\n   and the expression ends.\nObserved: 2+3*4 printed 14, 2^3^2 64, -2^2 -4, NOT 1=0 1, \"ab\"+\"cd\" abcd, \"a\"<\"b\" 1; \"ab\"*2\nwas refused with ? before the '*'.","comment":"A = the first character (GET_CHAR)"},
        "9468": {"comment":"Priority 0"},
        "9470": {"comment":"The bottom of the pending operations"},
        "9471": {"synopsis":"Reads an operand: its first character looked up in SCAN_FUNCS (TABLE_LOOKUP); a quote,\nbracket, number, RND, PI, INKEY$, SCREEN$, ATTR, POINT, FN or unary plus goes to its routine\nthere; anything else to OP_ALNUM.","comment":"C = the character"},
        "9472": {"comment":"HL = SCAN_FUNCS"},
        "9475": {"comment":"Looked up (TABLE_LOOKUP)"},
        "9479": {"comment":"Not there: OP_ALNUM"},
        "9485": {"comment":"HL = its routine"},
        "9486": {"comment":"To it"},
        "9487": {"synopsis":"Inside a string: the next character (NEXT_CHAR), BC + 1; ENTER before the closing quote is\nreport C. Returns at the closing quote with Z when another quote follows (a doubled quote\ninside the string).","comment":"The next character (NEXT_CHAR)"},
        "9491": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "9493": {"comment":"Then report C: no closing quote"},
        "9496": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "9500": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9503": {"comment":"Another quote?"},
        "9506": {"synopsis":"The \"(x,y)\" of SCREEN$, ATTR and POINT: two numbers (NEXT_2NUM) and ')', else report C; then\nSYNTAX_Z, so NZ when running.","comment":"Past the keyword"},
        "9507": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "9509": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "9511": {"comment":"Two numbers (NEXT_2NUM)"},
        "9514": {"comment":"A = the character after them"},
        "9515": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "9517": {"synopsis":"Report C unless Z (the ')'); then SYNTAX_Z."},
        "9520": {"synopsis":"Z when checking syntax (FLAGS bit 7 clear), NZ when running.\nChanges: F.","comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "9525": {"synopsis":"SCREEN$'s value: compares the cell at line C, column B (TAKE_TWO_BYTES) with the 96\ncharacters of the character set, row by row, plain or inverted. A match gives a\none-character string (WORK_ROOM), none an empty one; stacked by STK_STO_STR.\nObserved: \"Q\" printed at 0,0 gave SCREEN$ (0,0) = \"Q\".","comment":"C = the line, B = the column"},
        "9528": {"comment":"HL = CHARS"},
        "9531": {"comment":"DE = 256"},
        "9534": {"comment":"HL = the space's pattern"},
        "9535": {"comment":"A = the line"},
        "9536": {"comment":"Rotated right 3 times"},
        "9539": {"comment":"Its low 3 bits, times 32"},
        "9541": {"comment":"Plus the column"},
        "9542": {"comment":"E = the cell's low byte"},
        "9544": {"comment":"Its third of the screen"},
        "9546": {"comment":"In the screen, $4000 up"},
        "9548": {"comment":"D = the high byte"},
        "9549": {"comment":"96 characters to try"},
        "9551": {"synopsis":"One character: its 8 rows against the cell's."},
        "9554": {"comment":"The cell's top row"},
        "9555": {"comment":"Against the pattern's"},
        "9556": {"comment":"Same: a plain match so far"},
        "9558": {"comment":"Every bit different ($FF)?"},
        "9559": {"comment":"No: not this character"},
        "9561": {"comment":"A = $FF: an inverted match"},
        "9562": {"synopsis":"The first row matched (C = 0) or matched inverted (C = $FF): the other 7 must match the same\nway.","comment":"C = 0 or $FF"},
        "9563": {"comment":"7 more rows"},
        "9565": {"synopsis":"The next row: the screen's 256 bytes on, the pattern's 1.","comment":"The screen's next row"},
        "9566": {"comment":"The pattern's next row"},
        "9567": {"comment":"A = the screen's row"},
        "9568": {"comment":"Against the pattern's"},
        "9569": {"comment":"Inverted as the first?"},
        "9570": {"comment":"Differs: not this character"},
        "9572": {"comment":"All 7 rows"},
        "9576": {"comment":"B = the count left"},
        "9577": {"comment":"A = $80"},
        "9579": {"comment":"Less the count: the character's code"},
        "9580": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "9583": {"comment":"Room for it (WORK_ROOM)"},
        "9584": {"comment":"The character in it"},
        "9585": {"comment":"Stacked (SCR_STACK)"},
        "9587": {"synopsis":"No match: the next character, 8 bytes on."},
        "9588": {"comment":"DE = 8"},
        "9591": {"comment":"HL = the next character's pattern"},
        "9594": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "9596": {"comment":"BC = 0: an empty string"},
        "9597": {"synopsis":"Stacks the string (STK_STO_STR): BC = its length, 0 or 1."},
        "9600": {"synopsis":"ATTR's value: the attribute byte of line C, column B (TAKE_TWO_BYTES), stacked (STACK_A).\nObserved: ATTR (0,0) gave 56.","comment":"C = the line, B = the column"},
        "9604": {"comment":"Rotated right 3 times"},
        "9607": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "9608": {"comment":"Its low 3 bits, times 32"},
        "9610": {"comment":"Plus the column"},
        "9611": {"comment":"L = the address's low byte"},
        "9613": {"comment":"Its bits 3-4: the third"},
        "9615": {"comment":"In the attributes, $5800 up"},
        "9617": {"comment":"H = the high byte"},
        "9618": {"comment":"A = the attribute"},
        "9619": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9622": {"synopsis":"Operand table for SCAN_OPERAND (TABLE_LOOKUP): 12 (character, offset) pairs and a 0: '\"'\nOP_QUOTE, '(' OP_BRACKET, '.' OP_NUMBER, '+' OP_PLUS, FN OP_FN, RND OP_RND, PI OP_PI, INKEY$\nOP_INKEY, BIN OP_NUMBER, SCREEN$ OP_SCREEN, ATTR OP_ATTR, POINT OP_POINT. Each offset counts\nfrom its own byte."},
        "9647": {"synopsis":"A unary plus: skipped.","comment":"Past the '+'"},
        "9648": {"comment":"The operand after it (SCAN_OPERAND)"},
        "9651": {"synopsis":"A string in quotes: its length counted to the closing quote (QUOTE_NEXT), a doubled quote\nstanding for one quote. When running it is copied into the workspace (WORK_ROOM), the\ndoubled quotes made single, and stacked (STRING_RESULT).\nObserved: \"say \"\"hi\"\"\" printed say \"hi\".","comment":"HL = CH_ADD, the opening quote"},
        "9652": {"comment":"HL = the string's first character"},
        "9654": {"comment":"BC counts the characters"},
        "9657": {"comment":"To the closing quote (QUOTE_NEXT)"},
        "9660": {"comment":"Not doubled: the string's end"},
        "9662": {"synopsis":"Past a doubled quote: on to the next.","comment":"To the next closing quote"},
        "9665": {"comment":"Doubled again?"},
        "9667": {"comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "9670": {"comment":"Then no copy"},
        "9672": {"comment":"BC bytes of room (WORK_ROOM)"},
        "9673": {"comment":"HL = the first character"},
        "9674": {"comment":"The room's start kept"},
        "9675": {"synopsis":"Copies the string's characters; a doubled quote is copied once."},
        "9679": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "9683": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9685": {"comment":"Another quote (doubled)?"},
        "9687": {"comment":"Yes: copied once, on"},
        "9689": {"synopsis":"BC - 1: the closing quote not counted."},
        "9690": {"comment":"DE = the start (the room's when running)"},
        "9691": {"synopsis":"A string result: FLAGS bit 6 cleared; when running STK_STO_STR stacks DE, BC. Then\nSCAN_OPERATOR.","comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "9694": {"comment":"Bit 6 clear: a string"},
        "9696": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "9698": {"comment":"Then stacked (STK_STO_STR)"},
        "9701": {"comment":"To SCAN_OPERATOR"},
        "9704": {"synopsis":"A bracket: the expression inside (SCAN_EXPR) and ')', else report C.","comment":"Past the '('"},
        "9705": {"comment":"The expression inside (SCAN_EXPR)"},
        "9708": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "9710": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "9714": {"comment":"To SCAN_OPERATOR"},
        "9717": {"synopsis":"FN: FN_CALL."},
        "9720": {"synopsis":"RND, when running: SEED = (SEED + 1) x 75 mod 65537 - 1, and the value is SEED / 65536 (the\nexponent of the copy lowered by 16).\nObserved: from SEED 0, RND gave 0.0011291504 and left SEED 74.","comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "9723": {"comment":"Then only past RND"},
        "9725": {"comment":"BC = SEED"},
        "9729": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_BC)"},
        "9751": {"comment":"BC = the new SEED (FP_TO_BC)"},
        "9754": {"comment":"SEED = it"},
        "9758": {"comment":"A = the copy's exponent"},
        "9759": {"comment":"Zero (the value 0)?"},
        "9760": {"comment":"Then left as it is"},
        "9762": {"comment":"Divided by 65536"},
        "9764": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "9765": {"synopsis":"To OP_NUM_NEXT."},
        "9767": {"synopsis":"PI, when running: pi/2 from the calculator's constants, its exponent + 1.\nObserved: PRINT PI gave 3.1415927.","comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "9770": {"comment":"Then only past PI"},
        "9775": {"comment":"Exponent + 1: times 2"},
        "9776": {"synopsis":"Past the keyword; a number (SET_NUMERIC)."},
        "9780": {"synopsis":"INKEY$: with '#' a function of the stream (PUSH_PREFIX, operation $1A). Otherwise, when\nrunning, the key held now (READ_KEYS, KEY_MAIN_CODE, KEY_DECODE in L mode, MODE 0, so a\nletter gives a letter, never a keyword) as a one-character string, or an empty one.\nObserved: with no key, PRINT \"[\";INKEY$;\"]\" printed [].","comment":"Priority 16, operation $5A"},
        "9783": {"comment":"Past INKEY$"},
        "9784": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "9786": {"comment":"Then a function of the stream (PUSH_PREFIX)"},
        "9789": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "9792": {"comment":"Bit 6 clear: a string"},
        "9794": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "9796": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9798": {"comment":"The keys held (READ_KEYS)"},
        "9801": {"comment":"C = 0: an empty string so far"},
        "9803": {"comment":"Too many keys: empty"},
        "9805": {"comment":"Its main code (KEY_MAIN_CODE)"},
        "9808": {"comment":"No key: empty"},
        "9810": {"comment":"D = $FF: bit 3 set, L mode"},
        "9811": {"comment":"E = the main code"},
        "9812": {"comment":"The key's code (KEY_DECODE, MODE 0)"},
        "9816": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "9819": {"comment":"Room for it (WORK_ROOM)"},
        "9821": {"comment":"Into the room"},
        "9822": {"comment":"C = 1: one character"},
        "9824": {"synopsis":"Stacks the string (STK_STO_STR): C = its length."},
        "9826": {"comment":"Stacked (STK_STO_STR)"},
        "9829": {"synopsis":"To SCAN_OPERATOR."},
        "9832": {"synopsis":"SCREEN$ (x,y): TWO_COORDS, SCREENS_VALUE when running; a string.","comment":"The (x,y) (TWO_COORDS)"},
        "9835": {"comment":"Running: SCREENS_VALUE"},
        "9839": {"comment":"A string (STRING_RESULT)"},
        "9842": {"synopsis":"ATTR (x,y): TWO_COORDS, ATTR_VALUE when running; a number.","comment":"The (x,y) (TWO_COORDS)"},
        "9845": {"comment":"Running: ATTR_VALUE"},
        "9849": {"comment":"A number (SET_NUMERIC)"},
        "9851": {"synopsis":"POINT (x,y): TWO_COORDS, POINT_SUB when running; a number.","comment":"The (x,y) (TWO_COORDS)"},
        "9854": {"comment":"Running: POINT_SUB"},
        "9858": {"comment":"A number (SET_NUMERIC)"},
        "9860": {"synopsis":"An operand that is not in SCAN_FUNCS: a letter starts a variable (OP_VARIABLE), a digit a\nnumber (OP_NUMBER), anything else is a prefix (OP_PREFIX).","comment":"A letter or a digit (ALPHANUM)?"},
        "9863": {"comment":"No: OP_PREFIX"},
        "9865": {"comment":"From 'A' up: a letter?"},
        "9867": {"comment":"Then OP_VARIABLE"},
        "9869": {"synopsis":"A number in the line (digits, '.', or BIN). Checking: read (READ_NUMBER) and put after the\ndigits in its hidden form, the marker $0E and its 5 bytes, taken off the calculator stack.\nRunning: NUMBER_RUN.\nObserved: 10 PRINT 2.5 was stored with 0E 82 20 00 00 00 after the digits.","comment":"Running?"},
        "9872": {"comment":"Then NUMBER_RUN"},
        "9874": {"comment":"Read onto the calculator stack (READ_NUMBER)"},
        "9877": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD, the character after it"},
        "9878": {"comment":"6 bytes"},
        "9881": {"comment":"Room before it (MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "9884": {"comment":"HL = the room's first byte"},
        "9885": {"comment":"The hidden number's marker"},
        "9887": {"comment":"HL = where the 5 bytes go"},
        "9889": {"comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "9892": {"comment":"BC = 5"},
        "9895": {"comment":"HL = the number's start"},
        "9897": {"comment":"STKEND = it: the number taken off"},
        "9900": {"comment":"The 5 bytes after the marker"},
        "9903": {"comment":"HL = the last of them"},
        "9904": {"comment":"CH_ADD = past it (CH_ADD_PLUS1)"},
        "9907": {"comment":"A number (SET_NUMERIC)"},
        "9909": {"synopsis":"Running: past the digits to the $0E marker, and the hidden 5 bytes copied onto the\ncalculator stack (PUSH_NUMBER).","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "9910": {"synopsis":"The next byte, up to the marker.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "9912": {"comment":"The marker?"},
        "9916": {"comment":"HL = the 5 bytes"},
        "9917": {"comment":"Stacked (PUSH_NUMBER)"},
        "9920": {"comment":"CH_ADD = past them"},
        "9923": {"synopsis":"FLAGS bit 6 set: the operand is a number."},
        "9927": {"comment":"To SCAN_OPERATOR"},
        "9929": {"synopsis":"A variable: LOOK_VARS, report 2 when it is not there; subscripts or slicing\n(VAR_SUBSCRIPTS); a number's 5 bytes are stacked (PUSH_NUMBER) when running.\nObserved: PRINT zz with no zz gave \"2 Variable not found\".","comment":"Found (LOOK_VARS)?"},
        "9932": {"comment":"No: report 2"},
        "9935": {"comment":"A string or an array: VAR_SUBSCRIPTS"},
        "9938": {"comment":"A = FLAGS"},
        "9941": {"comment":"Running, and a number (bits 7, 6)?"},
        "9943": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9945": {"comment":"HL = the value's 5 bytes"},
        "9946": {"comment":"Stacked (PUSH_NUMBER)"},
        "9949": {"synopsis":"To SCAN_OPERATOR."},
        "9951": {"synopsis":"A prefix, pushed with its priority and operation (BC): '-' (9, negate), VAL$ (16), NOT (4);\nthe functions CODE to CHR$ (16, operation code + $DC), whose operand is a string for CODE,\nVAL and LEN (bit 6 clear) and whose result is a string for STR$ and CHR$ (bit 7 clear).\nAnything else is report C.\nObserved: VAL \"2+3\" gave 5, CODE \"A\" 65, LEN \"abc\" 3.","comment":"Priority 9, negate ($DB)"},
        "9954": {"comment":"'-'?"},
        "9956": {"comment":"Then pushed"},
        "9958": {"comment":"Priority 16, VAL$ ($18)"},
        "9961": {"comment":"VAL$?"},
        "9963": {"comment":"Then pushed"},
        "9965": {"comment":"Counted from CODE ($AF)"},
        "9967": {"comment":"Below $AF: not a function"},
        "9970": {"comment":"Priority 4, NOT ($F0)"},
        "9973": {"comment":"NOT ($C3)?"},
        "9975": {"comment":"Then pushed"},
        "9977": {"comment":"Past NOT: report C"},
        "9980": {"comment":"Priority 16"},
        "9982": {"comment":"The operation: + $DC"},
        "9985": {"comment":"Below $DF (CODE, VAL, LEN)?"},
        "9987": {"comment":"No: a number operand"},
        "9989": {"comment":"Yes: a string operand (bit 6 clear)"},
        "9991": {"synopsis":"CHR$ and STR$ ($EE up): a string result (bit 7 cleared).","comment":"STR$ or CHR$ ($EE up)?"},
        "9993": {"comment":"No: a number result"},
        "9995": {"comment":"Yes: a string result"},
        "9997": {"synopsis":"Pushes the prefix BC and reads the next operand (SCAN_OPERAND).","comment":"Pushed"},
        "9999": {"comment":"The operand (SCAN_OPERAND)"},
        "10002": {"synopsis":"The character after an operand: '(' slices a string (STR_SLICE) and is looked at again;\notherwise an operator from OPERATORS, with its priority from PRIORITIES; not an operator:\npriority 0.\nObserved: \"abcde\"(2 TO 3) gave bc.","comment":"A = the character (GET_CHAR)"},
        "10003": {"synopsis":"A '(' after a string: slicing; after a number it ends the operand.","comment":"'('?"},
        "10005": {"comment":"No: an operator?"},
        "10007": {"comment":"After a number?"},
        "10011": {"comment":"Then the operand has ended"},
        "10013": {"comment":"Sliced (STR_SLICE)"},
        "10017": {"comment":"Looked at again"},
        "10019": {"synopsis":"Looks the character up in OPERATORS: C = the operation, B = its priority ($26ED + C); B = 0\nwhen it is not an operator.","comment":"B = 0: priority 0 so far"},
        "10021": {"comment":"C = the character"},
        "10022": {"comment":"HL = OPERATORS"},
        "10025": {"comment":"Looked up (TABLE_LOOKUP)"},
        "10028": {"comment":"Not there: priority 0"},
        "10030": {"comment":"C = the operation"},
        "10031": {"comment":"HL = PRIORITIES less $C3"},
        "10034": {"comment":"Plus the operation"},
        "10035": {"comment":"B = its priority"},
        "10036": {"synopsis":"The pending operation on the machine stack (D = its priority, E = its operation) against the\nnew one (B, C): a lower priority waits (SCAN_OP_PUSH). Otherwise it runs now\n(SCAN_OP_APPLY); when it is the bottom 0, the expression is over (GET_CHAR).","comment":"D, E = the pending one"},
        "10038": {"comment":"Lower than the new one?"},
        "10039": {"comment":"Then it waits (SCAN_OP_PUSH)"},
        "10041": {"comment":"The bottom 0?"},
        "10042": {"comment":"Then done: A = the character (GET_CHAR)"},
        "10046": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "10049": {"comment":"A = the pending operation"},
        "10050": {"comment":"USR ($ED)?"},
        "10052": {"comment":"No: as it is"},
        "10054": {"comment":"On a number?"},
        "10056": {"comment":"Yes: as it is"},
        "10058": {"comment":"USR of a string: $99"},
        "10060": {"synopsis":"Runs the pending operation E: when running, the calculator's operation E AND $3F\n(fp-calc-2); when checking, the operand's type must be what E bit 6 asks (SCAN_OP_CHECK).\nUSR of a string becomes operation $19."},
        "10061": {"comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "10064": {"comment":"Then SCAN_OP_CHECK"},
        "10067": {"comment":"Its calculator code"},
        "10069": {"comment":"B = it, for fp-calc-2"},
        "10073": {"comment":"To SCAN_OP_TYPE"},
        "10075": {"synopsis":"Checking: E bit 6 and FLAGS bit 6 must agree (a number or a string operand), else report C."},
        "10076": {"comment":"Against FLAGS"},
        "10079": {"comment":"Bit 6 different?"},
        "10081": {"synopsis":"Report C: an operand of the wrong type for its operation."},
        "10084": {"synopsis":"The result's type: FLAGS bit 6 = E bit 7 (set: a number). Then the next pending one."},
        "10085": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "10088": {"comment":"A number for now"},
        "10090": {"comment":"Bit 7: a number result?"},
        "10092": {"comment":"Yes: left set"},
        "10094": {"comment":"No: a string"},
        "10096": {"synopsis":"BC back, and the next pending operation (SCAN_OP_LOOP)."},
        "10097": {"comment":"The next pending one"},
        "10099": {"synopsis":"Pushes the new operation and reads the next operand. With a string on its left it becomes\nthe string form (code + 8): + joins strings, AND gives the string or an empty one (its right\noperand a number), and the comparisons compare strings, giving a number; any other operator\nis report C.\nObserved: \"x\" AND 1 gave x, \"x\" AND 0 an empty string.","comment":"The pending one put back"},
        "10100": {"comment":"A = the new operation"},
        "10101": {"comment":"A number on the left?"},
        "10105": {"comment":"Then as it is"},
        "10107": {"comment":"Its calculator code"},
        "10109": {"comment":"The string form: + 8"},
        "10112": {"comment":"AND ($10)?"},
        "10114": {"comment":"No: the others"},
        "10116": {"comment":"Its right operand a number (bit 6)"},
        "10118": {"comment":"Pushed"},
        "10120": {"synopsis":"Below $10: -, *, /, ^ or OR on a string: report C. $17 (+, joining strings) keeps a string\nresult; the comparisons set bit 7 (a number).","comment":"Below $10: report C"},
        "10122": {"comment":"+ ($17)?"},
        "10124": {"comment":"Then a string result"},
        "10126": {"comment":"A comparison: a number result"},
        "10128": {"synopsis":"Pushes BC and reads the next operand (SCAN_OPERAND).","comment":"Pushed"},
        "10129": {"comment":"Past the operator"},
        "10130": {"comment":"The next operand (SCAN_OPERAND)"},
        "10133": {"synopsis":"Operator table for SCAN_OP_LOOKUP (TABLE_LOOKUP): 13 (character or keyword, operation) pairs\nand a 0: + $CF, - $C3, * $C4, / $C5, ^ $C6, = $CE, > $CC, < $CD, <= $C9, >= $CA, <> $CB, OR\n$C7, AND $C8. An operation's bits 0-5 are its calculator code (+ $0F addition, - $03\nsubtract, * $04 multiply, ...); bit 6 set: its operands are numbers; bit 7 set: its result\nis a number."},
        "10160": {"synopsis":"Operator priorities: 13 bytes for operations $C3-$CF, read as $26ED + operation: - 6, * 8, /\n8, ^ 10, OR 2, AND 3, <= >= <> > < = 5, + 6."},
        "10173": {"synopsis":"FN: a call of a function made with DEF FN. Checking: the name, '(' and the arguments (each\nan expression), ')'; the type from the name. Running: FN_RUN.\nObserved: with 10 DEF FN f(x,y)=x*y+1 / 20 DEF FN s$(a$)=a$+\"!\", FN f(3,4) gave 13 and FN\ns$(\"hi\") hi!; FN g(1) gave report P; FN f(1) and FN f(\"a\",2) report Q.","comment":"Running?"},
        "10176": {"comment":"Then FN_RUN"},
        "10178": {"comment":"Past FN"},
        "10179": {"comment":"A letter (ALPHA)?"},
        "10182": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "10185": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "10186": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "10188": {"comment":"Z kept: a string"},
        "10191": {"comment":"Past the '$'"},
        "10192": {"synopsis":"'(' must follow.","comment":"'('?"},
        "10194": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "10196": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "10197": {"comment":"')' at once?"},
        "10199": {"comment":"Then no arguments"},
        "10201": {"synopsis":"One argument (SCAN_EXPR); ',' for another.","comment":"An argument (SCAN_EXPR)"},
