        "10641": {"synopsis":"NZ and no carry: found.","comment":"The name's positions dropped"},
        "10643": {"comment":"No carry: found"},
        "10644": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "10646": {"synopsis":"After LOOK_VARS found a variable at HL (C its name form; C bit 7 set means checking): its\nsubscripts and slices.\n1. A simple string: stacked whole (STK_STO_STR), then any slices.\n2. A number array: each subscript in its range (SUBSCRIPT, report 3) gives the element's\n   offset; HL is left one byte before its 5 bytes.\n3. A string array: the subscripts but the last give a fixed-length string, stacked; a last\n   subscript with TO is a slice. One dimension: the whole array is a fixed-length string.\nChecking, only the syntax: subscripts, TO and the brackets.\nObserved: DIM m(2,3), m(2,3)=6, m(1,2)=4 printed 640, m(3,1) gave report 3; DIM n$(2,3),\nn$(2)=\"xy\" gave \"xy \", n$(2,2) \"y\".","comment":"A = 0"},
        "10647": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "10648": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "10650": {"comment":"Yes: only the syntax"},
        "10652": {"comment":"An array?"},
        "10654": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10656": {"synopsis":"A simple string (bit 7 of its first byte clear): A = 1, its length and start stacked.","comment":"A = 1: a simple string"},
        "10657": {"synopsis":"BC = the length word at HL + 1, DE = the characters after it; stacked (STK_STO_STR); then\nslices (SV_SLICE_Q).","comment":"Past the letter"},
        "10658": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "10661": {"comment":"HL = the first character"},
        "10662": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "10663": {"comment":"STK_STO_STR: stacked"},
        "10666": {"comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "10667": {"comment":"Any slices"},
        "10670": {"synopsis":"An array: B = its number of dimensions. A string array of one dimension is a string\n(SV_STRING); otherwise a '(' must follow (report 3).","comment":"Past the letter and length word"},
        "10673": {"comment":"B = the number of dimensions"},
        "10674": {"comment":"A number array?"},
        "10676": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10678": {"comment":"A string array: one dimension?"},
        "10679": {"comment":"Then the whole array is the string"},
        "10681": {"comment":"DE = the array kept"},
        "10682": {"comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "10683": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "10685": {"comment":"No: report 3"},
        "10687": {"comment":"HL = the array"},
        "10688": {"synopsis":"A number array: the subscripts.","comment":"DE = it, at the dimensions"},
        "10689": {"comment":"To the subscripts"},
        "10691": {"synopsis":"After a subscript: ',' for the next; otherwise, checking, ')' ends a number array's, TO or\n')' a string array's.","comment":"The offset kept"},
        "10692": {"comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
