        "10834": {"synopsis":"Slices the string on the calculator stack (STK_FETCH when running) by the bracket at CH_ADD:\n(a), (a TO b), (TO b), (a TO) or (): the first defaults to 1, the last to the length. An\nempty result (last < first) is fine even out of range; otherwise an index outside 1..length\nis report 3. The slice is stacked again.\nObserved: with a$ = \"hXYlo\", (TO 2) hX, (4 TO) lo, () the whole, (3 TO 2) and (9 TO 2)\nempty; a$(7) gave report 3.","comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "10837": {"comment":"Running: DE = the string, BC = its length"},
