        "11419": {"synopsis":"Reads the number at CH_ADD onto the calculator stack:\n1. BIN and binary digits: up to 16 bits (more is report 6), stacked as BC (STACK_BC).\n2. Decimal: the whole part (DIGITS_TO_FP), a fraction after '.', each digit scaled by the\n   next power of 1/10 (memory 0); a number may start with '.'.\n3. An exponent, E or e with an optional sign and digits (report 6 when too big), applied by\n   e-to-fp.\nObserved: BIN 11111111 255, BIN 1111111111111111 65535; BIN with 17 digits and 1E39 refused\nwhen checking (the ? marker); VAL \"1E3\" 1000.","comment":"BIN?"},
        "11421": {"comment":"No: a decimal number"},
        "11423": {"comment":"DE = 0: the value"},
        "11426": {"synopsis":"The next binary digit: '0' or '1' shifted into DE.","comment":"The next character"},
        "11427": {"comment":"'0' and '1' become 0, the carry set for '0'"},
        "11431": {"comment":"Neither: the end"},
        "11434": {"comment":"The bit: 1 for '1'"},
        "11435": {"comment":"Shifted into the value"},
        "11437": {"comment":"Over 16 bits: report 6"},
        "11443": {"synopsis":"Stacks DE (STACK_BC).","comment":"BC = the value"},
        "11448": {"synopsis":"Decimal: '.' first, or the whole part then an optional '.' and fraction.","comment":"A leading '.'?"},
        "11452": {"comment":"The whole part"},
        "11455": {"comment":"Then a '.'?"},
        "11457": {"comment":"No: an exponent?"},
        "11459": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11460": {"comment":"A digit after it?"},
        "11463": {"comment":"No: an exponent?"},
        "11465": {"comment":"Yes: the fraction"},
        "11467": {"synopsis":"A leading '.': a digit must follow (report C); the whole part is 0.","comment":"Past the '.'"},
        "11468": {"comment":"A digit must follow"},
        "11471": {"synopsis":"Report C.","comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "11477": {"synopsis":"The fraction: memory 0 = 1, divided by 10 for each digit, digit x memory 0 added."},
        "11482": {"synopsis":"One fraction digit (DIGIT_TO_STACK).","comment":"The current character"},
        "11483": {"comment":"A digit stacked?"},
        "11486": {"comment":"No: an exponent?"},
        "11496": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "11499": {"synopsis":"An exponent? E or e.","comment":"E?"},
        "11503": {"comment":"e?"},
        "11505": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "11506": {"synopsis":"B = $FF, made 0 by a '-'.","comment":"B = $FF: a positive exponent"},
        "11508": {"comment":"The character after the E"},
        "11509": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "11513": {"comment":"'-'?"},
        "11517": {"comment":"B = 0: negative"},
        "11518": {"synopsis":"Past the sign."},
        "11519": {"synopsis":"Its digits (a digit must come, report C): read (DIGITS_TO_FP), a byte (FP_TO_BYTE; too big\nis report 6), negated for '-'.","comment":"A digit must follow"},
        "11522": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "11524": {"comment":"The sign kept"},
        "11525": {"comment":"The exponent read"},
        "11528": {"comment":"A = it; carry over 255"},
        "11532": {"comment":"Over 255: report 6"},
        "11535": {"comment":"128 or more?"},
        "11536": {"comment":"Then report 6"},
        "11539": {"comment":"Was the sign '-'?"},
        "11540": {"comment":"No"},
        "11542": {"comment":"Yes: negated"},
        "11544": {"synopsis":"e-to-fp with A."},
        "11547": {"synopsis":"Carry unless A is a digit (\"0\"-\"9\").\nChanges: F.","comment":"Below '0': carry"},
        "11550": {"comment":"Up to '9': carry, flipped below"},
        "11552": {"comment":"Carry when above '9'"},
        "11554": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is not a digit; otherwise the digit stacked (STACK_A)."},
        "11557": {"comment":"Not a digit"},
        "11558": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "11560": {"synopsis":"Stacks A as a number (STACK_BC with BC = A)."},
        "11561": {"comment":"BC = A"},
        "11563": {"synopsis":"Stacks BC as a small integer (positive), IY restored to $5C3A first; HL and DE left at the\ncalculator stack's top (end-calc). No carry.","comment":"IY as the system variables need"},
        "11567": {"comment":"A and E = 0: the exponent and sign bytes"},
        "11569": {"comment":"D = the low byte, C = the high byte"},
        "11571": {"comment":"B = 0, the fifth byte"},
        "11572": {"comment":"The five bytes stacked"},
        "11575": {"comment":"HL and DE to the stack's top"},
        "11577": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "11579": {"synopsis":"Reads a run of digits at CH_ADD as a number: 0, then x 10 + each digit (DIGIT_TO_STACK),\nCH_ADD past them.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "11583": {"comment":"A back"},
        "11584": {"synopsis":"The next digit, or the end.","comment":"A digit stacked?"},
        "11587": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "11594": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "11599": {"synopsis":"e-to-fp ($3C): the number on the stack x 10 ^ A (A a signed byte): memory 0 = 1 for a\nnegative A (divide), 0 for a positive one (multiply); the power 10 squared for each bit of\n|A|, the number multiplied or divided by it where the bit is 1.\nObserved: VAL \"1E3\" 1000; 1.5E-5 printed .000015.","comment":"Bit 7 into the carry"},
        "11600": {"comment":"A as it was"},
        "11601": {"comment":"Positive"},
        "11603": {"comment":"Negative: A = |A|"},
        "11605": {"synopsis":"Memory 0 = the sign (STORE_0_OR_1 at MEMBOT); 10 stacked.","comment":"|A| kept"},
        "11606": {"comment":"HL = memory 0 (MEMBOT)"},
        "11609": {"comment":"Memory 0 = 1 for a negative A (the carry), else 0"},
        "11615": {"comment":"A = |A|"},
        "11616": {"synopsis":"The next bit of |A|: a 1 bit multiplies or divides (memory 0 chooses) by the power.","comment":"The next bit into the carry"},
        "11618": {"comment":"0: no multiply or divide"},
        "11620": {"comment":"The bits left kept"},
        "11629": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $2D68 and the jump at $2D6B land on (the listing cannot\ndecode them after RST $28): division (the negative case), get-mem-1, end-calc. The Z80 goes\non at TENS_BIT_DONE."},
        "11632": {"synopsis":"AF back.","comment":"The bits left back"},
        "11633": {"synopsis":"More bits: the power squared (duplicate, multiply).","comment":"None left: done"},
        "11635": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11643": {"synopsis":"The power deleted."},
        "11647": {"synopsis":"Reads the small integer at HL (5 bytes: 0, the sign $00 or $FF, the value's low and high\nbyte in two's complement, 0): C = the sign, DE = its magnitude (negated back for a negative\nsign). HL at its high byte."},
        "11648": {"comment":"C = the sign"},
        "11650": {"comment":"The low byte"},
        "11651": {"comment":"Negated when the sign is $FF (complemented, +1)"},
        "11655": {"comment":"The high byte, with the borrow"},
        "11657": {"comment":"Complemented for $FF"},
        "11658": {"comment":"DE = the magnitude"},
        "11660": {"synopsis":"SMALL_INT_PUT with C = 0 (positive)."},
        "11662": {"synopsis":"Stores DE with sign C as a small integer at HL (0, C, the value, 0). HL kept.\nObserved: LET v=-5 stored 00 FF FB FF 00; LET z=65535 00 00 FF FF 00."},
        "11663": {"comment":"0: the exponent byte"},
        "11666": {"comment":"The sign"},
        "11668": {"comment":"The low byte, negated when the sign is $FF"},
        "11673": {"comment":"The high byte, with the carry"},
        "11678": {"comment":"The fifth byte 0"},
        "11682": {"synopsis":"Takes the number off the calculator stack into BC, rounded to the nearest whole number (+\n1/2, int, unless it is already a small integer).\nExit: BC = |the value|, A = C; carry when it does not fit 16 bits; Z for positive, NZ for\nnegative."},
        "11684": {"comment":"The top number's exponent byte"},
        "11686": {"comment":"0: a small integer already"},
        "11693": {"synopsis":"Deleted from the stack; its value read (SMALL_INT_GET)."},
        "11696": {"comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "11698": {"comment":"HL = the deleted number"},
        "11699": {"comment":"B = its exponent byte: 0 for a small integer"},
        "11700": {"comment":"C = the sign, DE = the magnitude"},
        "11703": {"comment":"Carry unless B is 0: not a small integer, too big"},
        "11705": {"comment":"Z for a positive number"},
        "11707": {"comment":"BC = the magnitude"},
        "11709": {"comment":"A = C"},
        "11713": {"synopsis":"A = INT (A x log10 2) (0.30103): the decimal digits a binary exponent A stands for.","comment":"D = A"},
        "11714": {"comment":"Its sign into the carry"},
        "11715": {"comment":"E and C = $FF for a negative A"},
        "11718": {"comment":"A and B = 0"},
        "11720": {"comment":"A stacked as a signed small integer"},
        "11733": {"synopsis":"Takes the number off the calculator stack into A (FP_TO_BC). Exit: carry when it is over\n255; Z for positive, NZ for negative."},
        "11736": {"comment":"Over 16 bits"},
        "11737": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "11738": {"comment":"B 0?"},
        "11740": {"comment":"Yes: in range"},
        "11742": {"comment":"Otherwise carry"},
        "11745": {"synopsis":"AF back: in range."},
        "11747": {"synopsis":"Prints the number on top of the calculator stack through the current channel (and takes it\noff):\n1. 0 prints \"0\". A negative number prints '-' (NP_MINUS) and goes on positive.\n2. The whole part becomes decimal digits (BCD, then bytes in memories 3-5 from $5CA1); a\n   large one is first scaled down (LOG10_ESTIMATE, e-to-fp); then the fraction's digits (x\n   10, MUL10_ADD): at most 8 significant digits, rounded on the ninth (NP_ROUND).\n3. Plainly (NP_PLAIN) when the decimal point's place is from -4 to 8: \"0\" before the point\n   only when the first digit follows it; otherwise in E form, one digit, '.', the rest, E,\n   the exponent's sign and digits (NP_E_FORM).\nObserved: 1E9 1E+9, 123456789 1.2345679E+8, 12345678 12345678, .0001 .0001, .001 .001, .5\n0.5, -.5 -0.5, 1.5E-5 .000015, 2E10 2E+10, 1/7 0.14285714, 0 and -0 0, 1E38 1E+38."},
        "11758": {"comment":"Zero: '0'"},
        "11762": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $2DE6 lands on for a negative number: abs, end-calc. The\nZ80 goes on at NP_MINUS."},
        "11764": {"synopsis":"Prints '-'; then the calculator again, memories 3-5 cleared.","comment":"'-'"},
        "11774": {"comment":"HL' kept"},
        "11777": {"synopsis":"Splits the number: the whole part (INT) left on the stack, the fraction in memory 2."},
        "11787": {"comment":"The whole part's exponent byte"},
        "11789": {"comment":"Not a small integer: a large number"},
        "11791": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "11794": {"comment":"16 bits"},
        "11796": {"comment":"A high byte?"},
        "11800": {"comment":"The low byte 0 too?"},
        "11801": {"comment":"No whole part"},
        "11803": {"comment":"Only a low byte: moved up, 8 bits"},
        "11806": {"synopsis":"A small whole part: its 16 (or 8) bits into the BCD buffer.","comment":"D'E' = the bits"},
        "11810": {"comment":"Into the BCD buffer"},
        "11812": {"synopsis":"No whole part: the fraction scaled up by a power of ten (LOG10_ESTIMATE, e-to-fp), the place\ncounted in $5CAC."},
        "11815": {"comment":"The fraction's exponent byte"},
        "11816": {"comment":"Less $7E"},
        "11818": {"comment":"A = the decimal places it stands for"},
        "11821": {"comment":"D = them"},
        "11822": {"comment":"The point's place"},
        "11825": {"comment":"Less them"},
        "11829": {"comment":"A = them"},
