        "12997": {"synopsis":"Calculator constants for stk-const, in the compact form UNPACK_LITERAL reads: 0, 1, 1/2,\npi/2, 10 (stk-zero, stk-one, stk-half, stk-pi-half, stk-ten)."},
        "13015": {"synopsis":"The calculator's operations: 66 words, the routine of each code $00-$41 (the names Klive's\n48K decoder gives): $00 jump-true $01 exchange $02 delete $03 subtract $04 multiply $05\ndivision $06 to-power $07 or $08 no-&-no $09 no-l-eql $0A no-gr-eq $0B nos-neql $0C no-grtr\n$0D no-less $0E nos-eql $0F addition $10 str-&-no $11 str-l-eql $12 str-gr-eq $13 strs-neql\n$14 str-grtr $15 str-less $16 strs-eql $17 strs-add $18 val$ $19 usr-$ $1A read-in $1B\nnegate $1C code $1D val $1E len $1F sin $20 cos $21 tan $22 asn $23 acs $24 atn $25 ln $26\nexp $27 int $28 sqr $29 sgn $2A abs $2B peek $2C in $2D usr-no $2E str$ $2F chr$ $30 not $31\nduplicate $32 n-mod-m $33 jump $34 stk-data $35 dec-jr-nz $36 less-0 $37 greater-0 $38\nend-calc $39 get-argt $3A truncate $3B fp-calc-2 $3C e-to-fp $3D re-stack $3E series $3F\nstk-const $40 st-mem $41 get-mem. $3E-$41 are the groups of codes $80 and up."},
        "13147": {"synopsis":"The calculator: runs the operation codes that follow the call (RST $28) one by one, on the\ncalculator stack (STKEND) and its six memories (MEM), until end-calc:\n1. B goes to BREG (the count dec-jr-nz uses; the code for fp-calc-2). HL' points at the\n   codes.\n2. Each code: below $18 the routine gets two operands (HL the first, DE the second, 5 bytes\n   below STKEND); $18-$3F one (HL, DE = STKEND); $80 and up are groups with the index in\n   bits 0-4: series ($80), stk-const ($A0), st-mem ($C0), get-mem ($E0).\n3. The routine's address comes from CALC_OP_TABLE; it returns to CALC_LOOP, which sets\n   STKEND = DE.\nObserved: 2+3*4 printed 14, 7/2 3.5, 1/3 0.33333333, 0.1+0.2 0.3, 300*300 90000.","comment":"HL = the top number, DE = STKEND"},
        "13150": {"synopsis":"The calculator entered with BREG = B already set by the caller (CALL $335E).","comment":"B into BREG"},
        "13154": {"synopsis":"The calculator entered keeping BREG (CALL $3362)."},
        "13155": {"comment":"HL' = the codes after the call; the caller's HL' kept on the stack"},
        "13157": {"synopsis":"After each operation: STKEND = DE, the next code.","comment":"STKEND = DE: the stack's end after the last operation"},
        "13162": {"comment":"The next code"},
        "13164": {"synopsis":"Reads the next code (HL'): plain codes $00-$7F, or a group code.","comment":"The code pointer kept"},
        "13165": {"comment":"Bit 7 clear: a plain code"},
        "13169": {"comment":"D = the code"},
        "13170": {"comment":"Its group, bits 5-6"},
        "13172": {"comment":"Shifted down: 0, 2, 4 or 6"},
        "13176": {"comment":"L = $7C-$82: the index of series, stk-const, st-mem or get-mem"},
        "13179": {"comment":"A = the code's bits 0-4, the routine's parameter"},
        "13184": {"synopsis":"A plain code: below $18 HL is moved to the first of two operands (DE the second).","comment":"Codes from $18 work on one operand"},
        "13189": {"comment":"BC = -5"},
        "13192": {"comment":"DE = the second operand"},
        "13194": {"comment":"HL = the first, 5 bytes below"},
        "13196": {"synopsis":"The table index: 2 x the code.","comment":"A x 2"},
        "13198": {"synopsis":"The routine's address from CALC_OP_TABLE; CALC_LOOP pushed as its return; B = BREG.","comment":"DE = CALC_OP_TABLE"},
        "13204": {"comment":"DE = the routine"},
        "13207": {"comment":"CALC_LOOP as its return, the code pointer back into HL"},
        "13211": {"comment":"The routine, for the RET that follows"},
        "13213": {"comment":"B = BREG"},
        "13217": {"synopsis":"delete ($02): nothing to do; the loop sets STKEND = DE, the second operand's start, dropping\nit.","comment":"Into the routine pushed above (for delete itself, back to CALC_LOOP)"},
        "13218": {"synopsis":"fp-calc-2 ($3B): runs the single operation whose code is in BREG (SCAN_EXPR's operators).","comment":"CALC_LOOP's return dropped"},
        "13219": {"comment":"A = the code in BREG"},
        "13223": {"comment":"Run as if it came next"},
        "13225": {"synopsis":"Checks there is room for 5 bytes more (TEST_ROOM). Keeps DE and HL."},
        "13227": {"comment":"5 bytes"},
        "13236": {"synopsis":"Copies the 5-byte number at HL onto the calculator stack (MOVE_FP to STKEND); STKEND moves\non 5.","comment":"DE = STKEND"},
        "13243": {"comment":"STKEND moved on"},
        "13248": {"synopsis":"Copies 5 bytes from HL to DE, after checking there is room (ROOM_FOR_5). Also duplicate\n($31): the top number copied onto the stack."},
        "13251": {"comment":"The 5 bytes (BC = 5 still)"},
        "13254": {"synopsis":"stk-data ($34): the literal after the code goes onto the stack (UNPACK_LITERAL, HL' moved\npast it).","comment":"DE = STKEND, the literal's place; HL the same"},
        "13256": {"synopsis":"Unpacks a compact literal at HL' to DE: the first byte's bits 6-7 + 1 give the mantissa\nbytes that follow, bits 0-5 the exponent (or the next byte when 0), + $50; the bytes missing\nup to 5 are zero."},
        "13259": {"comment":"HL' (the code pointer) kept"},
        "13262": {"comment":"HL = the code pointer, the place kept"},
        "13263": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "13264": {"comment":"The first byte's bits 6-7"},
        "13267": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-1"},
        "13269": {"comment":"C = the mantissa bytes that follow, 1-4"},
        "13271": {"comment":"The first byte's bits 0-5"},
        "13274": {"comment":"Not 0: the exponent"},
        "13276": {"comment":"0: the exponent is the next byte"},
        "13278": {"synopsis":"The exponent + $50.","comment":"The exponent stored"},
        "13281": {"comment":"A = the zero bytes to add, + 1"},
        "13284": {"comment":"HL and DE to the mantissa"},
        "13286": {"comment":"The C mantissa bytes copied"},
        "13290": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "13291": {"comment":"HL = the place, the code pointer kept"},
        "13293": {"comment":"HL' = the code pointer, past the literal"},
        "13295": {"comment":"B = the count + 1"},
        "13296": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "13297": {"synopsis":"Zero bytes up to 5.","comment":"Up to five bytes in all"},
        "13299": {"comment":"A zero byte"},
