        "13304": {"synopsis":"One literal skipped."},
        "13307": {"comment":"DE = 0: unpacked into the ROM, so nothing is written"},
        "13310": {"comment":"HL' past one literal"},
        "13318": {"synopsis":"HL = HL + 5 x A: the address of memory A from MEM.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "13319": {"comment":"A x 4"},
        "13321": {"comment":"+ A: A x 5"},
        "13323": {"comment":"BC = 5 x A"},
        "13327": {"synopsis":"get-mem ($E0-$E5): memory A (from MEM) copied onto the stack.","comment":"DE (STKEND) kept"},
        "13328": {"comment":"HL = MEM"},
        "13331": {"comment":"HL = memory A"},
        "13334": {"comment":"Copied to STKEND"},
        "13337": {"comment":"HL = the old STKEND, the number's place"},
        "13339": {"synopsis":"stk-const ($A0-$A4): constant A of CALC_CONSTANTS onto the stack.","comment":"HL = DE: the constant's place"},
        "13341": {"comment":"HL' (the code pointer) kept"},
        "13343": {"comment":"HL' = the constants"},
        "13347": {"comment":"Past A of them"},
        "13350": {"comment":"That one unpacked to DE"},
        "13353": {"comment":"HL' back"},
        "13357": {"synopsis":"st-mem ($C0-$C5): the top number copied into memory A; it stays on the stack.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "13358": {"comment":"DE = the top number"},
        "13359": {"comment":"HL = MEM"},
        "13362": {"comment":"HL = memory A"},
        "13365": {"comment":"HL = the number, DE = the memory"},
        "13366": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13369": {"comment":"DE = STKEND again"},
        "13370": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "13372": {"synopsis":"exchange ($01): the top two numbers swap places.","comment":"5 bytes"},
        "13374": {"synopsis":"One byte of each swapped, 5 times.","comment":"A = the second's byte, C = the first's"},
        "13376": {"comment":"Swapped in place"},
        "13381": {"comment":"All five"},
        "13383": {"comment":"HL and DE back as they were"},
        "13385": {"synopsis":"series ($80+): sums a series of the number z on the calculator stack, with the coefficients\nas stk-data literals after the code (B of them, the code's low bits); the Clenshaw\nrecurrence for a Chebyshev series:\n1. Memory 0 = 2z; memory 2 = 0; 0 stacked as the running term.\n2. For each coefficient c: new term = 2z x term - memory 2 + c, memory 1 = the old memory 2,\n   memory 2 = the old term (dec-jr-nz).\n3. The result is the last term minus memory 1 (the term two steps back).\nChanges: memories 0-2.","comment":"B = the count of coefficients"},
        "13386": {"comment":"The calculator, BREG = B"},
        "13402": {"comment":"The next coefficient, from the caller's codes (stk-data)"},
        "13405": {"comment":"The calculator again, BREG kept for dec-jr-nz"},
        "13418": {"synopsis":"abs ($2A): the sign cleared (SIGN_BIT_SET with B = $FF).\nObserved: ABS -3 printed 3.","comment":"B = $FF: the sign cleared"},
        "13422": {"synopsis":"negate ($1B): the sign flipped; 0 stays 0 (IS_ZERO)."},
        "13425": {"comment":"0: stays 0"},
        "13426": {"comment":"B = 0: the sign flipped"},
        "13428": {"synopsis":"Sets the sign from B (abs) or flips it (negate); a small integer goes through\nSIGN_SMALL_INT.","comment":"Exponent 0: a small integer"},
        "13433": {"comment":"Bit 7 of B: set for abs"},
        "13436": {"comment":"ORed into the first mantissa byte"},
        "13437": {"comment":"Bit 7 flipped through the carry"},
        "13440": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "13443": {"synopsis":"A small integer: its value negated or made positive and stored back (SMALL_INT_GET,\nSMALL_INT_PUT)."},
        "13445": {"comment":"C = the sign, DE = the value"},
        "13449": {"comment":"B ($FF for abs) OR the sign, complemented: abs gives 0, negate the other sign"},
        "13453": {"comment":"Stored with the new sign"},
        "13458": {"synopsis":"sgn ($29): 1, -1, or 0 for 0.\nObserved: SGN -5 -1, SGN 0 0."},
        "13461": {"comment":"0: stays 0"},
        "13463": {"comment":"DE = 1"},
        "13467": {"comment":"The sign bit into the carry"},
        "13470": {"comment":"C = $FF for a negative number"},
        "13472": {"comment":"1 with that sign: 1 or -1"},
        "13477": {"synopsis":"in ($2C): the byte read from port n (TAKE_WORD), stacked.","comment":"BC = the port"},
        "13480": {"comment":"A = the byte read"},
        "13484": {"synopsis":"peek ($2B): the byte at address n (TAKE_WORD), stacked.","comment":"BC = the address"},
        "13487": {"comment":"A = the byte there"},
        "13488": {"synopsis":"STACK_A."},
        "13491": {"synopsis":"usr-no ($2D): calls the machine code at address n (TAKE_WORD); the BC it returns is stacked\n(STACK_BC is its return address)."},
        "13494": {"comment":"STACK_BC as the return address"},
        "13498": {"comment":"The routine's address"},
        "13499": {"comment":"Called"},
        "13500": {"synopsis":"usr-$ ($19): the address of a UDG: the one-character string must be a letter A-U (or a UDG\ncharacter $90-$A4); UDG + 8 x its index is stacked. Anything else is report A.","comment":"DE = the string, BC = its length"},
        "13503": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "13506": {"comment":"No: report A"},
        "13508": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "13509": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "13512": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "13514": {"comment":"A UDG character, $90-$A4?"},
        "13516": {"comment":"Below $90: report A"},
        "13518": {"comment":"Above $A4: report A"},
        "13522": {"comment":"For the DEC that follows"},
        "13523": {"synopsis":"The index x 8, past the 21 UDGs is report A.","comment":"A = the UDG's number; a letter's low five bits"},
        "13524": {"comment":"Times 8; a letter's top bits fall off"},
        "13527": {"comment":"Past the 21st: report A"},
        "13531": {"comment":"BC = UDG"},
        "13535": {"comment":"+ the offset"},
        "13540": {"synopsis":"UDG + offset, stacked (STACK_BC)."},
        "13543": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 9 (report A, \"Invalid argument\")."},
        "13545": {"synopsis":"Carry when the number at HL is 0: its first four bytes all zero. Keeps every register but F."},
        "13547": {"comment":"A kept in B"},
        "13548": {"comment":"The first four bytes ORed"},
        "13555": {"comment":"A back"},
        "13558": {"comment":"Not 0: no carry"},
        "13559": {"comment":"0: carry"},
        "13561": {"synopsis":"greater-0 ($37): 1 when the number is above 0, else 0."},
        "13564": {"comment":"0 is not above 0, and stays 0"},
        "13565": {"comment":"A = $FF: the sign flipped"},
        "13569": {"synopsis":"not ($30): 1 for 0, 0 for anything else.\nObserved: NOT 0 1, NOT 7 0."},
        "13572": {"comment":"Carry (0) stored as 1"},
        "13574": {"synopsis":"less-0 ($36): 1 when the number is below 0, else 0.","comment":"A = 0: the sign as it is"},
        "13575": {"synopsis":"The sign bit, flipped by A, into carry."},
        "13576": {"comment":"The sign byte, flipped for greater-0"},
        "13578": {"comment":"Its bit 7 into the carry"},
        "13579": {"synopsis":"Stores carry as the small integer 1 or 0 at HL."},
        "13580": {"comment":"A = 0, the carry kept"},
        "13582": {"comment":"The exponent and sign bytes 0"},
        "13586": {"comment":"The carry into bit 0: the value 0 or 1"},
        "13588": {"comment":"A = 0 again"},
        "13590": {"comment":"The high byte and the fifth 0"},
        "13595": {"synopsis":"or ($07): x OR y is x when y is 0, else 1.","comment":"Is y (at DE) 0?"},
        "13600": {"comment":"Yes: x stays"},
        "13601": {"comment":"No: 1"},
        "13604": {"synopsis":"no-&-no ($08): x AND y is x when y is not 0, else 0."},
        "13609": {"comment":"y not 0: x stays"},
        "13610": {"comment":"y is 0: the result is 0"},
        "13613": {"synopsis":"str-&-no ($10): a$ AND y is a$ when y is not 0, else an empty string (its length made 0).","comment":"Is y (at DE) 0?"},
        "13618": {"comment":"No: a$ stays"},
        "13620": {"comment":"DE back to a$'s entry: its length in the last two bytes"},
        "13621": {"comment":"The length 0"},
        "13627": {"synopsis":"The comparisons, numbers ($09-$0E: <=, >=, <>, >, <, =) and strings ($11-$16, the same\norder): the operands exchanged where needed so that each test is \"greater than\" or \"equal\";\nnumbers are subtracted (CALC_SUBTRACT), strings compared character by character (a string\nthat is the start of a longer one is the smaller); the result 1 for true, 0 for false.\nObserved: 2<=2 1, 3>=4 0, 2<>2 0, \"ab\"<\"abc\" 1, \"a\"<\"b\" 1.","comment":"A = the code"},
        "13628": {"comment":"Less 8: 1-6 for numbers, 9-14 for strings"},
        "13630": {"comment":"Bit 2: >, < and ="},
        "13634": {"comment":"<=, >= and <> one less"},
        "13635": {"synopsis":"Whether to exchange the operands (bit 0 after the shift).","comment":"Bit 0 into the carry: >= and < exchange the operands"},
        "13638": {"comment":"The operands exchanged"},
        "13643": {"comment":"HL and DE as before"},
        "13646": {"synopsis":"Numbers: subtract; strings: CMP_STRINGS.","comment":"Strings?"},
        "13650": {"comment":"The next bit kept with the flags"},
        "13652": {"comment":"Numbers: the first less the second"},
        "13657": {"synopsis":"Two strings (STK_FETCH twice): compared byte by byte.","comment":"The next bit kept with the flags"},
        "13659": {"comment":"The second string, X: DE, BC"},
        "13662": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13664": {"comment":"The first string, Y: DE = its address, BC = its length"},
        "13667": {"comment":"HL = X's length"},
        "13668": {"synopsis":"The next pair of characters, or an end.","comment":"Has X ended?"},
        "13670": {"comment":"HL = X's address, X's length on the stack"},
        "13672": {"comment":"X has not"},
        "13674": {"comment":"X has: has Y too?"},
        "13675": {"synopsis":"The first string ended.","comment":"X's length dropped"},
        "13676": {"comment":"Both ended: equal"},
        "13678": {"comment":"Y is the longer: the flags inverted"},
        "13682": {"synopsis":"Both ended together."},
        "13685": {"synopsis":"The second ended: the first is greater.","comment":"Has Y ended?"},
        "13686": {"comment":"Yes: Y is the shorter"},
        "13688": {"comment":"Y's character less X's"},
        "13690": {"comment":"Y's is lower"},
        "13692": {"comment":"Y's is higher"},
        "13694": {"comment":"The same: on to the next pair"},
        "13697": {"comment":"HL = X's length"},
        "13698": {"comment":"One less"},
        "13701": {"synopsis":"A character differs, or the second ended first.","comment":"X's length dropped"},
        "13703": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "13704": {"synopsis":"A zero on the stack for the result.","comment":"The test's flags kept"},
        "13708": {"synopsis":"Turns the subtraction's or the strings' outcome into 1 or 0 (NOT, GREATER_0)."},
        "13710": {"comment":"Carry: NOT"},
        "13715": {"comment":"No carry: greater-0"},
        "13719": {"comment":"The next bit into the carry"},
        "13720": {"comment":"Clear: NOT again, the inverted tests (<=, >= and <>)"},
        "13724": {"synopsis":"strs-add ($17): the two strings joined in the workspace (WORK_ROOM), stacked.","comment":"The second string: DE, BC"},
        "13729": {"comment":"The first string"},
        "13732": {"comment":"HL = the second's length"},
        "13733": {"comment":"Kept again, with the first's address and length"},
        "13736": {"comment":"BC = the total length"},
        "13739": {"comment":"Room in the workspace (DE = its start)"},
        "13740": {"comment":"The joined string stacked"},
        "13743": {"comment":"BC and HL = the first's length and address"},
        "13747": {"comment":"Empty: nothing to copy"},
        "13749": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13751": {"synopsis":"The second string copied after the first.","comment":"BC and HL = the second's"},
        "13755": {"comment":"Empty: nothing to copy"},
        "13757": {"comment":"Copied after it"},
        "13759": {"synopsis":"HL = STKEND - 5 (the top number), DE = STKEND.\nChanges: DE, HL."},
        "13762": {"comment":"DE = -5"},
        "13769": {"synopsis":"chr$ ($2F): a one-character string of code n (0-255, else report B).","comment":"A = n"},
        "13772": {"comment":"Over 255: report B"},
        "13774": {"comment":"Negative: report B"},
        "13777": {"comment":"Room for one character"},
        "13782": {"comment":"The character"},
        "13783": {"comment":"Stacked as a string"},
        "13788": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B)."},
        "13790": {"synopsis":"val ($1D) and val$ ($18): the string is copied into the workspace with an ENTER after it,\nchecked as an expression of the result's type (a number for val, a string for val$; report C\notherwise), then evaluated (SCAN_EXPR) with CH_ADD there, and CH_ADD put back.\nObserved: VAL \"2*3\" 6, VAL$ \"\"\"a\"\"+\"\"b\"\"\" ab; VAL of a string expression report C.","comment":"CH_ADD kept"},
        "13794": {"comment":"A = the code: $1D val, $18 val$"},
        "13795": {"comment":"A carry for val only"},
        "13797": {"comment":"A = $FF for val, 0 for val$"},
        "13798": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13799": {"comment":"DE = the string, BC = its length"},
        "13802": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13803": {"comment":"One more, for an ENTER"},
        "13804": {"comment":"Room in the workspace (DE = its start)"},
        "13805": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "13806": {"comment":"CH_ADD = the copy"},
        "13810": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13811": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13814": {"comment":"HL at the extra byte"},
        "13815": {"comment":"An ENTER after it"},
        "13817": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 clear: checking"},
        "13821": {"comment":"The expression checked"},
        "13824": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "13825": {"comment":"Must be the ENTER"},
        "13827": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "13829": {"comment":"HL = the copy"},
        "13830": {"comment":"A = $FF for val, 0 for val$"},
        "13831": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6 (a number) against it"},
        "13834": {"comment":"Not 0: the wrong type"},
        "13836": {"synopsis":"Report C, or CH_ADD into the copy for the run."},
        "13839": {"comment":"CH_ADD = the copy again"},
        "13842": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 set: running"},
        "13846": {"comment":"The expression evaluated"},
        "13849": {"comment":"CH_ADD back"},
        "13853": {"comment":"HL and DE to the stack's top"},
        "13855": {"synopsis":"str$ ($2E): the number printed by PRINT_FP through channel R (stream -1) into the workspace\n(from K_CUR), then stacked as a string; the channel is put back.\nObserved: STR$ (1/3) 0.33333333; LEN STR$ 100 3.","comment":"One byte"},
        "13858": {"comment":"Room in the workspace"},
        "13859": {"comment":"K_CUR = its start: channel R writes there"},
        "13862": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13863": {"comment":"CURCHL kept"},
        "13867": {"comment":"Stream -1: channel R"},
        "13872": {"comment":"The number printed into the workspace"},
        "13875": {"comment":"HL = the old channel"},
        "13876": {"comment":"Made current again"},
        "13879": {"comment":"DE = the text's start"},
        "13880": {"comment":"HL = its end"},
        "13884": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "13888": {"comment":"Stacked as a string"},
        "13893": {"synopsis":"read-in ($1A, INKEY$ #s): one call of the stream's input routine (CHAN_INPUT): one\ncharacter, or an empty string when there is none; the channel is put back. A stream of 16 or\nmore is report B.","comment":"A = the stream"},
        "13896": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "13898": {"comment":"Then report B"},
        "13901": {"comment":"CURCHL kept"},
        "13905": {"comment":"The stream made current"},
        "13908": {"comment":"Its input routine once: carry and A when there is a character"},
        "13911": {"comment":"BC = 0: an empty string"},
        "13914": {"comment":"None"},
        "13916": {"comment":"BC = 1"},
        "13917": {"comment":"Room for it"},
        "13918": {"comment":"The character"},
        "13919": {"synopsis":"Stacks the string (STK_STO_STR)."},
        "13922": {"comment":"HL = the old channel"},
        "13923": {"comment":"Made current again"},
        "13926": {"comment":"HL and DE to the stack's top"},
        "13929": {"synopsis":"code ($1C): the first character's code, 0 for an empty string.\nObserved: CODE \"\" 0."},
        "13932": {"comment":"An empty string?"},
        "13934": {"comment":"Yes: A = 0"},
        "13936": {"comment":"A = the first character"},
        "13937": {"synopsis":"STACK_A."},
        "13940": {"synopsis":"len ($1E): the string's length stacked (STK_FETCH, STACK_BC)."},
        "13946": {"synopsis":"dec-jr-nz ($35): BREG - 1; not 0: a jump by the next byte (CALC_JUMP_REL); 0: past it.","comment":"The code pointer's register set"},
        "13947": {"comment":"HL' kept"},
        "13948": {"comment":"HL = BREG"},
        "13951": {"comment":"Counted down"},
        "13952": {"comment":"HL' back"},
        "13953": {"comment":"Not 0: the jump"},
        "13955": {"comment":"0: past the displacement"},
        "13958": {"synopsis":"jump ($33): the code pointer moves by the signed byte after the code."},
        "13959": {"synopsis":"HL' + the signed byte.","comment":"E = the displacement"},
        "13961": {"comment":"D = its sign"},
        "13964": {"comment":"HL' moved by it"},
        "13967": {"synopsis":"jump-true ($00): the jump when the top number (a 0 or 1 result) is not 0; it stays on the\nstack.","comment":"DE to the top number's value byte"},
        "13970": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "13972": {"comment":"Not 0: the jump"},
        "13976": {"comment":"0: past the displacement"},
        "13979": {"synopsis":"end-calc ($38): the calculator ends; the Z80 goes on after this byte.","comment":"CALC_LOOP's return dropped"},
        "13981": {"comment":"HL' = the caller's again, the code pointer the return address"},
        "13983": {"comment":"Back to the Z80 code after end-calc"},
        "13984": {"synopsis":"n-mod-m ($32): from n and m, n - m x INT (n/m) and INT (n/m) on the stack (memory 0 used).","comment":"The codes of n-mod-m follow"},
        "13999": {"synopsis":"int ($27): truncate; for a negative number with a fraction, one less (CALC_INT_NEG).\nObserved: INT 2.5 2, INT -2.5 -3, INT -3 -3.","comment":"The codes of int follow"},
        "14007": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $36B2 lands on (the listing cannot decode them after RST\n$28): duplicate, truncate, st-mem-0, subtract, get-mem-0, exchange, not, jump-true (+3),\nstk-one, subtract, end-calc. The Z80 goes on at CALC_INT_END."},
        "14019": {"synopsis":"Returns."},
        "14020": {"synopsis":"exp ($26): e ^ x as 2 ^ (x / ln 2):\n1. y = x x 1.442695 (1/ln 2); n = INT y in memory 3, f = y - n (0 to 1).\n2. 2 ^ f from series-08 of 2f - 1 (CALC_SERIES).\n3. n added to the result's exponent byte: over 255 is report 6; a negative n taking it to 0\n   or below gives 0.\nObserved: EXP 1 2.7182818, EXP -1 0.36787944; EXP 100 report 6; EXP -100 0."},
        "14073": {"comment":"A = |n|; NZ for a negative n, carry over 255"},
        "14076": {"comment":"Negative"},
        "14078": {"comment":"Over 255: report 6"},
        "14080": {"comment":"n added to the exponent of 2 ^ f"},
        "14081": {"comment":"No carry: in range"},
        "14083": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 5 (report 6, \"Number too big\")."},
        "14085": {"synopsis":"n negative: under -255, or not less than the exponent, is 0; otherwise the exponent less\n|n|.","comment":"Below -255: 0"},
        "14087": {"comment":"|n| less the exponent"},
        "14088": {"comment":"Not below it: 0"},
        "14090": {"comment":"A = the exponent less |n|"},
        "14092": {"synopsis":"The new exponent stored.","comment":"The result's new exponent"},
        "14094": {"synopsis":"Underflow: the result is 0."},
        "14099": {"synopsis":"ln ($25): the natural logarithm; x of 0 or less stops with error code 9 (report A, \"Invalid\nargument\"):\n1. x split into its binary exponent e (exponent byte - 128) and mantissa m (exponent byte\n   $80, 0.5 to 1); m of 0.8 or less is doubled and e lessened by 1 (m then 0.8 to 1.6).\n2. ln x = e x ln 2 (0.693147) + (m - 1) x series-0C of 2.5 (m - 1) - 0.5 (CALC_SERIES).\nObserved: LN 1 0, LN 10 2.3025851; LN 0 report A."},
        "14108": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $3717 lands on for x above 0 (the listing cannot decode\nthem after RST $28): stk-zero, delete, end-calc. The Z80 goes on at LN_SPLIT."},
        "14111": {"synopsis":"The exponent byte taken (A) and replaced by $80 (m from 0.5 to 1); e = A - 128 stacked\n(STACK_A), then the calculator compares m with 0.8.","comment":"A = the exponent byte"},
        "14112": {"comment":"m: the mantissa from 0.5 to 1"},
        "14114": {"comment":"The exponent byte stacked"},
        "14117": {"comment":"The mantissa m against 0.8, and the rest of ln"},
        "14139": {"comment":"Doubles m (its exponent + 1)"},
        "14140": {"comment":"On: e x ln 2 plus the series"},
        "14211": {"synopsis":"get-argt ($39): reduces an angle x (radians) to z from -1 to 1 so that SIN x = SIN (z x\nPI/2), for sin and cos:\n1. y = x x 0.159155 (1/(2 PI)) less INT (that + 0.5): -0.5 to 0.5 turns; z = 4y (-2 to 2).\n2. |z| above 1 (memory 0 = 1, else 0): reflected to 2 - z, or -2 - z for a negative z\n   (ARGT_REFLECT).\nChanges: memory 0, read by cos."},
        "14241": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $379C lands on for |z| above 1 (the listing cannot decode\nthem after RST $28): stk-one, subtract, exchange, less-0, jump-true to the end-calc, negate,\nend-calc: |z| - 2, negated for a positive z. The Z80 goes on at $37A9."},
        "14249": {"comment":"Returns"},
        "14250": {"synopsis":"cos ($20): COS x = SIN (PI/2 - x): get-argt's z made 1 - |z| (|z| - 1 negated, or kept when\nmemory 0 says z was reflected), then sin's series.\nObserved: COS 0 1, COS PI -1, COS 1 0.54030231."},
        "14261": {"synopsis":"sin ($1F): get-argt's z, then z x series-06 of 2z^2 - 1 (CALC_SERIES).\nObserved: SIN 0 0, SIN (PI/2) 1, SIN PI 0, SIN 1 0.84147098, SIN 1000 0.82687939."},
        "14298": {"synopsis":"tan ($21): SIN x / COS x (division: report 6 when COS x is 0).\nObserved: TAN 1 1.5574077."},
        "14306": {"synopsis":"atn ($24): the arctangent:\n1. |x| below 1 (an exponent byte below $81): w = x with c = 0 (ATN_SMALL).\n2. Otherwise w = -1/x with c = PI/2, or -PI/2 for a negative x.\n3. ATN x = c + w x series-0C of 2w^2 - 1 (CALC_SERIES).\nObserved: ATN 1 0.78539816, ATN -2 -1.1071487.","comment":"The full form"},
        "14309": {"comment":"A = the exponent byte"},
        "14310": {"comment":"|x| below 1?"},
        "14312": {"comment":"Yes: c = 0"},
        "14314": {"comment":"No: w = -1/x, c = PI/2 with x's sign"},
        "14328": {"synopsis":"|x| below 1: c = 0."},
        "14387": {"synopsis":"asn ($22): ASN x = 2 x ATN (x / (1 + SQR (1 - x^2))); |x| above 1 makes sqr's ln stop with\nreport A.\nObserved: ASN .5 0.52359878; ASN 2 report A."},
        "14403": {"synopsis":"acs ($23): ACS x = PI/2 - ASN x.\nObserved: ACS .5 1.0471976."},
        "14410": {"synopsis":"sqr ($28): 0 gives 0 (the jump-true to $386C's end-calc); otherwise x ^ 0.5 by falling into\nto-power.\nObserved: SQR 2 1.4142136, SQR 0 0; SQR -1 report A."},
        "14417": {"synopsis":"to-power ($06): x ^ y with x below y on the stack:\n1. x not 0: EXP (y x LN x) (CALC_EXP), so a negative x stops in ln with report A.\n2. x = 0 (POWER_ZERO_BASE): y = 0 gives 1, y above 0 gives 0, y below 0 is 1/0, report 6.\nObserved: 2^10 1024, 2^.5 1.4142136, 0^0 1, 0^3 0; 0^-1 report 6, (-2)^2 report A."},
        "14426": {"comment":"EXP (y x LN x)"},
        "14429": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $3855 lands on for x = 0 (the listing cannot decode them\nafter RST $28): delete, duplicate, not, jump-true (y = 0) to the delete at $386A, stk-zero,\nexchange, greater-0, jump-true (y above 0) to the end-calc at $386C, stk-one, exchange,\ndivision (1/0), delete, stk-one, end-calc. sqr's jump-true at $384D also lands on the\nend-calc at $386C. The Z80 goes on at $386D."},
        "14445": {"comment":"Returns"},
        "14446": {"synopsis":"Unused: 1170 bytes of $FF from the end of the code to the character set, listed as one\n.fillb row. No code jumps here."},
        "15616": {"synopsis":"Character set: the pictures of the 96 character codes $20-$7F, 8 bytes each, 768 bytes up to\nthe ROM's end. A byte is one pixel row, top row first, bit 7 the leftmost pixel; code c's\npicture is at CHARACTER_SET + (c - $20) x 8, which is CHARS + c x 8 with CHARS = $3C00\n(SET_RAMTOP). Three readers:\n- printing: OUT_CHAR draws code c from CHARS + c x 8, on the screen or into the printer\n  buffer, so pointing CHARS elsewhere replaces the set;\n- SCREEN$: SCREENS_VALUE compares a screen cell with the 96 pictures from CHARS + $100,\n  plain and inverted;\n- start-up: RAM_TOP_FOUND (at $1203) copies the pictures of A to U ($3E08-$3EAF) as the 21\n  UDGs.\nCodes $80-$8F (block graphics), $90-$A4 (UDGs) and $A5 up (keywords) have no pictures here.\n$20 - Character: ' '"},
        "15624": {"synopsis":"$21 - Character: '!'"},
        "15632": {"synopsis":"$22 - Character: '\"'"},
        "15640": {"synopsis":"$23 - Character: '#'"},
        "15648": {"synopsis":"$24 - Character: '$'"},
        "15656": {"synopsis":"$25 - Character: '%'"},
        "15664": {"synopsis":"$26 - Character: '&'"},
        "15672": {"synopsis":"$27 - Character: apostrophe"},
        "15680": {"synopsis":"$28 - Character: '('"},
        "15688": {"synopsis":"$29 - Character: ')'"},
